/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mk-codex-2.md` |\n787:| D443 | 2026-11-13 | Shape B' (council consensus, D439): the stored clean chain against fresh production v118 draws as an exploratory census of final-answer losses; one-day slice first; one $5 shared ledger (conditional on stated bounds); shape A stays owed for D427 | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md` |\n788:| D444 | 2026-11-13 | D443's draws stopped at the $5 ledger (an over-conservative Jev charge, $4.999 ledger against $0.98 recorded); three fresh draws from empty under a new $3 ledger with Jev settled at three times its usage (council consensus, D439); stopped draws kept as records | in force | `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ml-codex-9.md` |\n789:| D445 | 2026-11-13 | Census: level on graded questions, every loss at opening; next a $0 path trace of the clean path's 17 graded opening losses, memory first, no repair until a cause is found (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/RESULT.md` |\n790:| D446 | 2026-11-13 | Trace: no single mechanism; 7 certain and 2 uncertain breaches of the standard's unit rules; next a $0 audit of a narrow typed-unit contract on stored losses and correct controls, with a stop rule (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/AUDIT-CONTRACT.md` |\n791:| D447 | 2026-11-13 | Typed-unit line stopped (audit: 2 of 16 detectable, none recovered); next a reviewed $0 design for the ladder step wired end to end and a diagnostic same-day run; the send decided after its review (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/AUDIT-RESULT.md` |\n792:| D448 | 2026-11-13 | Wiring contract settled (design v4); build the wiring and its $0 proof, then code review; the slice and the full run each by its own later decision (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md` |\n793:| D449 | 2026-11-13 | Wiring code review: