e for FY2027?\" | True | v3 0.99 \"What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\"; v4 0.84 \"What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2028?\"; v14 0.83 \"What will NVIDIA report as total CPU revenue for FY2027?\" |\n   108\t| 821 | v33 \"At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity inve\" | True | v29 0.99 \"Will NVIDIA complete its $5 billion investment in Safe Superintelligen\"; v27 0.96 \"Will NVIDIA complete an investment of $5 billion in Safe Superintellig\"; v20 0.68 \"Will NVIDIA complete its planned $1 billion investment in NAVER Corp. \" |\n   109\t| 893 | v34 \"Will NVIDIA complete its planned $1.5 billion investment in \" | True | v33 0.91 \"At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity investment com\" |\n   110\t| 932 | v35 \"What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\" | False | v3 1.00 \"What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\"; v4 0.84 \"What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2028?\" |\n   111\t| 1409 | v43 \"Will NVIDIA agree to invest approximately $2.5 billion in Th\" | True | v33 0.88 \"At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity investment com\" |\n   112\t| 1410 | v44 \"What year-over-year growth rate will NVIDIA report for total\" | False | v35 0.68 \"What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\"; v41 0.55 \"What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?\" |\n   113\t| 1664 | v47 \"Will NVIDIA agree to anchor Anthropic’s IPO with an investme\" | True | v33 0.78 \"At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity investment com\" |\n   114\t| 1668 | v48 \"Will NVIDIA agree to invest US$10 billion in Anthropic’s pla\" | True | v33 0.87 \"At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity investment com\" |\n   115\t\n   116\t### Number questions by typed key (measure, scope, period, unit): 18\n   117\t\n   118\t| question | measure | scope | period | unit | text |\n   119\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   120\t| v49 | market_size | Global semiconductor sales | 2026-01-01..2026-12-31 | USD | How much will global semiconductor sales total in calendar 2026? |\n   121\t| v6 | spend_total | Data-center capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers | 2026-01-01..2026-12-31 | USD | How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures i |\n   122\t| v1 | financing_amount | AI-cloud credit support | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | At NVIDIA's next annual filing, what amount of credit-support obligations under its AI-clo |\n   123\t| v15 | financing_amount | Supply purchase commitments | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of supply purchase commitments will NVIDIA r |\n   124\t| v19 | financing_amount | Financing to Amkor through the announced prepayment | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | At NVIDIA's FY2027 annual filing, what amount of financing to Amkor through the announced  |\n   125\t| v33 | financing_amount | Equity investment commitments | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity investment commitments will NVIDIA |\n   126\t| v42 | financing_amount | Financing to MediaTek through convertible bonds | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of financing to MediaTek through the agreed  |\n   127\t| v31 | gross_margin |  | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | percent | What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027? |\n   128\t| v14 | product_revenue | Vera CPU | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | What will NVIDIA report as total CPU revenue for FY2027? |\n   129\t| v30 | product_revenue | Vera CPU | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2027? |\n   130\t| v35 | segment_revenue | Data Center | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027? |\n   131\t| v3 | total_revenue |  | 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 | USD | What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027? |\n   132\t| v7 | spend_total | Data-center capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers | 2027-01-01..2027-12-31 | USD | How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures i |\n   133\t| v37 | gross_margin |  | 2027-02-01..2028-01-31 | percent | What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2028? |\n   134\t| v38 | gross_margin |  | 2027-02-01..2028-01-31 | percent | What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2028? |\n   135\t| v44 | growth_rate | NVIDIA total revenue | 2027-02-01..2028-01-31 | percent | What year-over-year growth rate will NVIDIA report for total revenue in FY2028? |\n   136\t| v41 | product_revenue | Vera CPU | 2027-02-01..2028-01-31 | USD | What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028? |\n   137\t| v4 | total_revenue |  | 2027-02-01..2028-01-31 | USD | What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2028? |\n   138\t\n     1\t\"\"\"$0 census for the dependency design review (D692): in the three finished poc-v118 draws (release comparison old-1..3), which\n     2\tquestions could be linked, and what the product already records about their relation.\n     3\t\n     4\tTwo sources are listed side by side, for every question the matcher opened as new:\n     5\t  1. the matcher's own relation answers stored in the match record's reason (\"v9: part_of 0.99\"); the criterion is \"one asks about a\n     6\t     strict component or subset of the other, in either direction\" (`jev_matching.RELATIONS`), so it carries no direction;\n     7\t  2. the typed keys code already stores per question (`view_keys`: measure, scope, period), listed for every number question of the\n     8\t     same company, so a reader can see which pairs share a period and how their measures relate.\n     9\t\n    10\t  python3 selection_census.py > selection-census.md\n    11\t\n    12\tThe stores are opened read-only. Nothing is judged here: the lists are for the council to read.\n    13\t\"\"\"\n    14\timport json\n    15\timport re\n    16\timport sqlite3\n    17\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    18\t\n    19\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n    20\tRUNS = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    21\tTHRESHOLD = 0.5                                        # jev_matching.THRESHOLD\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\tdef census(draw):\n    25\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUNS / draw}/prod/views.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    26\t    questions = dict(conn.execute('select view_id, question from views'))\n    27\t    opened_at = {}\n    28\t    for view_id, seq in conn.execute('select view_id, created_seq from views'):\n    29\t        opened_at.setdefault(seq, []).append(view_id)\n    30\t    keys = {row[0]: row for row in conn.execute('select view_id, measure, scope, period_start, period_end, unit from view_keys')}\n    31\t    relations = []\n    32\t    for seq, decisions in conn.execute('select seq, decisions_json from match_records order by seq, id'):\n    33\t        data = json.loads(decisions or '{}')\n    34\t        for candidate in (data.get('candidates', []) if isinstance(data, dict) else []):\n    35\t            if candidate.get('outcome') != 'new':\n    36\t                continue\n    37\t            best = {}\n    38\t            for other, probability in re.findall(r'(v\\d+): part_of ([0-9.]+)', candidate.get('reason', '')):\n    39\t                if float(probability) >= THRESHOLD:\n    40\t                    best[other] = max(best.get(other, 0.0), float(probability))\n    41\t            if best:\n    42\t                relations.append({'seq': seq, 'opened': opened_at.get(seq, []), 'collision_judge_asked': 'collision judge' in candidate.get('reason', ''),\n    43\t                                  'part_of': sorted(best.items(), key=lambda pair: -pair[1])})\n    44\t    numbers = sorted((k for k in keys.values() if k[5] in ('USD', 'percent')), key=lambda k: (k[3] or '', k[1] or '', k[0]))\n    45\t    return questions, keys, relations, numbers\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\tdef main():\n    49\t    print('# Selection census for the dependency design review (D692), $0\\n')\n    50\t    print('Generated by `selection_census.py` from the three finished poc-v118 draws (`poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{1,2,3}`).')\n    51\t    print('None of the three stores holds a dependency row (the Jev matcher returns `dependencies: []`, `jev_matching.py`).\\n')\n    52\t    for draw in ('old-1', 'old-2', 'old-3'):\n    53\t        questions, keys, relations, numbers = census(draw)\n    54\t        print(f'## {draw}\\n')\n    55\t        print(f'### The matcher\\'s \"part_of\" answers (>= {THRESHOLD}) on questions it opened as new: {len(relations)} openings\\n')\n    56\t        print('| seq | opened | collision judge asked | part_of (other question, probability) |')\n    57\t        print('|---|---|---|---|')\n    58\t        for row in relations:\n    59\t            listed = '; '.join(f'{other} {probability:.2f} \"{questions.get(other, \"?\")[:70]}\"' for other, probability in row['part_of'])\n    60\t            opened = ', '.join(f'{v} \"{questions.get(v, \"?\")[:60]}\"' for v in row['opened'])\n    61\t            print(f'| {row[\"seq\"]} | {opened} | {row[\"collision_judge_asked\"]} | {listed} |')\n    62\t        print(f'\\n### Number questions by typed key (measure, scope, period, unit): {len(numbers)}\\n')\n    63\t        print('| question | measure | scope | period | unit | text |')\n    64\t        print('|---|---|---|---|---|---|')\n    65\t        for view_id, measure, scope, start, end, unit in numbers:\n    66\t            print(f'| {view_id} | {measure} | {scope} | {start}..{end} | {unit} | {questions.get(view_id, \"?\")[:90]} |')\n    67\t        print()\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    71\t    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '165,300p'\ntail -n 7 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\nrg -n 'D(51|265|354|368|427|439|53[3-9]|54[0-2]|690|691|692)\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS.md\nrg -n '\"'^## D(51|265|354|368|427|439|53[3-9]|54[0-3]|690|691|692)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\nrg -n 'D69[0-2]|next|dependency' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | head -32\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '165,300p'\ntail -n 7 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\nrg -n 'D(51|265|354|368|427|439|53[3-9]|54[0-2]|690|691|692)\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS.md\nrg -n '\"'^## D(51|265|354|368|427|439|53[3-9]|54[0-3]|690|691|692)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\nrg -n 'D69[0-2]|next|dependency' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | head -32\"","aggregated_output":"   165\t  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n   166\t  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n   167\t\n   168\t## 7. Process (no drift)\n   169\t\n   170\t- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n   171\t  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n   172\t  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n   173\t- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n   174\t- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n   175\t  sentence, in both directions.\n   176\t- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n   177\t- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n   178\t\n   179\t## 8. Steps and where we are\n   180\t\n   181\t| # | Step | Output | Status |\n   182\t|---|---|---|---|\n   183\t| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n   184\t| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n   185\t| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n   186\t| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n   187\t| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n   188\t| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n   189\t| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n   190\t| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n   191\t| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n   192\t\n   193\t## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n   194\t\n   195\t- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n   196\t- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n   197\t- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n   198\t- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n   199\t- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n   200\t- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n   201\t- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n| 35 | 11-05 | 独立读者挑战\"现在做进生产、跑 14 天三遍\"的建议 | 核实属实的：资本开支那一行在新句子下 12 次读漏 3 次（旧句子 9/9，模型两次都怪\"更大的行\"半句）；句子照 5 月财报改、又只在 5 月财报上量，没有留出的财报；做进生产前的记录写法（同一个数挂几道题、指引不该写成\"事实\"、第二个提示词）要 Alex 定；分类和判断同时跑、说明里还引着旧句子，照实记下 | 建议撤回；下一步：修掉资本开支漏读（改成\"写完逐条复核\"），在 5 月和留出的 8 月两份财报上各测一遍，约 0.5 美元 |\n| 36 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好开始做到production 上，完整的更新所有系统设计等\"；同一个数挂几道题，他选\"存一条，挂到每道读到它的题\"（D364）。做进生产前先修资本开支漏读：第四版把\"是不是这道题的量\"挪到最后逐条复核（并删掉别的期间），文件规则补\"有申报的只读申报的\"；Codex 审 3 轮（共 6 条严重，都改）；试发 7 道题过；然后 5 月登记读法、8 月留出读法 | **没过**：5 月\"不能删掉该留的\"——v22 只留住 1/3、资本开支 3/6 读；8 月资本开支二季度 0/3（选了上半年、引用跳格被拒）。机理：复核里\"别的期间删掉\"让全年题删掉最近一季；\"最近一期\"在本季和年初至今两栏间没说清。好消息：8 月 v9 找到了新披露的担保 1,085 亿和承诺 560 亿 | 停，交 Alex：第三版是唯一过了 5 月三条的版本 |\n| 37 | 11-05 | Alex：\"为什么没过？…你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\"；\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\"。普查全部 7 次读法、606 次文件读（`census_all_reads.py`，$0） | 第三版 0 个错数、156 次读漏 3 次（全是资本开支）；第二版 2 个错数；第四版漏 24 次（5 月）、16 次（8 月）。我自己判错的：6 个对的数被我的引用检查拒（漏星号、跳格），8 月\"只认本季\"规则错，第 13 轮 3 条\"有争议\"的数是标准答案自己用的行，第三版全过后又改第四版 | 收敛方案：提示词定为第三版不再改；修引用检查（$0 重放全部 606 次读核对）；在 8 月财报上用第三版读一次（约 8 美分，只有\"收错数\"能叫停）；然后做进生产 |\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\"自己的量，别的期间\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n25:Nothing is open. The seven items this consolidation left for Alex were answered on 2026-11-05 (D368) and are written into the sections\n41:  the narrowest open question, plus the same answer's own candidates (D207, D259, D264, D265); the former coverage-start exception is retired (D370).\n69:  text and current documentation are English, the pages written for Alex's review included (D368); source quotations and historical\n146:- **Filing** (D207, D254, D259, D264, D265, D268, D273): a statement goes under the narrowest open question it bears on, as that\n169:- **The next extraction version** (D368): asset-thesis rungs stated against guidance, each thesis naming its favourable end (D186), and\n179:- Any company's own quantity is a thesis under that company, private companies included (D187); *(not built; to be built, D368: it needs\n221:- A new thesis's dependencies are chosen in matching (D51); the default Jev path does not ask for them, so a thesis opened from an article\n222:  has none of its own *(to be built, D368)*; a later item may add a dependency to an existing thesis (D191 point 2) *(to be built, D368)*.\n227:  (D51, D191, D195); daily, in one round (D63).\n236:- **Frozen** (D354): the collision judge (`collision-v2`), the judge (`judging-v7`), the matching prompt (`matching-v3`), the judge's\n249:  unresolved is dropped (D368).\n260:  into English with §4's standard version and a §5 status line corrected (D368); every step starts with its §0 checklist. Its steps and results are in §8 and `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`.\n279:  decis