~$9 (beyond D439); mutants not run (permission refused) | in force | `reflection-6/gate1-candidate/README.md`, `reflection-6/codex-challenge-36.md`–`38.md` |\n988:| D644 | 2026-11-16 | Council round 39: a fifth Stage A within the remaining budget (sol + A2 + v2) refused: D426 is Alex's specific decision not reversed by D439's general delegation, and the pair is unmeasured; no in-authority, in-budget step moves the production decision; the record waits on Alex | in force | `reflection-6/codex-challenge-39.md` |\n999:| D655 | 2026-11-17 | Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra (3 deciding targets, 2 reported, 5 controls, a share control; 52 sends, shared cap $3.60); verdict rules fixed before the send | in force | D655 record |\n1021:| D677 | 2026-11-19 | The release comparison's goal loop closed: the old system stays, no paid work continues; reversed only if Alex reverses D505 or funds a full run, with a written path to passing first (council consensus, D439/D544) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/council-c-codex.md` |\n1028:| D684 | 2026-11-20 | Under D683: Alex approves the presentation-only test and hands the phase-1 iteration to Claude under the council loop (D439 limits); fresh pool of 116 answers as of 09-06 that the design never read | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md` |\n1033:| D689 | 2026-11-20 | Alex chooses option 1: poc-v118 stays production, the hybrid's release line is paused, the release bar unchanged; council N (fresh Codex thread, consensus) closes the judge line and the c8 reading line for now under D543, D198 unchanged, nothing sent; reopening: judge on eight eligible failures on fresh questions plus matched controls and a source-checked summary (D198 option 2), then Alex's choice and funding; c8 on a traced decisive fact it delivers that old missed; D439 accounting error recorded ($39.65–$44.42 under two readings; $0 available without Alex) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.md` |\n1034:| D690 | 2026-11-20 | Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product and the research line rests until his new direction; B (other companies' own figures, the judge's carried conclusion) and C (new paid test questions) not taken; D689's reopening conditions stand; D681–D690 records committed locally, not pushed | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n1035:| D691 | 2026-11-20 | Alex chooses A after council Q (library useful for sources, not its number answers: linked questions contradict): no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few-cents probe; the dependency stretch D533–D542 stays a provisional candidate | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n1036:| D692 | 2026-11-20 | Under Alex's A: the dependency probe passes (linked 2 of 3 reconcile, unchanged 0 of 3; $0.0176); the stored extreme did not recur; the dependency design review reopens at $0, then Alex; the self-made reference traced apart | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md` |\n1256:## D51 · 2026-10-21 · Claude's open items settled: one re-judging rule, dependencies chosen in the matching call, no consensus\n3084:## D265 · 2026-11-02 · Extraction v72 / poc-v92 is the version: the default configuration, the base every later change builds on, the control of every later measurement; D207's narrowest rule is enforced in code\n3685:## D354 · 2026-11-03 · Steps 3 and 4 (opening and matching questions, judging them) are frozen as `poc-v108` runs them, after three draws on the frozen extraction\n3960:## D368 · 2026-11-05 · Alex's answers to the seven items left open by the consolidation\n4738:## D427 · 2026-11-11 · Clean Step 2 is closed and frozen; it goes to production only with the whole clean path\n4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n6375:## D533 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: this stretch of the lean investigation is closed and consolidated; the default and both systems stay; next a separate $0 assessment of D368's dependency channel on a stored, correctly directed case (council consensus, reflection round 24)\n6394:## D534 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency-channel assessment is corrected (its lines came from later conclusions); a $0 chronology and ordering proof comes before any measurement design (council consensus, reflection round 25)\n6411:## D535 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the one-chain ordering proof of D368's direction is accepted with its limits; a source-backed case and a verified pre-judgement state of 2026-07-14 come before any measurement design (council consensus, reflection round 26)\n6432:## D536 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: no measurement of the reversed reading direction is sent now; next, at $0, size where dependency selection could act in the stored unseeded fresh week (council consensus, reflection round 27)\n6457:## D537 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency-selection census has one clear case and negative controls; before any send, the edge's effect on filing and judging is proved on stored data (council consensus, reflection round 28)\n6479:## D538 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: one dependency edge shows the intended conclusion to the judge and removes seven filing links; the dependency slice's design is opened at $0, beginning with the separation of the edge's two uses (council consensus, reflection round 29)\n6504:## D539 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the separation of a dependency edge's two uses is kept as a candidate, not yet the builder's contract; its design continues at $0 (council consensus, reflection round 30)\n6525:## D540 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the separation stays a provisional research candidate; the filing and duplicate-label contracts are finished at $0 before any selection design or send (council consensus, reflection round 31)\n6544:## D541 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the seed edge's label stops everything that touches a seed edge; the filing finding is bounded; the unseeded failure-and-reader contract is finished at $0 before the separation is called sound (council consensus, reflection round 32)\n6566:## D542 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency stretch is closed with the separation recorded as a provisional candidate; the status is consolidated; nothing is sent (council consensus, reflection round 33)\n6589:## D543 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the cold reflection on the lean path: D518 stands with its reasons, the choice of system is not made in Alex's place, and no investigation is opened (reflection council consensus)\n10360:## D690 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product, the research line rests until his new direction; the D681–D689 records are committed locally\n10375:## D691 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A after council Q: no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents\n10398:## D692 · 2026-11-20 · Under Alex's A (D691): the dependency probe passes its registered rule; the dependency design review reopens at $0\n54:  re-asked caused the China miss. Observed defect of the frozen judge: it names the export-controls theme as a dependency of the China\n77:**Clean architecture Step 1 (2026-11-06, isolated work on `clean-arch`):** Alex reopened work with the clean architecture. An experimental prepared-source handoff now preserves the archived page, prior cleaned text, source-role decisions and selected-line mapping without changing the original database; quotations for prepared items must also occur contiguously in the original captured page. Two seven-item runs are available in the [clean architecture PRD](../clean-arch/PRD.md), one in the earlier selection order and one in recorded page-timestamp order. The source selector is not a production service and source ordering is not established event-arrival ordering. The runs expose unresolved semantic problems: citations can omit supporting facts despite an exact location match; model output can change a benchmark into a deployment, reverse a backup relation, omit a named customer or assign an unstated currency. A blinded 84-call check-placement/wording comparison and a 27-call same-article citation-completion diagnostic did not give a clean semantic fix and are not adopted. The latter missed an omitted connectivity condition and a reversed backup relationship, and left six expected evidence reviews unaddressed. A further five-round Codex–Claude council produced a narrowly scoped Step 1 link candidate, independently checked for prompt-contract drift. A six-article, 36-call blind comparison completed; the candidate still produced an explicitly self-contradictory link and both arms consistently omitted the same Kyber report and company response. It is not adopted and has not changed the active PRD prompt. A trace confirms that both the Kyber report and open Kyber thesis were supplied, and the raw model answers omitted the report and denial; the reason is not established. See ../poc/data/clean-step1-kyber-trace-2026-11-06/TRACE.md. An isolated six-call comparison showed that hiding the Kyber thesis did not recover the report or denial in any draw. A second six-call comparison returned them in 3/3 draws with the original Kyber paragraph alone and 0/3 with the full article; length, position and surrounding content changed together, so the reason is not isolated. Excerpt outputs have source-attribution limitations. Neither experiment changed state or established a production fix. (Superseded: the next task then was a whole-article coverage approach; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) See ../clean-arch/STEP1-IMPLEMENTATION-COUNCIL.md. The earlier four-round council agreed that no tested semantic fix is ready; its next investigation is a source-backed review of the 49-item historical run and its 160 evidence records, with overlapping issue flags and separate article-level omissions, then a separate comparison of the seven-item replays. See ../clean-arch/STEP1-COUNCIL-REVIEW.md. Preserve relevant evidence while identifying the next intervention; production/frozen history remains as described below. See [Step 1 run log](../clean-arch/STEP1-RUN-LOG.md) and [English reading page](../clean-arch/architecture.html).\n79:**Sealed (D379, 2026-11-06):** Alex asked to clean up and seal this version while he re-plans the system design. Work stops here and is sealed as it is: main's working tree is committed on branch `seal/2026-11-06` (tag `sealed-2026-11-06`) and merged into `main` on Alex's word (PR #10); the sealed split and two side experiments are pushed on their own branches (D379). No PRD 11 experiment is open, and the E1 next task below is withdrawn. The next task is Alex's re-planned system design.\n81:**E1 diagnosed (2026-11-06, Alex chose E1):** of 57 helpful matters frozen production wrote and then dropped, two readers agree on 17 link misses (4 core), 3 opening misses (1 core) and 24 small matters the standard itself drops; 10 are disputed on the fallback clause and 3 were quote refusals. Opening is not the experiment. The core of the link misses is the model reading a question's period, population or named configuration as a boundary; only 8 of the 13 window draws it dropped were lost to the product. No production change; $0.02 of probes. My recommendation was to fold that narrow change into the next extraction version; withdrawn by the seal (D379). Details: `docs/research/2026-11-06-e1-no-home-drops/README.md`, PRD 11 E1.\n114:**One-day smoke completed (2026-11-05 UTC):** Alex requested a quick 1–2 day end-to-end test. One day, 2026-08-29, ran in `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/v117-one-day-smoke-2026-11-05/`: config v117, an 8/28 historical library, 40 extraction calls, 93 evidence records written, four new questions, 54 judged and zero terminal failures. Two judgement attempts were refused and corrected. A Microsoft revenue forecast of $391.1bn was assigned to a rung whose upper bound excludes $391.1bn; the same article's actual quarterly revenue and next-quarter guidance were dropped with no home. Some source dates and bodies are not verified, and an independent 14-article sample review was incomplete due to truncated text. This is not semantic or production acceptance. Findings and scope: `docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/one-day-v117-smoke-2026-11-05.zh.md` in that worktree. The clean source-text comparison and its condition-hidden review are complete; council discussion of next steps is ongoing.\n116:**D371, in progress:** Alex directed that present and forward-looking revenue and financial information should be tracked. Diagnose the same-day extraction and filing losses before designing a general change. No new financial tracking implementation has been accepted yet. The old frozen standard and gold are unchanged. The original prompt-only pilot failed design review. The user approved an exact prompt addition for an experiment; it is not a production implementation. Four paired real-article diagnostic calls per arm completed for the exact approved sentence: v74i versus experimental role-d371-pilot. Microsoft next-quarter guidance and NVIDIA FY2028 guidance still dropped in the treatment; a single draw is not acceptance or proof of causation. Details: docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/d371-prompt-pilot-results.zh.md (isolated worktree). The requested full prompt audit and restructure were drafted experimentally; five real-article paired diagnostic requests per arm completed. Microsoft revenue guidance was missed in both arms, and the draft produced unsupported original dates, a quote refusal and suspect links. No production prompt change or acceptance; see restructure-pilot-results.zh.md in the isolated worktree.\n118:**Clean Step 1 coverage council (2026-11-06):** Codex and Claude Code independently reviewed the existing attempts and completed three discussion rounds. The proposed next research candidate moves the existing evidence-reading block ahead of the thesis-opening block while preserving the article, open-thesis state and paired output. It is a hypothesis, not an implemented or validated fix. A complete prompt/contract audit and independent review precede any controlled Luna comparison. Historical paragraph-based and source-first experiments, their noise and attribution problems, and the rejected overlap-based merge are recorded in [the council review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-COUNCIL.md). No new Luna experiment was run in the council.\n126:**Clean Step 1 source handoff council (2026-11-07):** The ongoing [council and offline checks](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-HANDOFF-COUNCIL.md) reconstructed 16 matching article-34 controls, all omitting a Kyber report and denial; the cause remains unknown. The 20-article saved source-role overlap review distinguished previously cited AI-generated summary lines and an unrelated recommendation from authored body. The clean runner does not send the saved source-role labels; the council chose to first compare original and previously selected source text on ten known articles. The isolated 60-call source-text comparison and condition-hidden review are complete; [results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-TEXT-RESULTS.md) show specific contamination reductions alongside persistent omissions and changed meaning. It did not advance state or write production. The isolated six-article low-versus-medium source-fidelity diagnostic completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-REASONING-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) show partial improvements alongside persistent source-qualification and attribution concerns; no production setting is changed. The [prompt audit](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-PROMPT-AUDIT.md) maps the observed failures to the full request and signed standard. The six-article isolated schema-description comparison completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review; the candidate did not preserve the repeated example qualification and is not adopted. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SUMMARY-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md). A further six-article 36-call low-versus-medium comparison used corpus-cleaned sources outside the original 49-item clean replay and a fixed exploratory context; results were mixed, including unsupported links and incorrect attribution/date fields. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-ADDITIONAL-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). The structured-claims candidate was not sent after review revealed scope and complexity concerns. Council review of the next action is ongoing. The date-text schema-description diagnostic completed 48/48 calls on eight known cases, with mixed results; the candidate is not adopted. A selected-run census found twelve literal \"null\" strings in date-text fields, but no production writer impact is established. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-DESCRIPTION-RESULTS.md). A further preregistered eight-source date comparison completed 48/48 calls; the candidate lost a supported company-article statement date in all three draws on one source and is not adopted. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-NEW-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). A bounded corpus census confirmed 163 source pages across three explicit generated-summary structures whose labels were removed while some summary text was retained; two NVIDIA cases were reproduced through the cleaner. [Source provenance investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). A read-only source-lineage replay reproduced 363/363 cleaned pages with current inputs, preserved ambiguous original-line locations, and surfaced the generated-summary label loss for review. [Source investigation and lineage replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). An offline neighboring-context observation exposed only 144 or 149 of 163 known labels and introduced many other page lines; it is not adopted as a general source fix. [Observations and viewer](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md). A new [saved-quote integrity investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-QUOTE-INTEGRITY-CENSUS.md) reconstructed 360 saved answers across eight overlapping cohorts, including 78 prepared-source calls. Five saved unverified passage instances were complete matches under the existing normalization; an in-memory candidate recovered their original slices, while ten others remained unverified. The normalized source-slice lookup is now installed only in the isolated clean Step 1 runner; saved-answer and entry-point checks are recorded there. Page provenance, Unicode completeness, production resource budgets and writer integration remain open. The existing writer stores only one quote, whereas 63 of 160 evidence items in the 49-article exploratory trace have multiple passages. A [source-first 49-article coverage review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-CENSUS.md) separates material missing from the model input from source-visible omissions in the saved answers, with uncertain matter boundaries labeled. (Superseded: the next investigation then was why supplied material is missed; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) The canonical prompt and production configuration remain unchanged. Adding fallible role annotations remains a separate untested candidate. Council streams and handoffs are in `poc/data/clean-step1-ongoing-council-2026-11-07/`.\n138:- **Repository:** `main` holds the product, the frozen ruler and the research records; run databases, logs and model archives stay on disk (D353), located by the [data manifest](research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md). Worktrees: `/Users/lchingen/hivemind` is the main checkout, where slice branches are cut from `main`; `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28` (the extraction branch, merged on 2026-11-03) keeps in its ignored folders the stored end-to-end runs of `poc-v91` to `poc-v95` that later comparisons read (D359); `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-run-v109-2026-11-04` is the finished judging-v8 run's worktree. Older branches stay in Git without worktrees (D359); none is merged work in progress. The clean source-text comparison and its condition-hidden review are complete; council discussion of next steps is ongoing.\n145:4. **A thesis opened from an article gets no dependency of its own**: the default Jev matching asks for none (`views/jev_matching.py`), although D51 has the matching call choose them; themes still reach every company thesis through the theme block (D191, D195). Found in the 2026-11-05 consolidation; building it is decided (D368).\n149:8. **Seen once, not traced.** A judgement named a shown theme as a dependency and the check refused it twice, stopping a draw for a day (2026-11-02, D266). The sealed run's review recorded that a succession's opening evidence is not linked to the new question (D358), not yet checked against today's code.\n159:## One next task\n194:   next quarter's guidance or a consensus for the year, filed under total revenue only\n208:  [census](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/DEPENDENCY-SELECTION-CENSUS.md), D537). As the code stands\n210:  seven filing links ([proof](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/EDGE-PROOF-RESULT.md), D538). A design that\n212:  ([design](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md), D539 to D542): two proofs on stored\n213:  data, the package's suite run under it, every stored dependency row classed. If the slice is reopened, its review must first\n219:  is kept ([page](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md)).\n300:product's. The next step is a pilot of Alex's own product-level review on the stored fresh week (sixteen cards, three hidden\n322:  closing on a day without items was invisible at the next day's start (`src/hivemind/replay.py`, D566).\n448:**The one next task: none open (D689, D690, 2026-11-20).** poc-v118 is the product (Alex chose A, D690), and the research line\n460:  version with the decided dependencies, tested at $0 on the request text, then a few cents. Alex chose A (D691). The probe passed\n461:  its registered rule (D692, [RESULT.md](research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md), $0.0176): linked to\n463:  example was partly one unlucky sample. Next ($0): the dependency design review (D542's five open items, the reads/supports\n517:**Earlier next task, closed by D676 and D677 (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\n552:- **If the verdict is not a practical lead:** the council-loop skill on the traces, and the next try from another angle (D674).\n671:- **Alex's instruction (D412):** every round is reflected on in the council to a recorded consensus, then the next test goes\n674:  form until the second result is read in full and reported; then one next step (if the event class is not closed, report\n676:  missed on due day or direction, diagnose the figure's due day over its whole class first); the next stage is not asked for\n678:  carry; whether an event undone counts as happened; the footnote marker; the next stage.\n796:- **The next step (D442–D444): an exploratory end-to-end census.** The clean path's stored chain (unseeded draws 2026-11-10, Stage A\n834:  next year's capex folded into this year's question (five of six clean draws), and show the standard's keep-apart line for unsigned deals\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '700,727p;3738,3765p;3960,4015p;4871,4896p;6375,6588p;10360,10433p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '700,727p;3738,3765p;3960,4015p;4871,4896p;6375,6588p;10360,10433p'\"","aggregated_output":"   700\t  the category yields) change per category, part 1 is shared and parts 3 and 5 are filled by code; each of T1–T15 has\n   701\t  its own prompt (T16 is not tracked by default); the output format is enforced by code, not written in the prompt;\n   702\t  every view and piece of evidence carries a checked source; failures retry from their step. One assembled prompt\n   703\t  (T7 news) is drawn on the page and in the PRD.\n   704\t- Decides: extraction is frozen as v1. Not frozen: how an item too long for one call is cut; the exact wording of each\n   705\t  category's prompt, written and tested on stored items when it is built, each version recorded in Config. A later\n   706\t  change needs a new decision.\n   707\t- Enforced: the extract node's status and `PROMPT_EXAMPLE`, `PROMPT_NOTES` of `docs/system-design/new-facts.js`;\n   708\t  `docs/prd/05-extraction.md`.\n   709\t- Changed 2026-10-18 (Alex: \"应该不会context 太长这不是一个问题，pass\"): cutting a long item is not an open item;\n   710\t  the only part not frozen is each category's prompt wording. A wording review aligned the page and the PRD: one\n   711\t  template, one prompt per category; step 2 names what a candidate view and its evidence carry, which the views\n   712\t  database reads; the source check is split between extraction (the quote is in the item) and the views database\n   713\t  (the source is in the processing record).\n   714\t- Changed by D37: frozen together with the input side; the page and the PRDs say 已冻结, not 定稿.\n   715\t\n   716\t## D36 · 2026-10-18 · One word per concept in the input and extraction modules\n   717\t\n   718\t- By: Alex (\"你和codex 要一起完全对齐用字用词，这个非常重要，不然我们的PRD就是瞎几把写的，你深度的抠\").\n   719\t- Why: rounds of review kept finding new wording mismatches, because each fix changed only the instance named. Claude\n   720\t  and Codex each took an independent inventory of every wording per concept in scope (universe, classification and\n   721\t  tagging, dispatch, extraction, and the sentences at their boundaries), and merged them into one glossary.\n   722\t- Decides: the glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section \"用词\") names one word per concept and the words not to use.\n   723\t  Notable choices: 信息 is the unit, 文件 is a text-form 信息 and 表格数据 a table-form one; 申报 and 申报代码 (not 表格代码,\n   724\t  which collided with 表格数据); 体裁 for transcript, minutes and the like (形式 is only text or table); 提示词模板 and\n   725\t  上传模板 (never a bare 模板); 角色 for the prompt's persona (身份 is the identity fields); 看法 for what authors in a\n   726\t  document think and 观点 only for the system's views; 说法 for what parties say and 主张 only for a view's claim;\n   727\t  主题层 and 对象层 for a view's level, separate from an evidence tier; 作者 (not 发布方). No rule changed.\n  3738\t  2. **No day-end re-judging without new evidence.** Pull mode closes the questions that are due and does nothing else at day end; it is\n  3739\t     revisited when a case is named.\n  3740\t  3. **A due day falls on or after the day the result is published,** set when the question is opened (the opening rule \"set the due date\n  3741\t     when the question can be resolved\", 06-views). A question whose result is still unknown on its due day closes at its state like any other;\n  3742\t     nothing waits (D54).\n  3743\t  4. **The frozen rung is recorded and shown, never a gate** (AGENTS §8). The closing record names the rung the question froze at; a question\n  3744\t     never judged closes with \"no data to verify\". Its judgement history, already stored and served, shows how the state moved up to the close.\n  3745\t     Telling a closing rung that reflects the published result from one that is still a forecast is not built until the first real due day\n  3746\t     (2026-12-31) gives a case.\n  3747\t- Built: `src/hivemind/pull.py` writes the closing record (rung and label, or \"no data to verify\"); `tests/test_pull.py` proves it (mutants:\n  3748\t  the first judgement instead of the last, the no-data branch removed). A $0 check on a copy of the frozen first draw with the day set to\n  3749\t  2027-03-01 closed the thirteen questions due by then at their last rung, and a dependent question's judging request shows the closed question\n  3750\t  with its last conclusion; two questions never judged closed with no state, which this change marks.\n  3751\t- Pages: PRD 07 becomes the closing contract (the D29 draft is removed from it; Git keeps it), PRD 08 states what pull mode does, the design\n  3752\t  page's two nodes and the closing drill-down say the same, and `docs/check.py` now reads both PRDs and both nodes in the wording check.\n  3753\t- Not built, not decided: fetching settlement figures (prices, filings) from a source; Claude's earlier daily duplicate check.\n  3754\t- After a read-only Codex review the same day, two gaps between this decision and the product were closed. (1) A closing on a day without\n  3755\t  items took the day's last sequence number, which belonged to the day before, so the question page showed the question closed a day\n  3756\t  early; pull mode now records the day under a sequence number of its own when it closes something on such a day (`pull.closing_sequence`).\n  3757\t  Census: 0 of the 42 day ends of the three frozen draws were affected, and 1 of the 119 days of the stored news window has no items\n  3758\t  (2026-10-27); in production a holiday is enough. (2) The closing record was served but never shown: the question page now shows it\n  3759\t  under \"About this thesis\" from the closing day on, and a closed question never judged shows \"No data to verify\". Tests:\n  3760\t  `tests/test_pull.py` (the empty-day closing, read through `service.is_open_as_of`) and `poc/ui/test/model.test.js` (`closingAt`); each\n  3761\t  fails on its mutant (the old numbering; the record shown while the question is open).\n  3762\t\n  3763\t## D357 · 2026-11-04 · Clean the repository of configurations and prompts nothing current names; the code paths of retired versions are a slice of their own\n  3764\t\n  3765\t- Alex, with D356: \"然后你也需要清理repo不要让旧的东西影响我们整个sanity\".\n  3960\t## D368 · 2026-11-05 · Alex's answers to the seven items left open by the consolidation\n  3961\t\n  3962\t- Alex, on the seven items at the head of `docs/DECISIONS.md` (D367): \"1. 这个你记住，我们要做 2. 做 3. 好那就按照后面的那条来 4. 好你来定 5. 你要来帮我看到底做不做\n  3963\t  6. 你看该怎么处理核实 7. 不，用英文吧。\"; then \"你开始逐条改，不要drift, 记录下来把1-7都清理了我们再commit push,开始快速做\".\n  3964\t- Decided:\n  3965\t  1. The asset-thesis rungs stated against guidance, each thesis naming its favourable end (D186), and the rename of `industry_aggregate`\n  3966\t     to `shared_quantity` (D191 point 4) are built in the next extraction version. The frozen v74i stays until then (D274); the new\n  3967\t     version is measured against it.\n  3968\t  2. The three decided rules not yet built are built, each designed and measured as its own slice (AGENTS §2, §7): a company's own\n  3969\t     quantity is a thesis under that company, private companies included (D187); a later item may add a dependency to an existing thesis\n  3970\t     (D191 point 2); the matching step chooses a new thesis's dependencies (D51), which the default Jev path does not ask today.\n  3971\t  3. At the due day pull mode closes the due questions and does nothing else (D356); D248 boundary 2's step that opens the next-deadline\n  3972\t     successor of an event question falling due unresolved is dropped.\n  3973\t  4. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation, by D208's design: a seed question's dependency arrow means \"supports\". For filing, the\n  3974\t     supporting (driver) question is the narrower one, so a statement linked to both goes to it, as `extraction.narrowest_links` does\n  3975\t     today. For judging, the supported (root) question reads the supporting questions' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged\n  3976\t     before their roots. Today the judging code reads the stored edge the other way: the driver reads the root and is judged after it\n  3977\t     (`seeding.seed_views` stores the seed's `depends_on` as the driver's dependency). The fix separates the two uses of the edge; it\n  3978\t     changes judgements, so it is measured before it enters the default.\n  3979\t  5. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: PRD 10 is corrected without changing any rule. §4 names the frozen standard's version 5 and\n  3980\t     §5 carries a status line (its links-rule version failed in §8 step 5; D361 keeps the fallback sentence).\n  3981\t  6. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: the three statements of the frozen extraction standard page that later decisions changed are\n  3982\t     noted in a dated correction record beside it, `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard-corrections.md`; the page is not edited (D261). Each\n  3983\t     statement was found verbatim in the page: \"抽取看不到库\" (§4 and §5.3; changed by D251 and D264), \"研究的交付物是论证\" (§7; the\n  3984\t     argument record set aside on 2026-11-04) and \"只有事实能确定落在哪一档\" (§5 and §7; changed by D260 and D263).\n  3985\t  7. Pages written for Alex's review are in English, like the rest of the maintained documentation (D163); PRD 10 is translated, his\n  3986\t     quotes kept in their own language. What is said to him keeps the plain-language rule (AGENTS, Authority and scope).\n  3987\t- Recorded in the same change: `docs/DECISIONS.md` (the open items cleared into their sections), AGENTS §11, the README, PRD 10, the\n  3988\t  correction record and `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` (the builds of items 1, 2 and 4 are the next tasks, in an order given there).\n  3989\t\n  3990\t## D369 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Capture core and supporting evidence without a strict boundary; retain the MXC case\n  3991\t\n  3992\t- Alex: “我觉得往后核心和辅助其实只要是捕捉到就好，不用真的严格区分了，把它作为decision, 因为这两个边界很模糊，我觉得没必要纠结到死” and “我觉得留下辅助，只要LLM自己的判断是相关且逻辑清晰就好”.\n  3993\t- For future extraction evaluation, evidence that the standard would keep as core or supporting is assessed together for whether it was captured. Do not make a hard pass/fail distinction between those two weights. This does not establish that every statement is relevant, change the optional or excluded boundary, replace source tiers, or remove checks for meaning, attribution, uncertainty, errors and delivery. Historical scores retain their original definitions and are not compared as if this was their ruler.\n  3994\t- In the reviewed Microsoft MXC example, retain the reported announcement as supporting evidence. The model may judge relevance using a clear logical connection; an unquantified indirect connection is not automatically rejected. A proposed NVIDIA demand effect is an inference, not a fact attributed to Microsoft; the article does not say MXC requires NVIDIA hardware. This is not permission to accept unrelated material or to hard-code a list or new mandatory output field.\n  3995\t- The frozen standard v5, golden-v5, seeds and historical results remain byte-for-byte unchanged (D261/D262). Applying this decision to a new real-article gold requires a separate evaluation version under D261. Alex asked for a real-article gold; treating that as authorization to develop the separate version is an implementation interpretation, not a quotation from his decision. It still needs its own traced references, independent review and Alex's sign-off before scoring. The experimental evidence comparison has not been sent.\n  3996\t\n  3997\t\n  3998\t## D370 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Remove the separate earnings-report import\n  3999\t\n  4000\t- Alex: “我觉得财报这个基本是没有的，我觉得可以记录下，删除这个财报倒入的环节。重新整理现在的系统设计”. He also previously directed removal of the 22 artificial preset questions and confirmed that extraction should read the existing research library.\n  4001\t- Remove the separate coverage-start report reading tied to seeded questions and do not add an earnings report as background to each news extraction request. This supersedes D363–D366 to the extent they require that separate report import and seeded default. An earnings release or filing arriving as an actual input remains a normal item under D28; existing research questions remain extraction context. Historical seeds, gold, results and records remain historical, not a new active starting library.\n  4002\t- Evidence is bounded: a diagnostic with three archived NVDA articles, the same 68-question 2026-08-28 library, two arms and three draws gave 14/27 complete matters without the appended report versus 13/27 with it; one report-arm answer supplied an unestablished CFO statement date. This tested adding a report to extraction, not the distinct D363–D366 coverage-start mechanism; the removal of both is Alex's decision, not a claim that the experiment directly tested both. The library is historical and not the complete article-day state. See `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/existing-library-results-2026-11-05.md` in the local worktree.\n  4003\t- Implementation and rollout status must be stated separately from this decision. The frozen earlier rulers and scores stay unchanged; no conclusion about other companies or report-as-source inputs is implied.\n  4004\t\n  4005\t\n  4006\t## D371 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Track present and forward-looking financial information\n  4007\t\n  4008\t- Alex: “收入和财务这边对于当下，未来应该都是需要track 的，你应该要修改”. This is the product decision for the financial extraction and filing issue discussed immediately before it.\n  4009\t- Present and forward-looking financial performance, estimates and guidance need to be tracked as evidence relevant to investment questions; a quarterly period is not itself a reason to withhold information from a related annual question. Do not confuse retaining and connecting evidence with automatically opening a separate question for every line. The research model continues to judge relevance and the strength of the connection; do not hard-code company, item or metric-specific importance. Existing research questions remain context; the separate report import and 22 preset questions remain retired under D370.\n  4010\t- The frozen earlier standard, gold and scores remain unchanged. Where the new decision changes how present financial context is treated, use a dated decision/correction and a separately versioned evaluation; never silently relabel old gold or compare scores across rulers. Implementation and diagnostic evidence must be recorded separately.\n  4011\t\n  4012\t## D372 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Score future evidence by usefulness, not core versus supporting\n  4013\t\n  4014\t- Alex: “我们金标的打分只要量化好有帮助/没帮助就好，至于是核心还是辅助我们不用特别分开因为这样造成不必要的ambiguity,这是之后量测的准则你记录好”.\n  4015\t- For future evidence measurement, the scoring distinction is whether a statement is helpful or not helpful to the investment-research task. Do not separately classify or score helpful evidence as core versus supporting. Quantify useful evidence captured or missed and unhelpful evidence returned, with the evaluated population and counting unit stated; inspect the source and output, not only aggregate numbers. A statement's source tier and faithful attribution, conditions and dates remain separate properties, not a proxy for usefulness.\n  4871\t## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n  4872\t\n  4873\t- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n  4874\t- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n  4875\t- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n  4876\t- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, \"Authority and scope\" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 \"Own the loop\"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\n  4877\t- **Scope:** all modules Alex has taken up; the current work is clean Step 1 (gates 2 and 3 of `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/COMBINED-PLAN.md`), then the Step 4 judgement faults that kept Stage B from passing.\n  4878\t\n  4879\t## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\n  4880\t\n  4881\t- **Council** (D439; Alex not active): an independent Codex member and Claude argued four rounds (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mj-*`). Agreed facts: gate 2 failed under its declared rules (two stop lines on the memory article); the link line measured the wrong thing (c8's request returns an uncovered statement with empty links); the 3-of-9 against 0-of-9 memory-thesis difference is real and its cause is not established. The council's first position was to keep c8; Claude's was a larger re-send. The consensus, after Claude adopted the council's changes (a margin fixed in advance, a three-way result in which inconclusive is not a pass, retained statements decisive, an exercised-control rule, a named and simulation-validated interval): \"Council position: consensus on the rule in mj-challenge-2.md as amended by mj-challenge-3.md\" (`mj-codex-4.md`).\n  4882\t- **Decided:** the diagnostic in `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate2/MEMORY-DIAGNOSTIC.md` runs (108 sends, ceiling $2.0); its rule is `gate2/memory_rule.py`, frozen by sha256. c15yc goes on to gate 3's design only on \"proceed\" for both decisive outcomes; otherwise c8 stays and the council decides the next step. The gate-2 failure stays recorded.\n  4883\t- **Amended 2026-11-13 (council round mj-5, `council/mj-codex-5.md`: \"Council position: consensus on (a)\"):** the 11 jobs the $2.0 ceiling never sent are sent alone, same requests, under a $1.2 completion ceiling (a recorded departure from D440's step ceiling; the $40 total unchanged), before any diagnostic answer is read; the combined sample must hold 18 per arm per draw, or the diagnostic is inconclusive.\n  4884\t\n  4885\t## D441 · 2026-11-13 · The memory diagnostic does not let c15yc go on: the year change stops, c8 stays (rule fixed by council consensus, D440)\n  4886\t\n  4887\t- **Result** (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate2/MEMORY-RESULT.md`): memory-price thesis 17 of 54 (c15yc) against 28 of 54 (c8), difference -20.4 points, 90% interval (-34.6, -4.8): inconclusive under the frozen rule; retention 49 against 49: proceed. The rule required both to proceed, so c15yc does not go on.\n  4888\t- **Decided (by the rule the council fixed before the send, D440; no new judgement):** the combined Step 1 candidate c15yc stops; c8 stays in force. The year change moved its error to a neighbouring case (capex years separated, the memory question pushed from the ruler's 2027-against-2026 shape to 2026), so under D391 it is not tuned further on these articles. Change 2 alone (the scoped capacity counterexample) is not carried as its own version without a council decision: its measured target without change 1 is one doubtful aggregate in 729 c8 calls.\n  4889\t- **Next:** the council chooses the next step toward the PRD's production goal (D439).\n  4890\t\n  4891\t## D442 · 2026-11-13 · Next step: D431's same-day end-to-end comparison, run as a diagnostic (council consensus under D439)\n  4892\t\n  4893\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mk-*`): Claude's reflection written first (`mk-my-reflection.md`); an independent Codex member investigated cold and reached the same recommendation (`mk-codex.md`: \"Run the bounded D431 comparison as a diagnostic, then choose the repair from the final-answer losses\"), correcting two of Claude's statements (the comparison does not by itself identify the largest cause; Stage B also missed its last-judgement line on the strictest reading). Consensus: \"Council position: consensus on the next step in mk-challenge-1.md\" (`mk-codex-2.md`).\n  4894\t- **Decided:** the next step is D431's same-day comparison as a diagnostic, never an acceptance and never waiving Step 4's failed lines: the clean path (c8, frozen Steps 2–3, the ladder step as it ran in the fourth Stage A, the frozen judge) against production as it now runs (poc-v116, no preset questions), the 14-day window, three draws each, the seven graded questions reported one by one, every lost answer read back through the opened question, the evidence it received and the judgement. Before any send: the comparison, matching rules, stop conditions and ceiling frozen in a design document; both paths' requests verified at no cost by replay; a component-by-component cost estimate from stored runs; a council review of the design until a round finds nothing serious.\n  4895\t- **Correction, 2026-11-13:** \"production as it now runs\" is `poc-v118` (D370, D374, the replay default; `scripts/replay.py` refuses `poc-v116`, which carries the retired baseline block). D442's \"poc-v116\" above is a factual error of mine; the decision means v118, as D431 says (\"production as it now runs\").\n  4896\t\n  6375\t## D533 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: this stretch of the lean investigation is closed and consolidated; the default and both systems stay; next a separate $0 assessment of D368's dependency channel on a stored, correctly directed case (council consensus, reflection round 24)\n  6376\t\n  6377\t- **The dependency trace** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/missing-input/DEPENDENCY-TRACE-RESULT.md`): no directionally valid\n  6378\t  case in which a dependency's conclusion would supply the needed figure, among the 22 reference facts the old system filed\n  6379\t  under another question (three with no question on their matter; the trial's 19 are the never-delivered subset). The council's\n  6380\t  wording governs: the one valid example is an unsized report, which may still have value; \"D368 is not a remedy\" is withdrawn\n  6381\t  (no judgement was re-run; some relations were unrecorded); D368's build stays decided.\n  6382\t- **Decided, citing D439:** (1) this stretch is closed and consolidated on the decision page (its section 7: what is still Alex's\n  6383\t  to choose; what he has decided and awaits implementation and acceptance, D375 and D368, not asked again; the defects with\n  6384\t  their evidence). (2) Production stays the default and both systems stay. (3) Waiting for Alex is not the next task: D439 lets\n  6385\t  the council decide a new version or a paid step, and a frozen piece or a cost of several dollars is not by itself a reason to\n  6386\t  wait; no such step is approved by this review. (4) **The next slice, $0, outside PRD 10's filing work:** on stored data,\n  6387\t  identify an existing supporting-question-to-supported-question pair under D368 and inspect the conclusion and shortened\n  6388\t  reasons that would reach the supported question at the relevant time (the Ohio example included as an unsized case): does\n  6389\t  the decided channel convey useful information in a real, correctly directed case. **Stop:** if no stored case establishes both\n  6390\t  the direction and what the receiving judge would see, the exercise is reported as unexercised and returned to the council\n  6391\t  before any measurement is designed; that absence does not cancel D368's build. A case found frames a separate design and its\n  6392\t  controls; no improved answer is inferred without a test.\n  6393\t\n  6394\t## D534 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency-channel assessment is corrected (its lines came from later conclusions); a $0 chronology and ordering proof comes before any measurement design (council consensus, reflection round 25)\n  6395\t\n  6396\t- **Claude's assessment** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md`): on the first frozen seeded\n  6397\t  draw, 14 conclusion lines built in D368's direction, 8 holding a figure absent from the receiving request.\n  6398\t- **The council's finding (checked in the store):** the supporting conclusions used were judged after the receiving question in the\n  6399\t  same day-end round (total revenue at judgement 198; its data-center supporter at 202) and had themselves read the receiver's\n  6400\t  conclusion: the lines are a counterfactual assembled from later outputs, and feeding them back would be a circle. The eight\n  6401\t  are edges into two receiving questions only. The stop condition of round 24 is not met as written; the count is a lead. The\n  6402\t  \"48 calls, ten cents\" estimate is withdrawn.\n  6403\t- **Decided, citing D439:** before any measurement design, at $0: (1) reconstruct the stored chronology for the two receiving\n  6404\t  questions (what existed before each call; what relied on the receiver; what the frozen reference and the sources say of the\n  6405\t  figures); (2) on a scratch copy, exercise the decided ordering and propagation with labelled fake judgement outputs\n  6406\t  (supporters first; changed conclusions queue the right dependants; no same-round circle; the edges' filing meaning unchanged;\n  6407\t  an article-opened question as a stated limit or a synthetic check); (3) stop if this cannot be done without changing a frozen\n  6408\t  piece, if a cycle or an unintended filing change appears, or if no source-backed, decision-relevant case is identified. D368\n  6409\t  directs both the corrected reading and the separate dependency selection; neither is accepted by the other's result.\n  6410\t\n  6411\t## D535 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the one-chain ordering proof of D368's direction is accepted with its limits; a source-backed case and a verified pre-judgement state of 2026-07-14 come before any measurement design (council consensus, reflection round 26)\n  6412\t\n  6413\t- **Done at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md`): the stored chronology (every\n  6414\t  supporting conclusion that existed before a receiver's call had been produced with the receiver's earlier conclusion in view);\n  6415\t  the ordering and propagation proof (`ordering_proof.py`: the production judging round on a scratch copy, the edges read in\n  6416\t  D368's direction for the judging use only, labelled fake outputs; seven registered expectations hold; a mutant keeping the\n  6417\t  stored direction fails).\n  6418\t- **The council's review:** the proof stands as a bounded wiring result for one chain; it does not show the information free of\n  6419\t  circular influence (the other supporting conclusions shown are stored ones made under the old direction). Claude's statement\n  6420\t  that the frozen reference answers both questions from their own figures is wrong and corrected: it also uses data-center,\n  6421\t  shipment and Vera CPU evidence for total revenue, and its total-revenue view with a segment-share inference for data-center\n  6422\t  revenue.\n  6423\t- **Decided, citing D439:** before the council reviews any measurement design, at $0: (a) read the figures of the candidate\n  6424\t  supporting lines against their source passages and the reference, stated figures apart from a judge's calculations and\n  6425\t  assumptions, and identify at least one source-backed, decision-relevant case; (b) establish whether the state of 2026-07-14\n  6426\t  before that day's judging round can be rebuilt and verified against the stored run, the retired preset questions accounted\n  6427\t  for; if not, stop and return the mismatch. A measurement would run the old and the corrected direction from copies of that\n  6428\t  one state (a one-day switch diagnostic of the corrected reading, not acceptance for today's default or for dependency\n  6429\t  selection), with harm, benefit and inconclusive registered before any send and its rule sized and calibrated before a pass\n  6430\t  line is named. An extra round after the window is at most a separately labelled exploration.\n  6431\t\n  6432\t## D536 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: no measurement of the reversed reading direction is sent now; next, at $0, size where dependency selection could act in the stored unseeded fresh week (council consensus, reflection round 27)\n  6433\t\n  6434\t- **Done at $0 after D535** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md`): the seeded run's state\n  6435\t  of 2026-07-14 before its judging round rebuilt from stored answers and verified table by table, the stored-direction round\n  6436\t  re-run from it identical to the stored one; the whole round dry in D368's direction with labelled fakes (14 to 18 calls; seven\n  6437\t  registered expectations hold; a mutant fails); the reference's ten facts for data-center revenue traced through the stored\n  6438\t  requests; the three stored seeded draws scored on the frozen reference as they are (15, 15, 16 of 17 agree; total revenue and\n  6439\t  data-center revenue in all three); judgements shown not to feed back into reading or matching requests.\n  6440\t- **Claude's errors, recorded:** the first source-backed case was the wrong pick; a lookup by wording matched statement ids; the\n  6441\t  table counted statements only, so \"four facts would be brought\" and \"the only sized reference is removed\" were too strong (the\n  6442\t  council's correction: the consensus, the guidance and the H200 permission already arrive through the total-revenue line or the\n  6443\t  theme block); and the earlier record of 2026-11-03 and 04 (`docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/core-problem.md`,\n  6444\t  `review-core-codex.md`) had not been searched before D533, nor D368 item 4 read whole: it was settled by Claude on Alex's\n  6445\t  delegation (\"好你来定\"), not in Alex's own words.\n  6446\t- **Decided, citing D439:** neither the one-day switch nor a 14-day judging-only comparison is sent now. D368 item 4 stays a\n  6447\t  recorded decision awaiting build and measurement; these results do not establish that a uniform reversal helps, and no other\n  6448\t  design replaces it here (a design that changes how a part and its whole read each other returns to the council). The harness\n  6449\t  is kept as that slice's acceptance material. **Next, $0:** in the stored unseeded fresh-week run of the old system, for each\n  6450\t  question opened, identify the questions and same-article candidates the matching step was allowed to consider; find candidate\n  6451\t  supporting relations among them, negative cases included; read their sources and the conclusions existing at that time; count\n  6452\t  which could carry a useful, source-backed conclusion in the permitted direction and which would repeat the theme block, need\n  6453\t  a question not yet open, or risk a cycle. A design census, not a claim about what the matching step would choose. Stop, and\n  6454\t  return to the council, if the openings yield no identifiable positive case and negative control, or if the relation cannot be\n  6455\t  stated without changing D368's contract. No send or build follows automatically.\n  6456\t\n  6457\t## D537 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency-selection census has one clear case and negative controls; before any send, the edge's effect on filing and judging is proved on stored data (council consensus, reflection round 28)\n  6458\t\n  6459\t- **The census** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/DEPENDENCY-SELECTION-CENSUS.md`): over the fifteen\n  6460\t  questions the old system opened in the stored unseeded fresh week, 97 pairs on which a dependency could have been chosen (each\n  6461\t  new question against the questions it was compared with and its same-article siblings). Claude's own read written first, then\n  6462\t  two blind readers of different model families (the same mark on 68 of 97; both mark \"the new question would want the earlier\n  6463\t  one's conclusion\" on 11, three of them strong). One clear case: data-center revenue FY2027 against total revenue FY2027 (the\n  6464\t  matching engine recorded \"part of\", 1.00): the total's conclusion carried the year's consensus ($406.05 billion from 09-23,\n  6465\t  about $412 billion from 09-25) and the $108 billion guidance (from 09-26), none of them anywhere in the data-center question's\n  6466\t  seven requests; its last answer names the gap and adds a step of its own. Negative controls: the Hugging Face commitments\n  6467\t  question (\"none\" in all three readings); a weakly granted pair whose line would carry a judge's own assumed numbers. The\n  6468\t  strongest driver relations of the week (Rubin shipping against the revenue questions) run from a later question to an earlier\n  6469\t  one and cannot be chosen at creation (D191 point 2, decided, unbuilt).\n  6470\t- **The council's corrections:** the $96.2 billion quarter was already in all seven requests (not a figure the line would\n  6471\t  supply); the one \"same question\" pair is one unordered pair; the line would not by itself make the answer supported.\n  6472\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the pair is a positive lead for the decided dependency-selection slice (D368 item 2), not a\n  6473\t  validation of it. Before the council reviews any six-call send on it: a bounded proof on stored data of what the edge would do\n  6474\t  to filing and to judging (a statement linked to both questions, the direction, ordering, cycle rejection, what the judge's\n  6475\t  request would contain, the unrelated pair as a negative case), with no frozen file changed. Stop, and return the conflict to\n  6476\t  the council as a design question, if the edge makes filing discard a home contrary to the governing rule, creates a cycle,\n  6477\t  cannot be represented without conflating the two meanings of the edge, or fails to show the intended conclusion.\n  6478\t\n  6479\t## D538 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: one dependency edge shows the intended conclusion to the judge and removes seven filing links; the dependency slice's design is opened at $0, beginning with the separation of the edge's two uses (council consensus, reflection round 29)\n  6480\t\n  6481\t- **The proof** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/EDGE-PROOF-RESULT.md`, `edge_proof.py`, $0): on scratch\n  6482\t  copies of the stored unseeded fresh week, the edge \"data-center revenue FY2027 depends on total revenue FY2027\" written by the\n  6483\t  writer's own steps. Judging, conditional on the rest of the week as stored: thirteen registered expectations hold (the reverse\n  6484\t  edge refused as a cycle; total revenue judged first; only the data-center request changes, by the dependency block holding\n  6485\t  total revenue's conclusion of the round cut at 600 characters and the closing sentence; the judge's check accepts the\n  6486\t  citation; every other judgement equal to the stored one); two mutants fail. Filing, every stored reading filed again by the\n  6487\t  production entry point (the control reproduces all 235 articles): through the narrowest rule in code (D265) the same edge\n  6488\t  removes the total-revenue link of seven statements: the company-wide outlook excluding China, which a total-revenue judgement\n  6489\t  cites and no other statement of it holds; three statements of the quarter's total and segment revenue in one sentence; three\n  6490\t  about the segment's competition (as the rule intends). An edge between an unrelated pair changes none.\n  6491\t- **The council's review:** the filing stop condition of D537 is met. A lost filing is not a demonstrated changed answer. The\n  6492\t  judging proof does not show a week with the edge present throughout. The selection slice (D368 item 2) cannot use the present\n  6493\t  edge behaviour unchanged; D368 already calls for separating the judging and filing uses for seed edges, and the proof extends\n  6494\t  the need to an article-created dependency. It decides no representation and does not authorize reversing D368's direction.\n  6495\t- **Decided, citing D439:** nothing is sent and no frozen piece changes. The dependency slice's design is opened at $0 for the\n  6496\t  council's review: the four tables of AGENTS §2, covering seed edges and matcher-chosen dependencies (a part reading its whole;\n  6497\t  a question reading a driver); the separate effects on filing, judging order, citations, propagation, cycles and later-added\n  6498\t  dependencies; the seven observed filing changes, a statement giving distinct figures for two questions, unrelated pairs and\n  6499\t  themes already covered by the theme block; D207, D259, D360 and D368's direction. Its first $0 proof must show the intended\n  6500\t  conclusion reaching the real judging path and the company-wide statement keeping its proper home, with unrelated filings\n  6501\t  unchanged and no cycle; if that cannot be shown under the existing decisions, stop and return the conflict, without fitting a\n  6502\t  special case. The six-call comparison stays deferred.\n  6503\t\n  6504\t## D539 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the separation of a dependency edge's two uses is kept as a candidate, not yet the builder's contract; its design continues at $0 (council consensus, reflection round 30)\n  6505\t\n  6506\t- **Reviewed** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md`, `separation_proof.py`): an edge\n  6507\t  carries a kind set by its writer (`supports`: a seed's driver and root, D208; `reads`: a dependency chosen for a question,\n  6508\t  D51 and PRD 06); judging reads one derived relation (a `reads` edge as written; a `supports` edge the other way round, D368\n  6509\t  item 4) and filing another (the driver of a `supports` edge is the narrower home; a `reads` edge states none). First proof,\n  6510\t  $0, 35 registered expectations: the unseeded fresh week's 235 filings unchanged with the `reads` edge and its last round\n  6511\t  showing the conclusion; a seeded draw's 243 filings unchanged and its last round ordered supporters first; circles refused.\n  6512\t- **The council's findings:** the proof passes its labelled examples and validates nothing more. Not applying D265's narrowest\n  6513\t  rule to a `reads` edge is a proposed interpretation with a trade-off, not a consequence D368 settles. The fresh-week result\n  6514\t  keeps double filing and does not show D207's one home satisfied. \"Kind is never inferred\" contradicted the table that read\n  6515\t  every old non-seed row as `reads`: the historical writers and ledgers must be inventoried and old rows given one explicit\n  6516\t  reading or refused, no ledger rewritten. The cycle rule had a counterexample: a `supports` edge and a `reads` edge in the\n  6517\t  same reading direction duplicate a reading and close no circle. The pages, the search records and the idea route expose the\n  6518\t  edge's meaning; the direction label is a blocker for a seeded build.\n  6519\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the separation stays a candidate. Continue its design at $0: the duplicate and old-row contracts,\n  6520\t  the D265 and D207 reading with its residual double filing stated, the reader and state tables completed, and a next proof\n  6521\t  that exercises both edge combinations and at least one real writer-and-reader path on a scratch store. Stop and return the\n  6522\t  conflict if the one-home requirement cannot be expressed without an unsupported new rule, or if the meaning of historical\n  6523\t  edges cannot be established. The selection call is not designed yet. No send; no frozen piece changed.\n  6524\t\n  6525\t## D540 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the separation stays a provisional research candidate; the filing and duplicate-label contracts are finished at $0 before any selection design or send (council consensus, reflection round 31)\n  6526\t\n  6527\t- **Reviewed:** the revised design and the second proof (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md`,\n  6528\t  `separation_proof_2.py`): the production seeding and writer steps, wrapped, store the kind of the edges they write; with the\n  6529\t  data-center revenue question's stored answers handed back, the whole unseeded fresh week keeps its stored filings and every\n  6530\t  other judgement while that question's seven requests gain total revenue's conclusion of the same round.\n  6531\t- **The council's findings:** not applying D265's narrowest rule to a chosen dependency is a reasonable provisional\n  6532\t  interpretation under D439, not a finished product rule and not an implementation of D207 and D360. A double link is not\n  6533\t  necessarily a reading error (D360 stores a two-figure sentence as one record linked to both questions); \"60 of 385\" sizes such\n  6534\t  records, not breaches. The second proof does not give the requests a live judge would produce: a real test runs each arm as a\n  6535\t  sequence from its own earlier answers. Two contracts still blocked calling the candidate sound: a proposed edge with the same\n  6536\t  reading pair and another direction label must not be discarded as a duplicate; and the inventory's claim must be bounded to\n  6537\t  the files and marks it read.\n  6538\t- **Decided, citing D439:** no judge call is sent. Finish at $0 the filing and duplicate-label contract: the seven observed\n  6539\t  statements, a single-figure driver-and-root case, a two-figure sentence and an unrelated pair, with the expected homes and the\n  6540\t  owner of each decision stated and no case-specific list in code; conflicting labels and unknown historical rows exercised.\n  6541\t  Stop and return to the council if the correct homes cannot be expressed under the existing decisions, or if resolving a label\n  6542\t  would require inventing its meaning.\n  6543\t\n  6544\t## D541 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the seed edge's label stops everything that touches a seed edge; the filing finding is bounded; the unseeded failure-and-reader contract is finished at $0 before the separation is called sound (council consensus, reflection round 32)\n  6545\t\n  6546\t- **Reviewed** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` sections 2.2, 2.3, 2.5;\n  6547\t  `filing_contract.py`; `separation_proof_2.py`, 20 registered expectations): ten filing cases run through the code's own rule\n  6548\t  (in every real case the reading step linked the statement to both questions; with no stated hierarchy five come out as the\n  6549\t  decisions call for, with one a different five); the outcomes for a second edge over an existing reading (the same label: not\n  6550\t  written; another label: a conflict, refused; over a seed edge: not comparable); the inventory bounded to 158 files and to\n  6551\t  marks.\n  6552\t- **The council's findings:** the seed-label stop has fired: `last_end`, written as a constant by the seeding module, is\n  6553\t  defined in no decision, page, seed file or prompt, and is given no meaning from its spelling; the stop covers the seeded\n  6554\t  reading and any comparison against a seed edge, not a separately bounded unseeded design. The filing stop has not fired: the\n  6555\t  expected homes are expressible under the existing decisions and not produced by an edge rule; the table is a hand reading of\n  6556\t  ten cases, and whether the company-wide outlook also bears on the segment stays open to review. Three gaps kept the unseeded\n  6557\t  contract from being called sound: a conflict seen only by the proof's helper, not by the production path, and a cycle\n  6558\t  described as a dropped note where PRD 06 says refuse and ask for a correction; old unseeded rows not shown through the\n  6559\t  service, search, bundle and idea readers; the everyday boundaries (a target closing or succeeded, an awaited target, a\n  6560\t  duplicate or conflict across articles, a theme already in the theme block).\n  6561\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the separation stays provisional. Finish the unseeded state-by-event and reader contracts at $0 and\n  6562\t  exercise the actual writer and readers on scratch stores, failure and resume included, a conflict observable; stop and record\n  6563\t  the conflict if the existing decisions do not determine a transition or a historical meaning. The seed-label question stays\n  6564\t  separate and unresolved. No selection-call design, no send.\n  6565\t\n  6566\t## D542 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency stretch is closed with the separation recorded as a provisional candidate; the status is consolidated; nothing is sent (council consensus, reflection round 33)\n  6567\t\n  6568\t- **Done at $0 after D541** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` section 2.6): the\n  6569\t  package's own 287 tests run with the separated reading installed (`seam_plugin.py`): 285 pass as they are; the two others\n  6570\t  write by hand a row neither writer produces (one, the resume test, passes once its row is restated as a chosen dependency;\n  6571\t  the other holds D265 in its literal reading). In the 28 stored ledgers that hold only matching-era rows, the service shows\n  6572\t  what the candidate reads for all 399 questions with an edge (read at one far date). Three places where decisions and code\n  6573\t  part or the decisions are silent: an edge that would close a circle is dropped with a note where PRD 06 says refuse and ask\n  6574\t  for a correction; \"historical only\" has a reader and no writer; no decision says what happens to a later proposal with\n  6575\t  another direction for a pair already read.\n  6576\t- **The council's corrections:** a circle with stored work can arise at creation through an awaited question (`resolve_waiting`\n  6577\t  checks it and leaves the edge unbound); the census does hold theme-to-theme pairs both readers grant, so \"no pair names a\n  6578\t  theme\" was too broad. The suite under the seam is compatibility evidence, not a proof of every event.\n  6579\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the dependency stretch (D533 to D542) is closed. The separation is a provisional candidate, not\n  6580\t  sound for build; if the slice is reopened its review must settle the cycle through an awaited question at creation, closing\n  6581\t  behaviour, a theme shown twice, the historical readers and the label's meaning before any build. No selection call is\n  6582\t  designed and nothing is sent. Claude's proposed general rule (\"a contract that depends on an unbuilt piece is written only\n  6583\t  when that piece opens\") is **not** adopted: some such contracts decide whether the pieces can coexist, as the filing and\n  6584\t  reading conflict did; AGENTS §2 still requires the contracts complete before code. The next task is the consolidation of the\n  6585\t  status and the decision record (one next-task statement; production the default and both systems kept; D375 and D368 decided\n  6586\t  and awaiting implementation and acceptance). No open investigation outranks that closure on the choice between the systems;\n  6587\t  a new step worth a decision returns to the council under D439.\n  6588\t\n 10360\t## D690 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product, the research line rests until his new direction; the D681–D689 records are committed locally\n 10361\t\n 10362\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-20), replying to the two items put to him after D689: \"1. OK 2. A\". Item 1 was a local commit of the\n 10363\t  D681–D689 records, not pushed. Item 2's options were:\n 10364\t  - **A**, recommended: poc-v118 is the product, and the research line rests until his new direction;\n 10365\t  - **B**, change the rules that bind the hybrid's lead: whether the library tracks other companies' own figures (5 matters, D688),\n 10366\t    and whether the judge carries its previous conclusion (D198). \"One bet, one question\" (D248) was not offered for change, because\n 10367\t    the comparison's list is finer than it;\n 10368\t  - **C**, new test questions from another company or a later NVIDIA window, at a price he would set.\n 10369\t- **Decided (Alex):** A. No improvement line on the hybrid, the judge, c8 or opening is open, and no paid send is open. The reopening\n 10370\t  conditions of D689 stand. B and C are not taken.\n 10371\t- **Done:** the D681–D690 records are committed on `clean-arch`, and nothing is pushed.\n 10372\t- **Asked next by Alex, in the same message:** a description of the end-to-end system (its components, how it runs, its current\n 10373\t  performance) and whether it is ready to go to production for testing. That answer is an assessment, recorded when it is given.\n 10374\t\n 10375\t## D691 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A after council Q: no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents\n 10376\t\n 10377\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-20): on the half-hour read of poc-v118's 09-20 output, \"dont' you take a look for me let the council tak\n 10378\t  ea crack at it\"; on the three options put to him after council Q, \"A\".\n 10379\t- **Council Q** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-q/RESULT.md`, consensus, $0): an analyst would use the\n 10380\t  library PARTLY: for sources and milestones, not for its number answers, because linked number questions contradict each other\n 10381\t  in all three draws (old-2: Data Center Q4 about $146B against a total Q4 of about $127B); no question has a dependency and no\n 10382\t  judgement cites another question.\n 10383\t- **The options were:**\n 10384\t  - **A**, recommended: no daily wrapper yet; link the related questions first, tested at $0 on the request text, then a few cents;\n 10385\t  - **B**, build the daily wrapper and tell testers the number questions do not yet agree;\n 10386\t  - **C**, stop here.\n 10387\t- **Decided (Alex):** A. B and C are not taken. Council P's daily wrapper and rehearsal week wait.\n 10388\t- **A correction of mine, made to Alex:** council Q called the dependencies \"decided (D368 item 2) and not built\". The dependency\n 10389\t  stretch D533–D542 had already worked on them and closed with the `reads`/`supports` separation as a provisional candidate, not\n 10390\t  sound for build (D542). A probe is not a build: it tests whether linking reconciles the answers before that design is reopened.\n 10391\t  The census of that stretch (D537) found the useful pair to be Data Center revenue reading total revenue.\n 10392\t- **Done ($0):** `dependency-probe/render_check.py` (the block production renders, cut at 600 characters, shows the total's decisive\n 10393\t  figures in old-2, its FY figure but no Q4 in old-1, and cuts old-3's final figure while showing its band) and `probe.py check`\n 10394\t  (each draw's scratch copy, rolled back to before the Data Center question's 09-20 judgement, rebuilds the stored request byte-equal\n 10395\t  in all three draws; the changed request adds 682–764 characters).\n 10396\t- **Next:** council round 3 on the probe's design (`dependency-probe/design.md`), then the send (18 requests, cap $0.40) on consensus.\n 10397\t\n 10398\t## D692 · 2026-11-20 · Under Alex's A (D691): the dependency probe passes its registered rule; the dependency design review reopens at $0\n 10399\t\n 10400\t- **Source of authority:** Alex's \"A\" (D691: link the related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents). The probe's design passed\n 10401\t  the council in rounds 3–6 (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/`, Codex thread `01a1fba6…`; rounds 3–5\n 10402\t  DISAGREE with changes, all taken: old-2 only, a stricter reading rule with Q3 and room for the rest of NVIDIA, one transport attempt,\n 10403\t  reservations charged when usage is unknown; round 6 CONSENSUS).\n 10404\t- **Result** (`dependency-probe/RESULT.md`, $0.0176): with v14's conclusion linked, 2 of 3 answers reconcile (Q4 Data Center sized\n 10405\t  from v14's $127B and the reported mix); the unchanged request reconciles 0 of 3. Claude's marks and a fresh blind Codex reader agree\n 10406\t  on every answer. PASS by the rule as written. Round 7 (CONSENSUS) on the result.\n 10407\t- **Disclosed with it:** none of the six answers repeats the stored extreme (rung 2, Q4 $146B): council Q's headline example was\n 10408\t  partly one unlucky sample; the recurring contradiction is milder. Coherence is not accuracy. Five of six answers still carry the\n 10409\t  self-made $414B reference.\n 10410\t- **Decided (council consensus under D691):** council Q's PARTLY and the deferral of the daily wrapper stand. The dependency design\n 10411\t  review reopens at $0 (D542's five open items, the `reads`/`supports` separation, D538's seven filing changes), then goes to Alex\n 10412\t  before any build or send. The self-made reference is traced apart on stored answers, at $0.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '40,235p'\nnl -ba poc/config/poc-v118.json\nnl -ba tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py\nnl -ba tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '40,235p'\nnl -ba poc/config/poc-v118.json\nnl -ba tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py\nnl -ba tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py\"","aggregated_output":"    40\t│       └─ Succession → The previous period's thesis (Successive periods of the same focus form a chain)\n    41\t├─ Research group → Organise theses by a continuing business process (Associate during extraction; full rules are in “Research groups: associate during extraction”)\n    42\t└─ Append-only records → Matching, rejudgement, succession, closure, reopening and labelling records (Append at every step, without editing or deleting. Read records up to a historical date to recover its judgement.)\n    43\t```\n    44\t<!-- /generated: structure -->\n    45\t\n    46\t## Two thesis kinds\n    47\t\n    48\t<!-- generated: kinds -->\n    49\t| Kind | Subject kind | Ladder rungs | Example |\n    50\t|---|---|---|---|\n    51\t| Asset thesis | Tradable subjects: companies, cryptocurrencies and commodities | Five rungs: strongly bullish, bullish, neutral, bearish, strongly bearish. Two for yes/no: bullish and bearish. These describe the business impact; set them at creation and keep them fixed. | How will NVDA FY2027 China revenue compare with FY2026? |\n    52\t| Theme thesis | Macro, policy and industry themes | Ordered outcomes from one end to the other: five rungs, or two for yes/no. Name outcomes without judging them good or bad. Dependent asset theses specify which outcome benefits them. | How will the Fed's target-rate upper bound after its last 2026 meeting compare with now? (Large cut … large hike) |\n    53\t\n    54\tThe same event can affect assets differently: rate cuts can be bullish for Ethereum and bearish for JPM net interest income. Theme theses therefore do not label outcomes good or bad.\n    55\t<!-- /generated: kinds -->\n    56\t\n    57\t## Ladder\n    58\t\n    59\t<!-- generated: ladder -->\n    60\t```\n    61\tTwo kinds of ladder (Illustrative ranges)\n    62\t├─ Asset thesis: numeric → NVDA FY2027 China revenue versus FY2026 | Five rungs describing NVDA's business impact (Due on the FY2027 annual earnings date)\n    63\t│   ├─ Strongly bullish → Up at least 50%\n    64\t│   ├─ Bullish → Up at least 10% but under 50%\n    65\t│   ├─ Neutral → Up or down by less than 10%\n    66\t│   ├─ Bearish → Down at least 10% but under 80%\n    67\t│   └─ Strongly bearish → Down at least 80% (At most one fifth remains)\n    68\t└─ Theme thesis: event → China export licensing for chips covered by the April 2025 rule, including H20 and MI308, as of April 15, 2026 | Five ordered outcomes, without good/bad labels (Use the rules in force on that date)\n    69\t    ├─ Rung 1 → Full ban; licence applications no longer accepted\n    70\t    ├─ Rung 2 → Licences required; none issued\n    71\t    ├─ Rung 3 → Licences required and issued; some conditional\n    72\t    ├─ Rung 4 → Licences required and issued; all unconditional\n    73\t    └─ Rung 5 → Licences no longer required\n    74\t```\n    75\t\n    76\t1. A ladder has five rungs. Asset theses run from strongly bullish to strongly bearish, describing business impact; theme theses name five ordered outcomes without good/bad labels. Use two rungs for yes/no rather than forcing five: bullish/bearish for assets; named outcomes for themes, such as signed by the deadline/not signed. Decided for the next extraction version (D186, D368): asset rungs state the business outcome against guidance (above, near, below) and each thesis names its favourable end.\n    77\t2. Each rung is verifiable: a numeric interval or event stage. Rungs must be exhaustive and non-overlapping, so exactly one applies at expiry. For example: up at least 50%; up 10% to under 50%; change under 10% either way; down 10% to under 80%; down at least 80%. Every boundary belongs to one rung. “Up a lot/a little” cannot be checked. Avoid vague partial outcomes; specify the partial state, such as conditional licences, as a distinct rung. State the comparison underlying neutral.\n    78\t3. One ladder concerns one thing. Separate numeric and event questions and connect them with dependencies. Likewise, separate components that can move in opposite directions, such as H20 and Blackwell chip classes.\n    79\t4. The extraction model writes the candidate's ladder. A new thesis adopts it unchanged until expiry. A merged candidate uses the existing thesis's ladder and due date.\n    80\t5. Numeric theses name a year. Non-company quantities use calendar years: the publication year is this year and the following year is next year, each ending December 31. Company quantities use the fiscal year containing publication day and its successor. Never use the computer clock. For a given quantity, open at most one thesis for each of this year and next year; do not open later years. The due date is the quantity's publication date.\n    81\t6. Set the due date when the debate can be resolved, usually 6–12 months away. Intermediate quarterly reports are evidence, not separate theses.\n    82\t<!-- /generated: ladder -->\n    83\t\n    84\t## State\n    85\t\n    86\t<!-- generated: positions -->\n    87\t|  | Meaning | Decision maker | Example |\n    88\t|---|---|---|---|\n    89\t| State | Our judgement of the thesis's current rung; evidence pushes toward either end | The model judges the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, against a reference (below). It reads the evidence in view, the arrivals since its fifth most recent judgement and the basis its last ten judgements cited, the request naming how many more pieces stay in force (D198); a revision is shown beside the piece it revises and a repeat beside the piece the matcher read it as, both in force (D202, D204); plus current dependency states and reasons and, for an asset thesis, the theme block. Do not increment or decrement the previous score. Cite evidence and compare with the conclusion before this round to state whether it changed. Do not rejudge if only source references were added and dependency conclusions did not change. | After the 8-K: strongly bearish |\n    90\t\n    91\t- Every judgement states its basis in a fixed response shape: evidence IDs such as e12 and e15, plus dependency thesis IDs such as #1 when their changes triggered rejudgement.\n    92\t- Code checks cited IDs against the request that was sent: evidence must be among the pieces shown to this thesis (D198); cited theses must be its dependencies. Accept only if all checks pass. Otherwise record the reason and ask for one corrected judgement. If that also fails, use normal failure handling: retry from this step, then human review after repeated failure. This checks references, not whether the judgement is correct, like verifying a cited page exists.\n    93\t- Each judgement also declares whether the conclusion changed and explains why, comparing with the state and reasons before this round, including during retries. That earlier conclusion is for comparison, not incremental scoring. A rung change or a material change in the supporting facts/numbers counts: AMZN capex guidance moving from 12% to 25% growth changes the conclusion even within one rung. Repetition does not. A changed conclusion triggers dependent theses in the same round. Code requires changed=true for a first judgement or rung change; otherwise refuse under the same correction rules.\n    94\t- For historical judgement, read the records saved on that date. Do not ask the model again; a new sample can differ.\n    95\t- The rung is a forecast against a reference (D260): the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, judged against what the market expects (consensus, guidance, the stated plan or deadline). The judgement names the reference and its rung and the outcome the evidence implies (a figure or date derived from reported figures, guidance and quantified revisions), and moves when the implied outcome crosses a rung boundary. A consensus figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and is not the reason to stay once other evidence has arrived; \"not established\" is confidence, not a reason to stay. From judging-v6 the reference and the implied outcome are required fields of the answer, stored beside the rung; an empty one is refused.\n    96\t<!-- /generated: positions -->\n    97\t\n    98\t## Four evidence tiers\n    99\t\n   100\t<!-- generated: tiers -->\n   101\t| Tier | Example | Role |\n   102\t|---|---|---|\n   103\t| Fact | Official actions, published figures and completed transactions | Fixes what is known; the forecast starts from it |\n   104\t| Party statement | Company guidance, management statements and official speeches | The strongest input to the forecast |\n   105\t| Third-party view | Sell-side analysts, media analysis and experts | Moves the forecast in proportion to its specificity |\n   106\t| Rumour | Unnamed-source claims and unattributed statements | Moves the forecast in proportion to its specificity |\n   107\t\n   108\t- The model determines the size of the push and gives reasons, by tier and novelty: a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing (D260). No tier has a fixed score.\n   109\t- Count independent original sources. Twenty outlets retelling one exclusive are twenty pieces, each related to the one it repeats (D204), and one source, not twenty independent confirmations (D30).\n   110\t- Tier follows who confirmed it. An unnamed-source report that Commerce is issuing licences is a rumour. An official or company confirmation is factual evidence recorded as a revision of it, both in force (D202). The rumour stays a rumour.\n   111\t- Store evidence once without an intrinsic direction. Each rejudgement writes its push on the evidence–thesis link. One statement can affect multiple theses differently.\n   112\t<!-- /generated: tiers -->\n   113\t\n   114\t## Dependencies: reading the arrows\n   115\t\n   116\t<!-- generated: dependencies -->\n   117\t```\n   118\tB depends on A | What kind of thesis is A? (For an asset thesis B, state which end of A is bullish for B. For a theme thesis B, state whether their ladders have the same or opposite orientation.)\n   119\t├─ Numeric thesis → Read the specified year's thesis (Example: JPM 2027 net interest income → Fed year-end 2027 rate)\n   120\t│   ├─ A is open → Read A's state and reasons\n   121\t│   ├─ A is closed → Read A's closing state and reasons (The frozen outcome is what B needs; keep reading it)\n   122\t│   └─ A does not exist yet → Wait for it (Record the awaited year on the chain containing the shown thesis. When that year's successor is created, bind the dependency and rejudge B once.)\n   123\t└─ Event thesis → Follow succession (Example: NVDA FY2027 China revenue → chip export licensing to China)\n   124\t    ├─ A is open → Read A's state and reasons\n   125\t    ├─ A is closed with a successor → Read the successor (Record the change. The successor changes B's input, so rejudge B once.)\n   126\t    └─ A is closed without a successor → Read A's closing state and reasons, marked “historical only”\n   127\t```\n   128\t\n   129\t- Theme theses do not judge outcomes as good or bad. Each dependent asset thesis records its direction: rate cuts are bullish for Ethereum and bearish for JPM.\n   130\t- A dependency has one direction. An apparent “good first, bad later” relationship needs an intermediate thesis: steel tariffs raising domestic steel prices and weakening downstream steel demand are separate paths.\n   131\t- Dependencies and the theme block are the two ways theses influence each other; succession only orders periods. B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion. The theme block (D191, D195) shows every open, judged theme thesis to every asset thesis's judgement, one to all, and the judgement states which way each theme it weighed pushes it; no edge is written for it. Keep B's direct evidence separate from dependency states and reasons. A's conclusion can affect B like evidence but is not stored as evidence: external events and statements are evidence, whereas A is our own judgement. Treating it as evidence would let the system convince itself.\n   132\t- Count a statement once. A statement about A is A's evidence, including when two candidates arise from one item. B learns it through A's conclusion. Daily filing gives a statement one home: the narrowest open thesis it bears on, as that thesis's own figure, step or estimate or through the demand, supply, competition or pricing behind its answer, plus the same answer's candidates (D207, D259, D264, D265); the separate coverage-start reading was retired (D370). Dependencies are chosen only when B is created; a later item adding a dependency to an existing thesis is decided (D191 point 2) and to be built (D368).\n   133\t- Rejudge an open thesis when its inputs change: new evidence, replacement, a new link to existing evidence, a dependency declaring a changed conclusion, or (for an asset thesis) a theme thesis declaring one. Additional source references alone do not count. Binding an awaited A or moving to its successor also changes B's inputs. Closed theses do not update. A memo-derived thesis is first judged when evidence first links to it; before that, it and its dependants see “not yet judged”.\n   134\t- The matching call chooses a new thesis's dependencies, stating which conclusions it relies on and each direction (D51). Choose only among searched theses, extraction block-5 theses and candidates opened from the same item; no extra search. Jev, the default matcher, is not asked for them, so new theses do not receive dependencies through the default matcher; building the choice on the Jev path is decided (D368). The historical seed questions are retired (D370). A historical seed's dependency arrow means \"supports\" (D368, by D208): for filing, the supporting (driver) thesis is the narrower one; for judging, the supported (root) thesis reads the supporting theses' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged before their roots. The judging code reads the stored edge the other way today; the fix is to be built and measured (D368). Completed events are evidence, not dependencies: today's oil price influencing OPEC output is evidence for the OPEC-output thesis.\n   135\t- Before adding an edge or following it to a successor, code checks for cycles. Refuse a cycle and ask the model to correct it; persistent cycles follow normal failure handling. Apparently mutually dependent questions indicate poorly defined theses.\n   136\t<!-- /generated: dependencies -->\n   137\t\n   138\t## Succession: the same focus over successive periods\n   139\t\n   140\t<!-- generated: chain -->\n   141\t- Successive periods of the same focus form a chain, such as Fed year-end 2026 rate → 2027 rate → 2028 rate. The chain records period order. Dependency traversal follows the rules above.\n   142\t- One thesis has at most one successor: FY2026 cannot produce two FY2027 successors.\n   143\t- Keep ladder orientation across succession: a strongly bullish first rung remains strongly bullish, although thresholds can change. Dependencies retain their direction; reversing the ends would break it.\n   144\t<!-- /generated: chain -->\n   145\t\n   146\t## Intake: search then compare\n   147\t\n   148\t<!-- generated: shape -->\n   149\t|  | Candidate thesis | Evidence |\n   150\t|---|---|---|\n   151\t| Comparison set | Top N search results from the entire thesis library | Top N evidence results within its thesis |\n   152\t| Decision | Existing identity or part, succession, new thesis or skip | Repeat, replace or new evidence |\n   153\t| Chain | Succession: Fed year-end 2026 rate → 2027 → 2028 | Revision: AMZN capex guidance 12% growth → 25%, both in force |\n   154\t| What counts as current | Open theses on the chain; numeric theses may have one for this year and one for next year | Every stored piece stays in force; revisions form a chain the judge reads (D202) |\n   155\t| Search scope | Entire thesis library, open and closed | Only evidence within its thesis, not the entire library |\n   156\t<!-- /generated: shape -->\n   157\t\n   158\t## One item entering the library\n   159\t\n   160\tProcess items one at a time in sequence order through steps 1–6; step 7, the rejudgement round, runs once a day after the day's last item (D63). Candidates arrive with associations and necessary group definitions, preserved under the grouping rules. Models perform steps 4 (Jev and the collision judge) and 7; code performs the others.\n   161\t\n   162\t<!-- generated: intake -->\n   163\t```\n   164\tEvidence and candidates from extraction, written item by item; one judging round a day (D63)\n   165\t  ↓ 1 Check sources (Code): Reject sources absent from processing records and record the reason\n   166\t  ↓ 2 Receive evidence (Code): Retries do not duplicate evidence. A revised input updates only its own source reference. A revised retelling does not alter the original evidence. If the revision is from the original source, compare its statements normally: a changed statement is stored as a revision of the old one, both in force (D202).\n   167\t  ↓ 3 Search (Code): Use a search engine such as Elasticsearch; semantic versus keyword search remains open. Search all open and closed theses for each candidate and take top N, initially 10 in Config. Search evidence only within its linked thesis, also top N. Evidence linked to candidates waits for their destinations, even if also linked to existing theses. Empty lists still proceed to matching.\n   168\t  ↓ 4 Match (Model): The matcher does not read the original item. Jev answers, with a score, each candidate's relation to every thesis on its list (shown with its subject, question, focus, ladder, due date and open/closed state) and each piece of evidence's relation to every stored piece on its list under each linked thesis; code turns the answers into the destinations below and owns identity on typed keys (D155, D169, D197). When a candidate's list holds a thesis of its own subject and measure, the collision judge, one generative call, answers the analyst's question for those theses under D248's test, and its verdict replaces Jev's (D190, D258). Jev is not asked for dependencies. Evidence linked to candidates waits for their destinations, then searches all linked existing theses together and is compared once more. Evidence linked only to new theses is new evidence.\n   169\t  ↓ 5 Validate (Code): Destination IDs must be in the shown lists or the relevant thesis's evidence. Merge only into open theses. New subjects must resolve within the universe using classification's identifier rules; otherwise skip. Dependencies must reference shown theses or an explicit awaited chain/year and remain acyclic. Return invalid answers for correction.\n   170\t  ↓ 6 Write to the library (Code): Resolve extraction's group associations to final theses and save them in this step. Each subject has its own writing queue; write theme theses before asset theses. Save new theses with their dependency edges. Store every incoming piece once, as its own record with all its links (D204): a repeat also records the pair as the same claim; a replacement is linked wherever the piece it revises is linked and the pair is recorded as a revision, ordered by when each statement was made, both in force (D202); an older statement arriving later is stored and linked as one more piece, with no revision recorded. The writer retires nothing. If compared data changes before writing, repeat matching only for the affected part.\n   171\t  ↓ 7 Run the day's rejudgement round (Model): Once a day, after the day's last item (D63), rejudge only open theses whose inputs changed that day: new or newly linked evidence (a repeat or a revision is a new piece), or a changed dependency conclusion, newly created awaited thesis or successor. Judge dependencies first, then theme theses before asset theses, and each thesis once per round; each judgement reads the evidence in view (D198). Extra source references alone do not trigger it. Memo-derived theses without evidence stay not yet judged. Each judgement declares whether its conclusion changed; changed conclusions propagate to dependants, and a theme's to every open asset thesis (D195). The round's queue is read from the ledger, so a resumed round recovers what an earlier commit queued.\n   172\t```\n   173\t<!-- /generated: intake -->\n   174\t\n   175\t## Step 4: candidate destinations\n   176\t\n   177\t<!-- generated: outcomes -->\n   178\t| Destination | When | Writes |\n   179\t|---|---|---|\n   180\t| Merge into existing | The candidate concerns the same focus or a part of it, such as H20 China revenue within China revenue. Merge only into open theses; closed theses can only be succeeded. | Compare its evidence within the target thesis and preserve grouping under this section's rules. Use the existing ladder and due date. |\n   181\t| Succession | The next period of the same focus: the next year for numbers, or continued tracking after an event thesis closed | Create a thesis and record succession |\n   182\t| New thesis | Distinct or merely similar: Blackwell export licences and H20 export licences are different questions | Create a thesis with its ladder and due date fixed from now on |\n   183\t| Skip | Too broad or mixed, bundling questions that can move oppositely, such as all US chip controls on China; numbers beyond this/next year; the same focus and period as a closed thesis; or an out-of-universe subject. Proposed themes go to human review; out-of-universe companies receive only a processing-log entry. | Do not create it. Evidence also linked to a specific valid thesis still counts; evidence linked only to the skipped candidate is not stored. |\n   184\t\n   185\t- The D155 POC uses code for fully determined duplicate identity and model comparison when scope or legacy identity needs judgement. A shared quantity (an aggregate opened under its admission reason) is one thesis per theme, measure and period: its population or wording is not identity, so code merges another wording into the open one and succeeds it for the next period (D197). Reference lists guide research without vetoing candidates. Same group does not mean same thesis. See docs/poc/grouping-improvement-plan.md for the contract and measured scope.\n   186\t- Search finds plausible candidates; the model handles semantic comparison. H20 and Blackwell export licences can look similar but are separate questions. Bullish and bearish accounts of one question share its identity.\n   187\t- Search includes closed theses, allowing an FY2027 candidate to find closed FY2026 and be classified as succession.\n   188\t<!-- /generated: outcomes -->\n   189\t\n   190\t## Step 4: evidence destinations\n   191\t\n   192\t<!-- generated: evidence-outcomes -->\n   193\t| Destination | When | Writes |\n   194\t|---|---|---|\n   195\t| Repeat | The same evidence already exists under the thesis from another input: a retelling, or the same speaker repeating the same statement (within one input, the same number in text and table is one piece with several quotes) | Store it as its own piece with its own source and links, and record the pair as the same claim (D204). The judge sees the pair labelled as the matcher's opinion and counts one claim; its links queue their theses for the day's round. |\n   196\t| Replace | A later account of the same matter: a speaker revises guidance, forecast or event progress; an official confirms/denies a rumour; or the original source revises its statement | Store the later statement beside the earlier one and record the pair as a revision, ordered by statement date; both stay in force (D202); rejudge. A late-arriving older statement is stored and linked as one more piece, with no revision recorded. |\n   197\t| New evidence | Anything else: a new event, another period's figure or another speaker's statement, including disagreement. Uncertainty also means new evidence. | Add it alongside existing evidence and rejudge |\n   198\t\n   199\t- First resolve the evidence's thesis destination from extraction or candidate matching. Search the top N evidence items still in force within that thesis and ask the model to compare. Unlike candidate-thesis search, evidence search never spans the whole library.\n   200\t- Store evidence once even when linked to several theses. Compare all those theses' evidence together. If any link is to a candidate, wait for that candidate's destination.\n   201\t- A revision is linked wherever the piece it revises is linked, and those open theses are rejudged, so each sees the change (D202).\n   202\t- Replacement applies to a statement or number, not the whole report. A revised sell-side revenue forecast is recorded as a revision of that forecast; both stay in force, as do the report's other arguments.\n   203\t- Matching reads the evidence summary, speaker, original source and statement date, not the full original item. When uncertain, treat it as new evidence; both then remain available for judgement.\n   204\t<!-- /generated: evidence-outcomes -->\n   205\t\n   206\t## Example: three items\n   207\t\n   208\t<!-- generated: intake-example -->\n   209\t```\n   210\tThree items, starting with an empty library (Illustration)\n   211\t├─ NVIDIA 8-K, April 15, 2025 → Empty library; two candidates arrive | Empty comparison lists; open both as new theses\n   212\t│   ├─ #1 Theme thesis → China export licensing for this chip class: event (Evidence: H20 exports to China require a licence (fact))\n   213\t│   └─ #2 NVDA asset thesis → FY2026 China revenue: numeric (Evidence: expected charges up to approximately $5.5 billion (party statement); the licence theme #1 reaches it through the theme block (an explicit dependency, easing bullish, would be chosen in matching, D51, not yet on the default Jev path))\n   214\t├─ AMD 8-K, April 16, 2025 → AMD has no existing theses; two candidates arrive | Match\n   215\t│   ├─ Candidate: MI308 export licensing to China → Merge into #1 (Search finds #1. The model identifies the same question: the same chip class under the same rule. AMD's MI308 statement is new evidence. #1 is rejudged in that day's round but declares its conclusion unchanged: an additional affected model does not change the key facts or rung. #1 therefore queues no rejudgement of #2.)\n   216\t│   └─ Candidate: AMD 2025 China revenue → New thesis #3 (AMD has no open thesis; evidence is expected charges up to approximately $800 million (party statement))\n   217\t└─ Reuters, April 16, 2025, retelling NVIDIA's 8-K → Existing context: #2 and the licence theme #1 | Match\n   218\t    └─ Evidence links to #1 and #2 → Both are repeats (The original source is the same NVIDIA 8-K and both statements already exist under #1 and #2. Each retelling is stored as its own piece under its thesis, with the pair recorded as the same claim (D204). Both theses are rejudged in that day's round, #2 for this piece alone; the judge counts one claim, so neither conclusion changes.)\n   219\t```\n   220\t<!-- /generated: intake-example -->\n   221\t\n   222\t## Example: AMZN 2026 capex evidence updates\n   223\t\n   224\t<!-- generated: evidence-example -->\n   225\t| Item | Evidence comparison | Library result | Rejudgement |\n   226\t|---|---|---|---|\n   227\t| February 5 call: capex guidance up 12% | New evidence; none previously under this thesis | Add g1 | Rejudge |\n   228\t| February 6 Reuters report retells the guidance | Repeat of g1 | Add r1, recorded as the same claim as g1 | Rejudge; one claim, conclusion unchanged |\n   229\t| March 10 Morgan Stanley forecast: up 18% | New evidence from another speaker | Add m1 | Rejudge |\n   230\t| April 30 call: guidance revised to 25% growth | Replace g1 | Add g2 beside g1, both in force; the revision g1 → g2 is recorded | Rejudge, reading “12% → 25%” |\n   231\t| May 2 Morgan Stanley forecast revised to 27% | Replace m1 | Add m2 beside m1, both in force; the revision m1 → m2 is recorded | Rejudge |\n   232\t| Arrives May 20: Morgan Stanley's February forecast | Late older statement; Morgan Stanley already revised it in March (m1) and May (m2) | Add m0 as one more piece with its February date; no revision is recorded and the late-statement log keeps a row | Rejudge; m2 is still the latest forecast, so the conclusion stays |\n   233\t| June 10 meeting reiterates “still around 25%” | Repeat of g2 | Add j1, recorded as the same claim as g2 | Rejudge; one claim, conclusion unchanged |\n   234\t\n   235\tAfter six months the thesis may have dozens of evidence items, all in force. A rejudgement reads those in view, the arrivals since its fifth most recent judgement and the basis its last ten judgements cited (D198), each revision beside the piece it revises: company guidance of 25% growth revising February's 12%, Morgan Stanley's 27% forecast revising March's 18%, plus other speakers and events.\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"version\": \"poc-v118\",\n     3\t  \"_note\": \"Field-free configuration derived from poc-v117.json; all active model and prompt settings remain unchanged.\",\n     4\t  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n     5\t  \"search_top_n\": 10,\n     6\t  \"extraction\": {\n     7\t    \"T1\": {\n     8\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n     9\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T1-v74i\",\n    10\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    11\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    12\t    },\n    13\t    \"T2\": {\n    14\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    15\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T2-v74i\",\n    16\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    17\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    18\t    },\n    19\t    \"T3\": {\n    20\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    21\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T3-v74i\",\n    22\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    23\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    24\t    },\n    25\t    \"T4\": {\n    26\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    27\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T4-v74i\",\n    28\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    29\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    30\t    },\n    31\t    \"T5\": {\n    32\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    33\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T5-v74i\",\n    34\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    35\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    36\t    },\n    37\t    \"T6\": {\n    38\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    39\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T6-v74i\",\n    40\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    41\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    42\t    },\n    43\t    \"T7\": {\n    44\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    45\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T7-v74i\",\n    46\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    47\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    48\t    },\n    49\t    \"T8\": {\n    50\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    51\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T8-v74i\",\n    52\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    53\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    54\t    },\n    55\t    \"T10\": {\n    56\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    57\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T10-v74i\",\n    58\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    59\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    60\t    },\n    61\t    \"T11\": {\n    62\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    63\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T11-v74i\",\n    64\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    65\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    66\t    }\n    67\t  },\n    68\t  \"matching\": {\n    69\t    \"model\": \"jev-1.14.0\",\n    70\t    \"prompt_version\": \"matching-v3\",\n    71\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    72\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 12000,\n    73\t    \"engine\": \"jev\"\n    74\t  },\n    75\t  \"rejudging\": {\n    76\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    77\t    \"prompt_version\": \"judging-v7\",\n    78\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    79\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    80\t  },\n    81\t  \"final_verdict\": {\n    82\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    83\t    \"prompt_version\": \"verdict-v0\",\n    84\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    85\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    86\t  },\n    87\t  \"idea\": {\n    88\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    89\t    \"prompt_version\": \"idea-v11\",\n    90\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"none\",\n    91\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n    92\t  },\n    93\t  \"collision\": {\n    94\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    95\t    \"prompt_version\": \"collision-v2\",\n    96\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    97\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n    98\t  }\n    99\t}\n     1\t\"\"\"Steps 3 and 4 are frozen (D354, Alex 2026-11-03: \"那你跑了吧，我们赶紧确认step 3,4 可以freeze\"): opening and matching questions, and\n     2\tjudging them, as `poc/config/poc-v108.json` runs them (its sha256 is pinned in test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py). Every piece that shapes\n     3\tthose requests is pinned here: the collision judge's and the judge's prompt files, the matching prompt the configuration names, the\n     4\tjudge's answer schema, and the three questions the Jev matcher is asked. A change is a new version opened only by Alex's decision.\"\"\"\n     5\timport hashlib\n     6\timport json\n     7\timport os\n     8\timport sys\n     9\t\n    10\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n    11\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\n    12\tfrom hivemind.views import jev_matching, judging  # noqa: E402\n    13\t\n    14\tFROZEN_FILES = {\n    15\t    'src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v2.txt': 'a5f0f58d53c4f4215b14e534935b1f95a79b35ba097d68c0ab598af7b88a3bd0',\n    16\t    'src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt': 'd499c4b89ad038ade9bd41e037d766d5e54defecef273541f46dc01509db5a2c',\n    17\t    'src/hivemind/prompts/matching-v3.txt': '04e23ee314e71cb094273b23e75f816c467176969b8c17dfec5a6e5d17a45a49',\n    18\t}\n    19\tJUDGING_SCHEMA_SHA = '4d1469ae9c14256c24e2c39e1b6cc772cb25e160c937f32091fc4f35bf539ca9'\n    20\tMATCHER_QUESTIONS_SHA = '86cb70600ce456be3cd5197ef173c38023513157fa3c92e341036651f95a5218'\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\tdef sha_of(value):\n    24\t    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True).encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tdef test_the_frozen_question_and_judgement_prompt_files_are_unchanged():\n    28\t    for path, expected in FROZEN_FILES.items():\n    29\t        with open(os.path.join(ROOT, path), 'rb') as handle:\n    30\t            assert hashlib.sha256(handle.read()).hexdigest() == expected, f'{path} changed; steps 3 and 4 are frozen (D354)'\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\tdef test_the_code_written_parts_of_the_question_and_judgement_requests_are_unchanged():\n    34\t    assert sha_of(judging.schema_for('judging-v7')) == JUDGING_SCHEMA_SHA\n    35\t    questions = [jev_matching.relation_question('X'), jev_matching.member_question('X'), jev_matching.piece_question('X')]\n    36\t    assert sha_of(questions) == MATCHER_QUESTIONS_SHA\n     1\t\"\"\"The clean path's Step 2 is frozen (D427, Alex, 2026-11-11: \"好jev 收尾冻结\"): the search, the Jev comparison and its request text, the\n     2\tchoice of the group a repeat joins, the forward runner, and Step 3's grouping library stay as accepted at D381 and measured through\n     3\tthe Step 2 log §17. This test holds their sha256 and fails the suite when any of them moves; the positive control flips one byte of a\n     4\tcopy and shows the check catches it. A change is a new version that only Alex opens, measured against this one.\"\"\"\n     5\timport hashlib\n     6\timport os\n     7\t\n     8\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n     9\tFROZEN = {\n    10\t    'clean-arch/step2/compare.py': 'c7fcf0903d7df58a12f29c8a74171bf51968c68cb3cfcbcae54fd449935ffabe',\n    11\t    'clean-arch/step2/run_forward.py': 'ca2a49f85e58283737e06457b0875c28e56294802148b9b443f7447f5cb4a96d',\n    12\t    'clean-arch/step2/test_compare.py': '6f1cc0ba2d4cc5c9177aa40a181a82e8fcf28df686330216daf4cf8ecd13ee3f',\n    13\t    'clean-arch/step2/test_run_forward.py': '8f4d8779fd248a22b3a57fea6d9d08c6a1d374cda14c57ef88ffbcdc15e5ffca',\n    14\t    'clean-arch/step3/library.py': 'e091095d3034791d6d59a0ddce0be190aa468e8539abbb941eaeca228d089885',\n    15\t    'clean-arch/step3/test_library.py': 'b3d20fb9dd05e818039febbcbf6b026cf47e93bc88e645ee404a7b407fa74b7c',\n    16\t}\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef sha256_of(path):\n    20\t    with open(path, 'rb') as handle:\n    21\t        return hashlib.sha256(handle.read()).hexdigest()\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\tdef moved(expected, actual):\n    25\t    return [path for path, digest in expected.items() if actual.get(path) != digest]\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef test_every_frozen_step2_file_still_has_its_recorded_hash():\n    29\t    actual = {path: sha256_of(os.path.join(ROOT, path)) for path in FROZEN}\n    30\t    assert moved(FROZEN, actual) == [], 'a frozen clean Step 2 file changed: a change is a new version Alex opens (D427)'\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\tdef test_the_check_catches_a_one_byte_change(tmp_path):\n    34\t    key = 'clean-arch/step2/compare.py'\n    35\t    with open(os.path.join(ROOT, key), 'rb') as handle:\n    36\t        data = bytearray(handle.read())\n    37\t    data[len(data) // 2] ^= 0x01\n    38\t    mutant = tmp_path / 'compare.py'\n    39\t    mutant.write_bytes(bytes(data))\n    40\t    assert moved({key: FROZEN[key]}, {key: sha256_of(str(mutant))}) == [key]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
