\nsrc/hivemind/research_context.py:35:        result = self.rows('select * from dependencies where view_id=? and seq<? order by seq,dependency_id', (vid,self.seq))\nsrc/hivemind/research_context.py:37:            res = self.rows('select * from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? and seq<? order by seq desc,id desc limit 1', (dep['dependency_id'],self.seq))\nsrc/hivemind/research_context.py:50:                    key=keys[0] if keys else None, dependencies=self.dependencies(vid))\nsrc/hivemind/research_context.py:62:            for dep in q['dependencies']:\nsrc/hivemind/research_context.py:66:                        raise ValueError('historical dependency target missing: ' + vid)\nsrc/hivemind/universe.py:95:        \"\"\"One spelling per year for the join between a view's year and a waiting dependency's year: a fiscal form\nsrc/hivemind/universe.py:99:        not one single year stays as written (a multi-year span never resolves a waiting dependency).\"\"\"\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt:1:You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt:3:- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt:4:- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt:8:- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt:10:- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/matching-v3.txt:10:2. For new or successor theses, select dependencies.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/matching-v3.txt:11:A dependency is another thesis whose conclusion the new thesis needs. Choose only supplied theses or candidates opened in this answer; use the candidate's c ID for the latter. For an asset thesis, identify which end of the dependency's ladder is bullish for it: first_is_bullish or last_is_bullish. For a theme thesis, specify whether the ladders move in the same or opposite direction: same or opposite. An event that has already happened is evidence, not a dependency. If the required numeric thesis for a particular year does not exist yet, supply wait_chain_view_id from any member of that succession chain and the required wait_year. Use no dependencies when none are needed. Do not create a cycle.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v3.txt:1:You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence and dependency conclusions. Be precise about what is established and what remains a judgement.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v3.txt:3:- Rejudge from all evidence currently in force and the current conclusions of dependencies. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v3.txt:6:- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/judging-v3.txt:7:- Return the rung's one-based position, reasons, citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs, each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none), changed, and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/review-v74i.txt:7:- a political or strategic stance with no figure and no decision (\"diversifying suppliers will not reduce dependence\"); it does not cover a policy or regulatory step, nor a decision still in force that the item reports;\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:147:    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:160:                    'dependencies': [d['view_id'] for d in dependencies(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)], 'dependants': dependants(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)})\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:178:d