{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/ui/src/model/thesis.js | sed -n '1,145p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/vocabulary.py | rg -n 'DIRECTIONS|direction|last_end'\nrg -n 'def (writer|acquire)|LockRefused|writer lock' src/hivemind/{live_lock,replay,parallel_day}.py\ncat docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/check.txt\"","aggregated_output":"     1\texport const SCORES = ['+2', '+1', '0', '−1', '−2'];\n     2\texport const score = (thesis, position) =>\n     3\t  thesis.rungs.find((r) => r.position === position)?.score ?? '—';\n     4\texport const rungLabel = (thesis, position) => {\n     5\t  const state = thesis.rungs.find((r) => r.position === position);\n     6\t  return state && state.label !== state.score ? state.label : '';\n     7\t};\n     8\t/** A new-system question whose ladder states no direction for the company: an event, an unrecorded shape or a theme's range. */\n     9\texport const undirected = (thesis) =>\n    10\t  ['event', 'unrecorded'].includes(thesis?.answerShape) || thesis?.favourableEnd === 'n/a';\n    11\t/** The chart's title: an investment score only where the ladder states a direction (page-contract/DESIGN.md). */\n    12\texport const scoreTitle = (thesis) =>\n    13\t  thesis.answerShape === 'event'\n    14\t    ? 'Current outcome'\n    15\t    : thesis.answerShape === 'unrecorded'\n    16\t      ? 'Current answer'\n    17\t      : thesis.favourableEnd === 'n/a'\n    18\t        ? 'Current range'\n    19\t        : 'AI score';\n    20\t/** What a state shows: a yes/no ladder or an undirected one names its own outcome or range once; a five-rung ladder shows its score and label. */\n    21\texport function stateWords(thesis, position) {\n    22\t  const state = thesis.rungs.find((r) => r.position === position);\n    23\t  return (thesis.rungs.length === 2 || undirected(thesis)) && state\n    24\t    ? { main: state.label, label: '' }\n    25\t    : { main: score(thesis, position), label: rungLabel(thesis, position) };\n    26\t}\n    27\texport const stateText = (thesis, position) => {\n    28\t  const { main, label } = stateWords(thesis, position);\n    29\t  return `${main} ${label}`.trim();\n    30\t};\n    31\texport const stateTone = (value, thesis = null) =>\n    32\t  undirected(thesis)\n    33\t    ? 'state--neutral'\n    34\t    : ['+2', '+1', 'Yes'].includes(value)\n    35\t      ? 'state--positive'\n    36\t      : ['−1', '−2', 'No'].includes(value)\n    37\t        ? 'state--negative'\n    38\t        : 'state--neutral';\n    39\t/** What the chart's axis marks: the score where the ladder states a direction, else the choice's position. */\n    40\texport const axisMark = (thesis, position) =>\n    41\t  undirected(thesis) ? String(position) : score(thesis, position);\n    42\texport const laneOf = (thesis, position) =>\n    43\t  undirected(thesis)\n    44\t    ? thesis.rungs.findIndex((r) => r.position === position)\n    45\t    : (thesis.rungs.length === 2 ? ['Yes', 'No'] : SCORES).indexOf(score(thesis, position));\n    46\texport const lastOf = (array) => array.at(-1);\n    47\texport const judgementsUpTo = (thesis, day) => thesis.judgements.filter((j) => j.day <= day);\n    48\texport function assessmentAt(thesis, day) {\n    49\t  return lastOf(judgementsUpTo(thesis, day)) ?? null;\n    50\t}\n    51\texport function historyIndexAt(thesis, day) {\n    52\t  return thesis.judgements.findLastIndex((j) => j.day <= day);\n    53\t}\n    54\texport function statusAt(thesis, day) {\n    55\t  if (day < thesis.created_day) return 'Not open yet';\n    56\t  const last = lastOf(thesis.switches.filter((s) => s.day <= day));\n    57\t  return last && !last.open ? 'Closed' : 'Open';\n    58\t}\n    59\texport function closingAt(thesis, day) {\n    60\t  const last = lastOf(thesis.switches.filter((s) => s.day <= day));\n    61\t  return last && !last.open ? last.reason : null;\n    62\t}\n    63\texport function snapshotThesis(thesis, day) {\n    64\t  return {\n    65\t    ...thesis,\n    66\t    judgements: judgementsUpTo(thesis, day),\n    67\t    evidence: thesis.evidence\n    68\t      .filter((e) => e.arrival_day <= day)\n    69\t      .map((e) => ({\n    70\t        ...e,\n    71\t        sources: e.sources.filter((s) => s.arrival_day <= day),\n    72\t        replaced_by: e.replaced_by?.day && e.replaced_by.day > day ? null : e.replaced_by,\n    73\t      })),\n    74\t    dependencies: dependenciesAt(thesis, day),\n    75\t    successions: thesis.successions.filter((s) => s.day <= day),\n    76\t    switches: thesis.switches.filter((s) => s.day <= day),\n    77\t    notJudged: day < thesis.created_day ? null : (thesis.notJudged ?? null),\n    78\t  };\n    79\t}\n    80\texport function dependenciesAt(thesis, day) {\n    81\t  return thesis.dependencies\n    82\t    .filter((d) => d.day <= day)\n    83\t    .map((d) => ({\n    84\t      ...d,\n    85\t      depends_on: d.resolutions.filter((r) => r.day <= day).at(-1)?.target ?? d.depends_on,\n    86\t      resolutions: d.resolutions.filter((r) => r.day <= day),\n    87\t    }));\n    88\t}\n    89\texport const isSuperseded = (evidence, day) =>\n    90\t  Boolean(evidence.replaced_by?.day && evidence.replaced_by.day <= day);\n    91\texport const groupsFor = (dataset, thesisId, day) =>\n    92\t  dataset.groups.filter(\n    93\t    (g) => g.created_day <= day && g.members.some((m) => m.thesis_id === thesisId && m.day <= day),\n    94\t  );\n    95\texport function relatedTheses(thesis, dataset, day) {\n    96\t  const ids = new Set(dependenciesAt(thesis, day).map((d) => d.depends_on));\n    97\t  for (const other of dataset.theses) {\n    98\t    if (dependenciesAt(other, day).some((d) => d.depends_on === thesis.id)) ids.add(other.id);\n    99\t  }\n   100\t  return dataset.theses.filter((t) => ids.has(t.id) && t.created_day <= day);\n   101\t}\n   102\texport function dayRounds(judgements) {\n   103\t  const rounds = [];\n   104\t  for (let i = 0; i < judgements.length; i++) {\n   105\t    const judgement = judgements[i];\n   106\t    if (rounds.at(-1)?.j.day === judgement.day) rounds[rounds.length - 1] = { i, j: judgement };\n   107\t    else rounds.push({ i, j: judgement });\n   108\t  }\n   109\t  return rounds;\n   110\t}\n   111\texport function changePoints(judgements) {\n   112\t  const points = [];\n   113\t  let previous = null;\n   114\t  for (const { i, j } of dayRounds(judgements)) {\n   115\t    if (previous !== null && j.rung !== previous) points.push({ i, from: previous, to: j.rung, j });\n   116\t    previous = j.rung;\n   117\t  }\n   118\t  return points;\n   119\t}\n   120\texport function humanise(thesis, text) {\n   121\t  return String(text ?? '')\n   122\t    .replace(\n   123\t      /\\bview(s?)\\b/gi,\n   124\t      (word, plural) => (word[0] === 'V' ? 'Thes' : 'thes') + (plural ? 'es' : 'is'),\n   125\t    )\n   126\t    .replace(/\\brung (\\d)\\b/gi, (_, n) => `state ${score(thesis, Number(n))}`)\n   127\t    .replace(/\\brungs\\b/gi, 'states')\n   128\t    .replace(/\\brung\\b/gi, 'state');\n   129\t}\n13:    13\tDIRECTIONS = ['first_is_bullish', 'last_is_bullish', 'same', 'opposite']\n23:    23\t    'direction': {'对方第一格是看多': 'first_is_bullish', '对方最后一格是看多': 'last_is_bullish', '同向': 'same', '反向': 'opposite'},\n58:    58\t    \"\"\"A matching answer with canonical candidate outcomes, evidence outcomes and dependency directions.\"\"\"\n61:    61\t                              dependencies=[dict(dep, direction=canonical('direction', dep.get('direction'))) for dep in d.get('dependencies', [])])\nsrc/hivemind/live_lock.py:21:class LockRefused(RuntimeError):\nsrc/hivemind/live_lock.py:34:        raise LockRefused(f'the lock folder {LOCK_FOLDER} cannot be created: {error}') from error\nsrc/hivemind/live_lock.py:36:        raise LockRefused(f'the lock folder {LOCK_FOLDER} cannot be written')\nsrc/hivemind/live_lock.py:45:        raise LockRefused(f'{real} has {status.st_nlink} hard links: a store is opened only by its own path')\nsrc/hivemind/live_lock.py:57:def acquire(store_path):\nsrc/hivemind/live_lock.py:66:        raise LockRefused(f'{real} is being written (its lock is held): read a snapshot of it instead (scripts/snapshot_store.py)') from None\nold-1 control: day 2026-09-20 seq 1884 chars 42892 (+0) sha == stored\nold-1 changed: day 2026-09-20 seq 1884 chars 43574 (+682) sha differs\nold-2 control: day 2026-09-20 seq 1884 chars 66729 (+0) sha == stored\nold-2 changed: day 2026-09-20 seq 1884 chars 67486 (+757) sha differs\nold-3 control: day 2026-09-20 seq 1884 chars 41502 (+0) sha == stored\nold-3 changed: day 2026-09-20 seq 1884 chars 42266 (+764) sha differs\ncontrol requests byte-equal to the stored ones: True\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '1,202p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,141p'\nrg -n 'engine|round_module|round_of_judgements|end_of_day|check|rebuild' scripts/replay.py scripts/preflight.py src/hivemind/parallel_day.py\nnl -ba src/hivemind/extraction.py | sed -n '38,78p;460,484p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"One item = one round (06-views.md 进库): source check → store → lists → the matching calls → checks → write.\n     2\tRe-judging is the day's step (D63, 2026-10-24: once a day, over every view whose reading changed that day), run by\n     3\tthe replay after the day's items and before pull mode; see judge_day. Each step appends its processing row in the\n     4\tsame commit as its writes; a resume continues at the step the processing record names (after an ok step, or the\n     5\tfailed step itself) and never repeats a completed step.\"\"\"\n     6\timport dataclasses\n     7\timport json\n     8\t\n     9\tfrom .. import dispatch, extraction, vocabulary\n    10\tfrom . import jev_matching, judging, matching, store, writing\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t@dataclasses.dataclass\n    14\tclass RoundResult:\n    15\t    input_id: str\n    16\t    evidence: int = 0\n    17\t    candidates: int = 0\n    18\t    new_views: int = 0\n    19\t    judged: int = 0\n    20\t    changed: int = 0\n    21\t    cost: float = 0.0\n    22\t    cached_calls: int = 0\n    23\t    failed: str = ''\n    24\t    dropped: int = 0\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tdef _fail(conn, item, seq, result, step, kind, detail, pool_key):\n    28\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, step, 'failed', detail[:300])\n    29\t    store.pool(conn, kind, pool_key, {'input_id': item['input_id'], 'error': detail[:300]}, seq)\n    30\t    result.failed = detail[:200]\n    31\t    conn.commit()\n    32\t    return result\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, *, extra_views=(), call_offset=0, transport=None, workers=1):\n    36\t    \"\"\"One matching call with one retry on a refused check. Returns Checked, or None after marking the failure.\"\"\"\n    37\t    note = ''\n    38\t    checked = None\n    39\t    engine = jev_matching if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else matching      # Jev answers once; a retry would be the same answer\n    40\t    for attempt in range(1 if engine is jev_matching else 2):\n    41\t        try:\n    42\t            options = {'workers': workers, 'llm_transport': transport} if engine is jev_matching else {}     # the collision judge sends with the caller's transport too\n    43\t            answer = engine.decide(archive, cfg, conn, item, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, extra_views=extra_views, retry_note=note, transport=transport, **options)\n    44\t        except Exception as error:\n    45\t            _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_failed', 'matching: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n    46\t            return None\n    47\t        result.cost += answer.cost_usd\n    48\t        result.cached_calls += int(answer.cached)\n    49\t        checked = matching.check(conn, universe, answer.data, candidates, evidence, lists, shown)\n    50\t        shown_record = {'candidates': lists.candidate_lists, 'evidence': {f'{k[0]}|{k[1]}': v for k, v in lists.evidence_lists.items()}}\n    51\t        if getattr(answer, 'request_records', None):\n    52\t            shown_record['requests'] = answer.request_records\n    53\t        store.insert(conn, 'match_records', seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], call_no=call_offset + attempt + 1,\n    54\t                     shown_json=json.dumps(shown_record),\n    55\t                     request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, call_id=answer.call_id, decisions_json=json.dumps(answer.data, ensure_ascii=False),\n    56\t                     checks_json=json.dumps({'refusals': checked.refusals, 'not_opened': checked.not_opened, 'notes': checked.notes}, ensure_ascii=False), written_json=None)\n    57\t        if not checked.refusals:\n    58\t            return checked\n    59\t        note = '；'.join(checked.refusals)\n    60\t    _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_refused_twice', 'matching refused twice: ' + note, item['category'])\n    61\t    return None\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef changed_views_of_day(conn, day):\n    65\t    \"\"\"The views whose reading changed on a replay day: the union of the 'written' records of that day's items and of the coverage-start reading's\n    66\t    record dated that day (D364: the questions it linked starting figures to are judged in the first day's round).\"\"\"\n    67\t    changed = set()\n    68\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select reason from processing_steps where step in ('written', 'baseline') and result='ok' and publication_day=?\", (day,)):\n    69\t        changed.update(json.loads(row['reason']).get('changed', []))\n    70\t    return changed\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, *, transport=None, log=print):\n    74\t    \"\"\"D63: one re-judging round per day over every open view whose reading changed that day, dependencies first,\n    75\t    recorded under the day's own processing record (input 'day:<date>'); a view already judged at this sequence\n    76\t    number (a resumed day) is not judged twice.\"\"\"\n    77\t    marker = {'input_id': f'day:{day}', 'publication_day': day}\n    78\t    changed = changed_views_of_day(conn, day)\n    79\t    result = RoundResult(marker['input_id'])\n    80\t    if not changed:\n    81\t        return result\n    82\t    try:\n    83\t        judged = judging.round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, sorted(changed), seq, marker, transport=transport)\n    84\t        result.judged = len(judged)\n    85\t        result.changed = sum(1 for j in judged if j['changed'])\n    86\t        result.cost += sum(j['cost'] for j in judged)\n    87\t        result.cached_calls += sum(1 for j in judged if j['cached'])\n    88\t        dispatch.mark(conn, marker, seq, 'judged', 'ok', f'{len(changed)} views changed, {len(judged)} judged, {result.changed} changed conclusions')\n    89\t        conn.commit()\n    90\t    except judging.JudgementRefused as error:\n    91\t        return _fail(conn, marker, seq, result, 'judged', 'judgement_refused_twice', 'judgement refused twice: ' + str(error), 'day')\n    92\t    except Exception as error:\n    93\t        return _fail(conn, marker, seq, result, 'judged', 'judging_failed', 'judging: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n    94\t    return result\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tdef run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, *, resume_from=None, transport=None, log=print, extractor=None, matching_workers=1):\n    98\t    result = RoundResult(item['input_id'])\n    99\t    if resume_from in ('judged', 'handed_over'):       # written already; judging is the day's step\n   100\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'resumed')\n   101\t        conn.commit()\n   102\t        return result\n   103\t    objects = [o['value'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or [] if universe.has(o['value'])]\n   104\t    shown = extraction.shown_views(conn, cfg, item, objects)\n   105\t    # extraction (or its stored handover on resume)\n   106\t    handover = None\n   107\t    if resume_from and resume_from != 'extracted':\n   108\t        row = conn.execute('select handover_json from handovers where input_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (item['input_id'],)).fetchone()\n   109\t        if row:\n   110\t            saved = vocabulary.extraction_answer(json.loads(row['handover_json']))          # a handover saved by a Chinese version reads in the canonical vocabulary\n   111\t            handover = extraction.Handover(saved['evidence'], saved['candidates'], saved['dropped'], 0, '', True, 0.0, saved.get('new_groups') or [])\n   112\t    if handover is None:\n   113\t        try:\n   114\t            handover = (extractor or extraction.extract)(archive, cfg, item, item['text'], shown, universe, transport=transport)\n   115\t        except Exception as error:\n   116\t            return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'extracted', 'extraction_failed', 'extraction: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   117\t        result.cost += handover.cost_usd\n   118\t        result.cached_calls += int(handover.cached)\n   119\t        store.insert(conn, 'handovers', input_id=item['input_id'], seq=seq,\n   120\t                     handover_json=json.dumps({'evidence': handover.evidence, 'candidates': handover.candidates, 'dropped': handover.dropped, 'new_groups': handover.new_groups}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   121\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'extracted', 'ok', f'{len(handover.evidence)} evidence, {len(handover.candidates)} candidates, {len(handover.dropped)} dropped')\n   122\t        conn.commit()\n   123\t    result.evidence, result.candidates, result.dropped = len(handover.evidence), len(handover.candidates), len(handover.dropped)\n   124\t    if not handover.evidence and not handover.candidates:\n   125\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'nothing to match')\n   126\t        conn.commit()\n   127\t        return result\n   128\t    # first matching call: the candidates and the evidence linked straight to existing views\n   129\t    lists = matching.build_lists(conn, handover, shown, cfg.search_top_n)\n   130\t    checked = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, handover.candidates, handover.evidence, lists, shown, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   131\t    if checked is None:\n   132\t        return result\n   133\t    # second call: evidence linked to candidates that attached to an existing view, compared under that view\n   134\t    second_pass = {}\n   135\t    pending = []\n   136\t    for e in handover.evidence:\n   137\t        for link in e['links']:\n   138\t            outcome = checked.outcomes.get(link)\n   139\t            if outcome and outcome[0] == 'merge':\n   140\t                pending.append((e, outcome[1]))\n   141\t    if pending:\n   142\t        lists2 = matching.Lists({}, {(e['id'], view_id): matching.rank_evidence(conn, view_id, e['one_line'], cfg.search_top_n) for e, view_id in pending})\n   143\t        evidence2, seen = [], set()\n   144\t        for e, view_id in pending:\n   145\t            if e['id'] not in seen:\n   146\t                evidence2.append(dict(e, links=[v for x, v in pending if x['id'] == e['id']]))\n   147\t                seen.add(e['id'])\n   148\t        checked2 = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, [], evidence2, lists2, [], extra_views=sorted({v for _, v in pending}),\n   149\t                          call_offset=2, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   150\t        if checked2 is None:\n   151\t            return result\n   152\t        second_pass = checked2.evidence\n   153\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   154\t    # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   155\t    try:\n   156\t        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   157\t    except Exception as error:\n   158\t        return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'written', 'writing_failed', 'writing: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   159\t    result.new_views = len(set(written.new_views.values()))\n   160\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'written', 'ok', json.dumps({'changed': sorted(written.changed_views), 'new': written.new_views, 'notes': written.notes[:20]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   161\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', '')\n   162\t    conn.commit()\n   163\t    return result\n    51\tdef run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n    52\t        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n    53\t    items_db = testdb.open_db(testdb_path)\n    54\t    conn = store.open_db(views_path)\n    55\t    refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn)\n    56\t    last_done = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    57\t    start = from_day\n    58\t    if last_done and from_day <= last_done:\n    59\t        next_day = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(last_done) + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()\n    60\t        if next_day > until_day:\n    61\t            raise BackdatingError(f'views database already completed {last_done}; nothing to run before it')\n    62\t        log(f'resuming after the last completed day {last_done}')\n    63\t        start = next_day\n    64\t    last_written = conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0').fetchone()[0]\n    65\t    if last_written and start < last_written:\n    66\t        raise BackdatingError(f'views database already holds rounds of {last_written}; a replay cannot start before it (D31)')\n    67\t    totals = {'items': 0, 'extracted': 0, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 0, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0,\n    68\t              'evidence': 0, 'new_views': 0, 'judged': 0, 'changed': 0, 'closed': 0}\n    69\t    calls_before, cost_before, *_ = archive.totals()\n    70\t    for day in calendar_days(start, until_day):\n    71\t        day_stats = {k: 0 for k in totals}\n    72\t        day_cost_before = archive.totals()[1]\n    73\t        processed = 0\n    74\t        to_run = []\n    75\t        for item in testdb.feed(items_db, day, day):\n    76\t            if item['publication_day'] > day:\n    77\t                raise LookAheadError(f'{item[\"input_id\"]} is dated {item[\"publication_day\"]}, after replay day {day}')\n    78\t            if only_objects and not any(o['value'] in only_objects for o in item['object_identifiers']):\n    79\t                continue\n    80\t            if max_items_per_day and processed >= max_items_per_day:\n    81\t                break\n    82\t            day_stats['items'] += 1\n    83\t            route = dispatch.route(conn, item, universe)\n    84\t            if route.kind != 'extract':\n    85\t                day_stats[route.kind] += 1\n    86\t                if route.kind == 'skipped':\n    87\t                    processed += 1      # written by an earlier run of this day: a restart keeps the day's item limit\n    88\t                if route.kind == 'merged':\n    89\t                    dispatch.mark(conn, item, 0, 'merged', 'ok', route.reason)\n    90\t                    conn.commit()\n    91\t                continue\n    92\t            processed += 1\n    93\t            to_run.append((item, route))\n    94\t        results = (day_runner(conn, archive, cfg, universe, to_run, day=day, transport=transport, log=log) if day_runner else\n    95\t                   (round_module.run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, route.sequence_no, resume_from=route.resume_from, transport=transport, log=log)\n    96\t                    for item, route in to_run))\n    97\t        finished = 0\n    98\t        try:\n    99\t            for index, result in enumerate(results):\n   100\t                if index >= len(to_run) or result.input_id != to_run[index][0]['input_id']:\n   101\t                    raise RuntimeError('day runner returned results out of input order')\n   102\t                finished += 1\n   103\t                day_stats['extracted'] += 1\n   104\t                day_stats['evidence'] += result.evidence\n   105\t                day_stats['new_views'] += result.new_views\n   106\t                day_stats['judged'] += result.judged\n   107\t                day_stats['changed'] += result.changed\n   108\t                if result.failed:\n   109\t                    day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   110\t                    log(f'  ! {result.input_id[:60]}: {result.failed}')\n   111\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'item failed; day {day} remains resumable: {result.failed}')\n   112\t                if spend_cap_usd is not None and archive.totals()[1] - cost_before > spend_cap_usd:\n   113\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'spend cap {spend_cap_usd} reached on {day}')\n   114\t        finally:\n   115\t            if hasattr(results, 'close'):\n   116\t                results.close()\n   117\t        if finished != len(to_run):\n   118\t            raise RuntimeError('day runner did not complete every routed item')\n   119\t        seq = store.next_sequence(conn) - 1\n   120\t        judged = round_module.judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, transport=transport, log=log)\n   121\t        day_stats['judged'] += judged.judged\n   122\t        day_stats['changed'] += judged.changed\n   123\t        if judged.failed:\n   124\t            day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   125\t            log(f'  ! day judging: {judged.failed}')\n   126\t            raise RuntimeError(f'judging failed; day {day} remains resumable: {judged.failed}')\n   127\t        closed = pull.end_of_day(conn, day, seq)\n   128\t        day_stats['closed'] = len(closed)\n   129\t        # The day ends at the last sequence it wrote, a closing's own sequence on a day without items included, so the next day starts after it.\n   130\t        store.complete_day(conn, day, store.next_sequence(conn) - 1, time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   131\t        conn.commit()\n   132\t        for key in totals:\n   133\t            totals[key] += day_stats[key]\n   134\t        calls, cost, _, _ = archive.totals()\n   135\t        day_cost = cost - day_cost_before  # Includes discarded speculative calls and repaired refusals.\n   136\t        open_count = len(store.open_views(conn))\n   137\t        log(f'{day} | items {day_stats[\"items\"]:3d} extracted {day_stats[\"extracted\"]:3d} merged {day_stats[\"merged\"]:2d} skipped {day_stats[\"not_processed\"]:2d} '\n   138\t            f'failed {day_stats[\"failed\"]:2d} | evidence {day_stats[\"evidence\"]:3d} new views {day_stats[\"new_views\"]:2d} judged {day_stats[\"judged\"]:3d} '\n   139\t            f'changed {day_stats[\"changed\"]:3d} closed {len(closed)} | open views {open_count} | day ${day_cost:.2f} total ${cost - cost_before:.2f} calls {calls - calls_before}')\n   140\t        if day0 and day == day0:\n   141\t            conn.commit()\nsrc/hivemind/parallel_day.py:9:the default replay stays serial. The run's spend cap is checked after each committed item, so in-flight early\nsrc/hivemind/parallel_day.py:93:        if cfg.matching.engine != 'jev' and self.jev_workers != 1:\nscripts/preflight.py:1:\"\"\"Preflight: run every code check and every prompt against the stored model answers before a paid run ($0).\nscripts/preflight.py:3:AGENTS.md §3 \"Strictness is code too\" and §4 \"a check must judge something\": a check is accepted on real data,\nscripts/preflight.py:4:reports how many cases it judged, and a check over an empty population is unexercised. This script replays what\nscripts/preflight.py:5:the archive and the earlier runs' views databases already hold through the current code and prints, per check,\nscripts/preflight.py:9:  B. extraction's code checks (extraction.sift) over every stored extraction answer\nscripts/preflight.py:10:  C. matching's code checks (matching.check) over every stored matching record, with the lists shown at the time\nscripts/preflight.py:16:Exit status 1 when a check judged no case.\nscripts/preflight.py:67:        for error in model.check_schema(json.loads(answer_json), SCHEMAS.get(purpose, {})):\nscripts/preflight.py:110:    rows = list(archive_conn.execute(\"select config_version, config_checksum, request_sha256, request_json, answer_json from model_calls where purpose='extract'\"))\nscripts/preflight.py:112:    for config_version, checksum, sha, request_json, answer_json in rows:\nscripts/preflight.py:133:            key = (config_version, checksum)\nscripts/preflight.py:139:                if cfg.version != config_version or cfg.checksum != checksum:\nscripts/preflight.py:164:    tally('B. current extraction checks before the handover, using the supplied universe', produced_e + produced_c, (produced_e - kept_e) + (produced_c - kept_c), reasons, examples)\nscripts/preflight.py:185:    written is refused with the snapshot route named; the path checked on both sides of the open and after the copy; the copy made by\nscripts/preflight.py:226:        # matching.check writes suggested themes to the review pool, so it runs on a scratch copy, never on the real file\nscripts/preflight.py:249:                checked = matching.check(conn, uni, json.loads(rec['decisions_json']), candidates, evidence, lists, shown_views)\nscripts/preflight.py:251:                key = 'check raised ' + type(error).__name__\nscripts/preflight.py:257:            if checked.refusals:\nscripts/preflight.py:259:            for refusal in checked.refusals:\nscripts/preflight.py:264:    tally('C. matching code checks over stored records (database state is the final one, not the state at the time)', judged, refused_records, reasons, examples)\nscripts/preflight.py:280:    checks = [(f'role-{v}.txt', extraction.TIERS + vocabulary.KINDS + vocabulary.ASSET_LABELS) for v in extraction.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS]\nscripts/preflight.py:281:    checks += [(f'{v}.txt', judging.PUSHES) for v in judging.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS]\nscripts/preflight.py:284:        checks.append((os.path.basename(path), (matching.OUTCOMES + matching.EVIDENCE_OUTCOMES + vocabulary.DIRECTIONS) if matching.is_english(version)\nscripts/preflight.py:287:    for name, values in checks:\nscripts/preflight.py:345:        print('\\nUNEXERCISED: a check judged no case')\nscripts/replay.py:13:Jev matching questions at a time (8; one at a time for another matching engine); the ledger equals the serial one for\nscripts/replay.py:66:                        help='Jev matching questions sent at a time when --workers > 1; default 8 for Jev, 1 for another engine')\nscripts/replay.py:85:        jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\nscripts/replay.py:88:    log(f'--- replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version}'\n    38\t    if version not in SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\n    39\t        raise ValueError(f'extraction {version!r} is not built; this code builds only {\", \".join(SUPPORTED_VERSIONS)} (D274)')\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef shown_views(conn, cfg, item, objects):\n    43\t    \"\"\"The questions an item's extraction request shows (05-extraction block 5): the objects' questions open at the start of the\n    44\t    item's day, the same list for every item of that day (D251), with the key, groups and aliases each had then (they feed its takes\n    45\t    line) and its direct parents (they feed the narrowest rule). The one place the stream and the parallel runner take the list from.\"\"\"\n    46\t    require_supported(cfg.extraction_setting(item['category']).prompt_version.rpartition('-')[2])\n    47\t    from .views import store\n    48\t    return [dict(v, key=store.view_key(conn, v['view_id']) or {},\n    49\t                 groups=[{'name': g['name'], 'scope': g['scope'], 'aliases': g.get('aliases') or []}\n    50\t                         for g in store.groups_of_view_at(conn, v['view_id'], v['snapshot_seq'])],\n    51\t                 parents=store.direct_parents(conn, v['view_id'], v['snapshot_seq']))\n    52\t            for v in store.views_open_at_day_start(conn, objects, item['publication_day'])]\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef narrowest_links(links, parents):\n    56\t    \"\"\"D207's one rule the filing enforces in code (2026-11-02, D265): a statement linked to a question and to a question that question\n    57\t    depends on (a driver and its root, transitively) keeps the narrower one only. `parents` maps a view id to the ids it depends on.\"\"\"\n    58\t    def ancestors(view_id, seen):\n    59\t        for parent in parents.get(view_id, ()):\n    60\t            if parent not in seen:\n    61\t                seen.add(parent)\n    62\t                ancestors(parent, seen)\n    63\t        return seen\n    64\t    broader = set()\n    65\t    for link in links:\n    66\t        broader |= ancestors(link, set())\n    67\t    return [l for l in links if l not in broader]\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\tdef base_schema():\n    72\t    return {\n    73\t        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence', 'candidates'],\n    74\t        'properties': {\n    75\t            'evidence': {'type': 'array', 'items': {\n    76\t                'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n    77\t                'required': ['id', 'quote', 'one_line', 'speaker', 'original_who', 'original_day', 'tier', 'event_time', 'links'],\n    78\t                'properties': {\n   460\tdef read_item(archive, cfg, item, text, shown_views, universe, *, transport=None):\n   461\t    \"\"\"The extraction call and the code checks on its answer: a statement may link to a shown question or to a kept candidate.\"\"\"\n   462\t    setting, system, user, schema = request_for(cfg, item, text, shown_views, universe)\n   463\t    answer = model.call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, 'extraction', 'extract', transport=transport)\n   464\t    evidence, candidates, dropped, new_groups = sift_with_groups(answer.data, item, text, {v['view_id'] for v in shown_views}, universe)\n   465\t    return Reading(evidence, candidates, dropped, new_groups, answer, setting.prompt_version.rpartition('-')[2])\n   466\t\n   467\t\n   468\tdef file_reading(reading, item, shown_views):\n   469\t    \"\"\"The handover: the extraction's own links are the filing (D256). A statement linked to a question and to a question that\n   470\t    question depends on keeps the narrower one (D207); a statement no open question and no kept candidate takes is dropped as 'no\n   471\t    home' (D209), like every other drop: a candidate left with none of its evidence is dropped too, and a statement whose only link was\n   472\t    such a candidate has no home.\"\"\"\n   473\t    candidates, dropped, answer = reading.candidates, list(reading.dropped), reading.answer\n   474\t    parents = {v['view_id']: v.get('parents') or [] for v in shown_views}\n   475\t    evidence = [dict(e, links=narrowest_links(e['links'], parents)) for e in reading.evidence]\n   476\t    while True:\n   477\t        candidates = candidates_with_evidence(candidates, {e['id'] for e in evidence}, item, dropped)\n   478\t        candidate_ids = {c['id'] for c in candidates}\n   479\t        evidence = [dict(e, links=[l for l in e['links'] if not placement.CANDIDATE_ID.match(l) or l in candidate_ids]) for e in evidence]\n   480\t        homeless = [e for e in evidence if not e['links']]\n   481\t        if not homeless:\n   482\t            break\n   483\t        dropped.extend((e['id'], 'no home') for e in homeless)\n   484\t        evidence = [e for e in evidence if e['links']]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json,statistics\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nfor draw,center,total in [(\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"v8\\\",\\\"v4\\\"),(\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\"),(\\\"old-3\\\",\\\"v35\\\",\\\"v3\\\")]:\n p=root/draw/\\\"prod\\\"\n with db(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n  print(draw, \\\"counts\\\", *(c.execute(\\\"select count(*) from \\\"+t).fetchone()[0] for t in (\\\"views\\\",\\\"judgements\\\",\\\"dependencies\\\")))\n  for v,k,day in c.execute(\\\"select v.view_id,v.created_seq,(select min(publication_day) from processing_steps p where p.sequence_no=v.created_seq) from views v where v.view_id in (?,?)\\\",(center,total)):\n   print(v,k,day)\n  for day,seq,jid,v,changed,num,out in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,seq,judgement_id,view_id,changed,call_id,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day >= ? order by judgement_id\\\",(center,total,\\\"2026-09-19\\\")):\n   usage=a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\", (num,)).fetchone()\n   print(day,seq,jid,v,changed,usage,out)\n  if draw==\\\"old-2\\\":\n   for v in (center,total):\n    for day,num in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,call_id from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day in (?,?) order by judgement_id\\\",(v,\\\"2026-08-24\\\",\\\"2026-08-25\\\")):\n     print(\\\"early\\\",v,day,a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(num,)).fetchone())\n   for v in (center,total):\n    print(v,\\\"archive cost example avg\\\",statistics.mean([sum(x*y/1e6 for x,y in zip(a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(num,)).fetchone(),(.1,.50))) for (num,) in c.execute(\\\"select call_id from judgements where view_id=?\\\",(v,))]))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json,statistics\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nfor draw,center,total in [(\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"v8\\\",\\\"v4\\\"),(\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\"),(\\\"old-3\\\",\\\"v35\\\",\\\"v3\\\")]:\n p=root/draw/\\\"prod\\\"\n with db(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n  print(draw, \\\"counts\\\", *(c.execute(\\\"select count(*) from \\\"+t).fetchone()[0] for t in (\\\"views\\\",\\\"judgements\\\",\\\"dependencies\\\")))\n  for v,k,day in c.execute(\\\"select v.view_id,v.created_seq,(select min(publication_day) from processing_steps p where p.sequence_no=v.created_seq) from views v where v.view_id in (?,?)\\\",(center,total)):\n   print(v,k,day)\n  for day,seq,jid,v,changed,num,out in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,seq,judgement_id,view_id,changed,call_id,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day >= ? order by judgement_id\\\",(center,total,\\\"2026-09-19\\\")):\n   usage=a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\", (num,)).fetchone()\n   print(day,seq,jid,v,changed,usage,out)\n  if draw==\\\"old-2\\\":\n   for v in (center,total):\n    for day,num in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,call_id from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day in (?,?) order by judgement_id\\\",(v,\\\"2026-08-24\\\",\\\"2026-08-25\\\")):\n     print(\\\"early\\\",v,day,a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(num,)).fetchone())\n   for v in (center,total):\n    print(v,\\\"archive cost example avg\\\",statistics.mean([sum(x*y/1e6 for x,y in zip(a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(num,)).fetchone(),(.1,.50))) for (num,) in c.execute(\\\"select call_id from judgements where view_id=?\\\",(v,))]))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 counts 47 1609 0\nv4 22 2026-07-02\nv8 62 2026-07-06\n2026-09-19 1856 1534 v4 1 (28786, 4873) About $398 billion: add FY2027 Q1 actual revenue of $81.62 billion, Q2 actual revenue of $96.2 billion, and the Q3 guidance midpoint of $108 billion, then apply the 65% Q4 year-over-year growth expectation to an estimated FY2026 Q4 base of about $68.1 billion (about $112.4 billion).\n2026-09-19 1856 1538 v8 0 (12684, 4140) About $395 billion: approximately $164 billion in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue midpoint at the recent Data Center mix, and an estimated roughly $131 billion in Q4 as supply builds and hyperscale growth reaccelerates.\n2026-09-20 1884 1575 v4 1 (25527, 3052) About $404 billion: add reported Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, an estimated Q3 of about $113.6 billion (the cited 3.1% historical beat applied to the $110.16 billion high end of guidance), and Q4 of about $112.2 billion (65% growth on Q4 FY2026's $68 billion actual).\n2026-09-20 1884 1580 v8 1 (12332, 3987) About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 using the $108 billion total-revenue guidance midpoint and 92.5% recent Data Center mix, plus an estimated $126 billion in Q4 as hyperscale growth reaccelerates and Vera Rubin supply builds, discounted for continuing constraints.\nold-2 counts 43 1616 0\nv14 148 2026-07-10\nv9 62 2026-07-06\n2026-09-19 1856 1547 v14 0 (19168, 3550) Approximately $418 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2, about $113.5 billion estimated for Q3, and about $127 billion for Q4 by carrying roughly 12% sequential growth forward from the estimated Q3 level.\n2026-09-19 1856 1559 v9 1 (20471, 3856) About $385–390 billion: approximately $164 billion in Q1–Q2, about $100 billion in Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, plus roughly $120–125 billion in Q4 as hyperscale growth reaccelerates and Rubin supply builds.\n2026-09-20 1884 1585 v14 1 (17790, 4107) About $419 billion: Q1 $81.6 billion plus Q2 $96.2 billion, estimated Q3 of about $113.5 billion (the $110.16 billion guidance high end plus the reported average 3.1% beat), and Q4 of about $127 billion by carrying forward the guided 12% sequential growth.\n2026-09-20 1884 1592 v9 1 (18361, 7590) Approximately $410 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and roughly $146 billion estimated for Q4. The Q4 estimate reflects management's expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp, with a discounted contribution from SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half Data Center revenue would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\nearly v9 2026-08-24 (18480, 3868)\nearly v9 2026-08-25 (18349, 4190)\nearly v14 2026-08-24 (21031, 3916)\nearly v14 2026-08-25 (22445, 4901)\nv9 archive cost example avg 0.003959152702702703\nv14 archive cost example avg 0.0036712845070422536\nold-3 counts 49 1707 0\nv3 22 2026-07-02\nv35 932 2026-08-19\n2026-09-19 1856 1633 v3 1 (30785, 3615) About $446 billion: $177.837 billion reported in H1, roughly $113.6 billion for Q3 using the historical beat over guidance, and about $127 billion for Q4 carrying forward 12% sequential growth, plus approximately $27–28 billion from SemiAnalysis’s 20% uplift applied only to second-half data-center compute.\n2026-09-19 1856 1636 v35 1 (12769, 4273) About $375 billion: $164 billion reported for the first half (e5360), plus approximately $100 billion for Q3 (the $108 billion total-revenue outlook, e3322, applied to the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, e3453; the resulting $99.9 billion calculation is e3455), plus roughly $110 billion for Q4 as growth reaccelerates. This is an estimate, not a reported FY2027 outcome.\n2026-09-20 1884 1672 v3 1 (28176, 5897) About $446 billion: $177.837 billion in first-half revenue, approximately $113.6 billion for Q3 using the guidance midpoint and the cited average beat, and approximately $127 billion for Q4 by carrying forward 12% sequential growth, then adding about $27–28 billion for the estimated 20% second-half data-center-compute uplift.\n2026-09-20 1884 1674 v35 1 (11928, 3503) About $374–375 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, approximately $100 billion implied for Q3 by the $108 billion total-revenue outlook and the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, plus roughly $110 billion for Q4 given expected reacceleration and the forecast of more than $100 billion.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
