{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/parallel_day.py | sed -n '1,142p'\nrg -n 'def |retry_note|WriteConflict|\\\\.run\\\\(' src/hivemind/parallel_day.py\nrg -n 'DIRECTIONS|def validate|def call|def openai_transport' src/hivemind/{vocabulary,model}.py\nnl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '448,471p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"One day's items with concurrent request preparation and one ordered writer (D172, D181).\n     2\t\n     3\tAn item's accepted extraction must answer the exact request built from the ledger committed by the items before it,\n     4\tas in serial processing (D159). Extraction requests for later items are sent early, from the ledger as it stands;\n     5\tafter each commit, every waiting request that commit changed is built again and sent again, and at its turn an item\n     6\taccepts a prepared answer only if its request is byte-identical to the request built now. Matching questions within\n     7\tan item run concurrently and are applied in their planned order. Only this coordinator reads or writes the ledger;\n     8\tworkers receive copies and write only the thread-safe call archive. Opt-in through `replay.run(day_runner=...)`;\n     9\tthe default replay stays serial. The run's spend cap is checked after each committed item, so in-flight early\n    10\trequests can pass it by at most the worker count's calls.\n    11\t\"\"\"\n    12\timport concurrent.futures\n    13\timport copy\n    14\timport dataclasses\n    15\timport hashlib\n    16\timport json\n    17\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    18\timport time\n    19\t\n    20\tfrom . import extraction, model\n    21\tfrom .views import round as rounds, store\n    22\t\n    23\tPACKAGE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\tdef digest(path):\n    27\t    value = hashlib.sha256()\n    28\t    with path.open('rb') as handle:\n    29\t        for chunk in iter(lambda: handle.read(1024 * 1024), b''):\n    30\t            value.update(chunk)\n    31\t    return value.hexdigest()\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tdef environment_key(cfg, universe):\n    35\t    return model.request_identity({'config': dataclasses.asdict(cfg), 'universe': vars(universe)})[1]\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef runtime_key():\n    39\t    files = sorted(PACKAGE.rglob('*.py')) + sorted((PACKAGE / 'prompts').glob('*'))\n    40\t    return model.request_identity({str(path.relative_to(PACKAGE.parent)): digest(path) for path in files if path.is_file()})[1]\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef item_key(item):\n    44\t    return model.request_identity(item)[1]\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef extraction_key(cfg, item, text, shown, universe):\n    48\t    setting, system, user, schema = extraction.request_for(cfg, item, text, shown, universe)\n    49\t    return model.request_identity(model.build_request(setting, system, user, schema, 'extraction', cfg.provider))[1]\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tclass ParallelDay:\n    53\t    \"\"\"A `day_runner` for replay.run: per-day manifest, bounded early extraction, validated ordered commits.\"\"\"\n    54\t\n    55\t    def __init__(self, source_path, manifest_dir, *, extraction_workers=2, jev_workers=2):\n    56\t        for workers in (extraction_workers, jev_workers):\n    57\t            if not isinstance(workers, int) or isinstance(workers, bool) or workers < 1:\n    58\t                raise ValueError('worker counts must be positive integers')\n    59\t        self.source_path, self.manifest_dir = Path(source_path), Path(manifest_dir)\n    60\t        if not self.source_path.is_absolute() or not self.source_path.is_file() or not self.manifest_dir.is_absolute():\n    61\t            raise ValueError('use an existing absolute source path and an absolute manifest directory')\n    62\t        self.extraction_workers, self.jev_workers = extraction_workers, jev_workers\n    63\t        self.events = []\n    64\t\n    65\t    def _event(self, input_id, event, **fields):\n    66\t        self.events.append(dict(fields, input_id=input_id, event=event, t=time.perf_counter()))\n    67\t\n    68\t    def _manifest(self, conn, cfg, universe, items, day):\n    69\t        self.manifest_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    70\t        path = self.manifest_dir / f'day-{day}.json'\n    71\t        metadata = {'day': day, 'environment': environment_key(cfg, universe), 'runtime': runtime_key(),\n    72\t                    'source': digest(self.source_path), 'extraction_workers': self.extraction_workers,\n    73\t                    'jev_workers': self.jev_workers}\n    74\t        entries = [{'input_id': item['input_id'], 'seq': route.sequence_no, 'hash': item_key(item)} for item, route in items]\n    75\t        started = conn.execute(\"select 1 from processing_steps where publication_day=? and step in ('extracted','written','handed_over') limit 1\", (day,)).fetchone()\n    76\t        if not started:\n    77\t            # Nothing of this day is written in this ledger: a manifest left by another run or ledger guards nothing here.\n    78\t            path.write_text(json.dumps(dict(metadata, inputs=entries), sort_keys=True), encoding='utf-8')\n    79\t        elif not path.exists():\n    80\t            raise ValueError('cannot adopt a partially processed day without its parallel-day manifest; finish it with --workers 1')\n    81\t        try:\n    82\t            saved = json.loads(path.read_text())\n    83\t        except (OSError, ValueError) as error:\n    84\t            raise ValueError('unreadable parallel-day manifest; refusing to guess its inputs') from error\n    85\t        if {k: saved.get(k) for k in metadata} != metadata:\n    86\t            raise ValueError('parallel-day manifest source, configuration or runtime changed')\n    87\t        remaining = [entry for entry in saved['inputs'] if not store.is_processed(conn, entry['input_id'])]\n    88\t        if remaining != entries:\n    89\t            raise ValueError('parallel-day manifest input order or content changed')\n    90\t        return metadata\n    91\t\n    92\t    def __call__(self, conn, archive, cfg, universe, items, *, day, transport=None, log=print):\n    93\t        if cfg.matching.engine != 'jev' and self.jev_workers != 1:\n    94\t            raise ValueError('parallel matching is only implemented for Jev')\n    95\t        metadata = self._manifest(conn, cfg, universe, items, day)\n    96\t        frozen_cfg, frozen_universe = copy.deepcopy(cfg), copy.deepcopy(universe)\n    97\t        pending, prepared_futures, next_index = {}, [], 0\n    98\t        pool = concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=self.extraction_workers)\n    99\t\n   100\t        def current_request(item):\n   101\t            objects = [o['value'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or [] if frozen_universe.has(o['value'])]\n   102\t            shown = copy.deepcopy(extraction.shown_views(conn, frozen_cfg, item, objects))\n   103\t            owned_item = copy.deepcopy(item)\n   104\t            return owned_item, shown, extraction_key(frozen_cfg, owned_item, owned_item['text'], shown, frozen_universe)\n   105\t\n   106\t        def submit(item, owned_item, shown, key):\n   107\t            future = pool.submit(extraction.read_item, archive, frozen_cfg, owned_item, owned_item['text'], shown,\n   108\t                                 frozen_universe, transport=transport)      # the read; filing waits for the turn\n   109\t            pending[item['input_id']] = (key, item_key(owned_item), future, item)\n   110\t            prepared_futures.append((item['input_id'], future))\n   111\t            self._event(item['input_id'], 'prepared', request=key)\n   112\t\n   113\t        def fill():\n   114\t            nonlocal next_index\n   115\t            while next_index < len(items) and len(pending) < self.extraction_workers:\n   116\t                item, route = items[next_index]\n   117\t                next_index += 1\n   118\t                if route.resume_from and route.resume_from != 'extracted':\n   119\t                    continue  # The authoritative saved handover is owned by normal recovery.\n   120\t                submit(item, *current_request(item))\n   121\t\n   122\t        def refresh():\n   123\t            \"\"\"Re-prepare, right after a commit, every waiting request that commit changed; the turn still validates.\"\"\"\n   124\t            for input_id, (key, _, future, item) in list(pending.items()):\n   125\t                owned_item, shown, current = current_request(item)\n   126\t                if current != key:\n   127\t                    future.cancel()\n   128\t                    self._event(input_id, 'stale', before=key, request=current)\n   129\t                    submit(item, owned_item, shown, current)\n   130\t\n   131\t        def accepted_extraction(current_archive, current_cfg, item, text, shown, current_universe, *, transport=None):\n   132\t            prior_key, source_key, future, _ = pending[item['input_id']]\n   133\t            def validate_inputs():\n   134\t                if (environment_key(current_cfg, current_universe) != metadata['environment']\n   135\t                        or environment_key(cfg, universe) != metadata['environment'] or runtime_key() != metadata['runtime']):\n   136\t                    raise ValueError('configuration, universe or runtime changed during the day')\n   137\t                if item_key(item) != source_key or text != item['text']:\n   138\t                    raise ValueError('source changed after preparation')\n   139\t            validate_inputs()\n   140\t            current_key = extraction_key(current_cfg, item, text, shown, current_universe)\n   141\t            if current_key == prior_key:\n   142\t                reading = future.result()\n8:workers receive copies and write only the thread-safe call archive. Opt-in through `replay.run(day_runner=...)`;\n26:def digest(path):\n34:def environment_key(cfg, universe):\n38:def runtime_key():\n43:def item_key(item):\n47:def extraction_key(cfg, item, text, shown, universe):\n55:    def __init__(self, source_path, manifest_dir, *, extraction_workers=2, jev_workers=2):\n65:    def _event(self, input_id, event, **fields):\n68:    def _manifest(self, conn, cfg, universe, items, day):\n92:    def __call__(self, conn, archive, cfg, universe, items, *, day, transport=None, log=print):\n100:        def current_request(item):\n106:        def submit(item, owned_item, shown, key):\n113:        def fill():\n122:        def refresh():\n131:        def accepted_extraction(current_archive, current_cfg, item, text, shown, current_universe, *, transport=None):\n133:            def validate_inputs():\n159:                result = rounds.run(conn, archive, frozen_cfg, frozen_universe, item, route.sequence_no, resume_from=route.resume_from,\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:13:DIRECTIONS = ['first_is_bullish', 'last_is_bullish', 'same', 'opposite']\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:131:def openai_transport(provider, request, timeout=180, max_attempts=3):   # the default preserves the production retry behavior\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:251:def call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   448\t**The one next task: none open (D689, D690, 2026-11-20).** poc-v118 is the product (Alex chose A, D690), and the research line\n   449\trests until his new direction. The hybrid's release line is paused, and the judge and c8 lines are closed for now. A line reopens only\n   450\ton its condition below. No paid send is open, and D439 has $0 available without Alex's word.\n   451\t- **Production readiness (council P, consensus, $0; [RESULT.md](research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/RESULT.md)):** not ready for\n   452\t  a daily production test (no daily feed and start, no publishing of a finished day, no alerts), and no person has read poc-v118's own\n   453\t  output. Recommended to Alex: a $0 half-hour read of old-2's finished 09-20 store served locally; only on his yes, the daily wrapper\n   454\t  and a rehearsal week over 09-21..09-27. Alex said go (2026-11-20; his word in RESULT.md): step 1 is served on the host at http://127.0.0.1:8792\n   455\t  (API 8790, MCP 8791; `poc/data/review-v118-old2-0920-2026-11-20/README.md`, $0). Alex handed the read to the council (his words in\n   456\t  RESULT.md). Council Q (consensus, $0; [council-q/RESULT.md](research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-q/RESULT.md)): PARTLY.\n   457\t  An analyst would use it for sources and milestones, not for its number answers: linked number questions contradict each other in\n   458\t  all three draws (old-2: Data Center Q4 about $146B against a total Q4 of about $127B) because each question is judged alone; the\n   459\t  dependencies that link them are decided (D368 item 2) and not built. Recommended to Alex: no daily wrapper yet; open a judging\n   460\t  version with the decided dependencies, tested at $0 on the request text, then a few cents. Alex chose A (D691). The probe passed\n   461\t  its registered rule (D692, [RESULT.md](research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md), $0.0176): linked to\n   462\t  total revenue, 2 of 3 Data Center answers reconcile, unchanged 0 of 3; none of the six repeats the stored extreme, so the headline\n   463\t  example was partly one unlucky sample. Next ($0): the dependency design review (D542's five open items, the reads/supports\n   464\t  separation, D538's filing changes) with the council, then Alex; the self-made $414B reference traced apart.\n   465\t- **D689 (Alex chose option 1; council N closed both lines; record:\n   466\t  [council-n-codex.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.md), [council-n2-codex.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n2-codex.md)).**\n   467\t  - **Judge.** The carried previous conclusion holds rejected forecasts: on full evidence, 0 of 13 move with it and 8 of 13 without it,\n   468\t    with 0 of 8 controls moving.\n   469\t    - The readers jointly support 4 net repairs against the 5 required, including M14 in two of three old draws.\n   470\t    - The frozen gold reads 44.3 against 45.0, with China share regressed.\n   471\t    - It reopens on eight eligible failures on fresh questions, which the design never read and are counted once across draws, with\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nfor draw,center,total,seq,start in [(\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"v8\\\",\\\"v4\\\",62,\\\"2026-07-06\\\"),(\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",148,\\\"2026-07-10\\\"),(\\\"old-3\\\",\\\"v35\\\",\\\"v3\\\",932,\\\"2026-08-19\\\")]:\n p=root/draw/\\\"prod\\\"\n with db(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n  print(draw)\n  print(\\\"match at\\\",seq)\n  for record in c.execute(\\\"select call_id,shown_json,decisions_json,checks_json from match_records where seq=?\\\",(seq,)):\n   shown,decisions,checks=map(json.loads,record[1:])\n   print(\\\"shown\\\",shown[\\\"candidates\\\"])\n   for x in decisions[\\\"candidates\\\"]: print(x)\n   print(\\\"usage\\\",[(r[0],r[1],r[2],r[3]) for call in shown.get(\\\"requests\\\",[]) for r in a.execute(\\\"select model,purpose,input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(call[\\\"call_id\\\"],))])\n  for day,seq,jid,v,changed,num,out,cites in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,seq,judgement_id,view_id,changed,call_id,implied_outcome,cited_evidence_json from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day>=? order by judgement_id limit 10\\\",(center,total,start)):\n   print(day,seq,jid,v,changed,a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\", (num,)).fetchone(),out,cites)\n  v,= [center]\n  print(\\\"pair uncached cost per treatment entire window from date\\\",c.execute(\\\"select view_id,count(*) from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day>=? group by view_id\\\",(center,total,start)).fetchall())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nfor draw,center,total,seq,start in [(\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"v8\\\",\\\"v4\\\",62,\\\"2026-07-06\\\"),(\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",148,\\\"2026-07-10\\\"),(\\\"old-3\\\",\\\"v35\\\",\\\"v3\\\",932,\\\"2026-08-19\\\")]:\n p=root/draw/\\\"prod\\\"\n with db(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n  print(draw)\n  print(\\\"match at\\\",seq)\n  for record in c.execute(\\\"select call_id,shown_json,decisions_json,checks_json from match_records where seq=?\\\",(seq,)):\n   shown,decisions,checks=map(json.loads,record[1:])\n   print(\\\"shown\\\",shown[\\\"candidates\\\"])\n   for x in decisions[\\\"candidates\\\"]: print(x)\n   print(\\\"usage\\\",[(r[0],r[1],r[2],r[3]) for call in shown.get(\\\"requests\\\",[]) for r in a.execute(\\\"select model,purpose,input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(call[\\\"call_id\\\"],))])\n  for day,seq,jid,v,changed,num,out,cites in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,seq,judgement_id,view_id,changed,call_id,implied_outcome,cited_evidence_json from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day>=? order by judgement_id limit 10\\\",(center,total,start)):\n   print(day,seq,jid,v,changed,a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\", (num,)).fetchone(),out,cites)\n  v,= [center]\n  print(\\\"pair uncached cost per treatment entire window from date\\\",c.execute(\\\"select view_id,count(*) from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day>=? group by view_id\\\",(center,total,start)).fetchall())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1\nmatch at 62\nshown {'c1': ['v6', 'v7', 'v4', 'v5', 'v2', 'v1', 'v3']}\n{'id': 'c1', 'outcome': 'new', 'target_view_id': '', 'dependencies': [], 'reason': 'jev: v1: different 0.85; v2: different 0.87; v3: different 0.92; v4: part_of 1.00; v5: part_of 0.70; v6: different 0.61; v7: different 0.56; groups joined: none'}\nusage [('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 5036, 580), ('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 3278, 454), ('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 3277, 454)]\n2026-07-06 76 28 v4 1 (10186, 3868) Around $420 billion, in the low $400 billions: start from the $392 billion consensus reference, then allow a single-digit-percent gross uplift because SemiAnalysis's 20% upside applies only to roughly half-year second-half data-center compute revenue, a subset of total revenue. The delay/cancellation and China evidence temper that uplift but do not quantify an offset that moves the estimate below the reference. [\"e28\", \"e51\", \"e97\", \"e112\", \"e154\", \"e141\", \"e142\", \"e144\", \"e146\", \"e165\", \"e169\", \"e171\", \"e130\", \"e126\", \"e133\"]\n2026-07-06 76 30 v8 1 (1909, 1627) About $410 billion: starting with Q1 FY2027 revenue of $75.25 billion and carrying forward the reported 21% sequential growth for the next three quarters gives approximately $75.25B + $91.05B + $110.17B + $133.31B. This assumes the observed sequential growth continues and is not guidance. [\"e109\", \"e110\"]\n2026-07-07 98 36 v4 1 (12698, 2858) About $425 billion for FY2027: retain the prior roughly $420 billion central outlook supported by reported Q1 revenue and Q2 guidance, then allow a limited uplift for the $20 billion stand-alone CPU forecast because the planned fall launch leaves few selling quarters and shipments are not yet shown. The resulting estimate remains below $431.2 billion. [\"e28\", \"e51\", \"e97\", \"e111\", \"e112\", \"e127\", \"e64\", \"e65\", \"e74\", \"e141\", \"e144\", \"e146\", \"e165\", \"e169\", \"e171\"]\n2026-07-07 98 38 v8 1 (3207, 3058) About $410 billion: take Q1 FY2027 revenue of $75.25 billion, then carry its 21% sequential growth forward for Q2–Q4 ($91.1 billion, $110.2 billion, and $133.3 billion, respectively), for roughly $409.8 billion total. [\"e109\", \"e110\", \"e173\", \"e179\", \"e180\", \"e181\", \"e182\", \"e192\", \"e199\", \"e200\", \"e201\", \"e202\", \"e203\"]\n2026-07-08 124 45 v4 1 (17507, 4332) About $430 billion. Starting from the roughly $393 billion consensus, the reported $81.6 billion Q1 revenue and $91 billion Q2 guidance support a strong run-rate; applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% upside only to H2 data-center compute, rather than all revenue, implies an uplift that brings the total to roughly $430 billion. [\"e28\", \"e234\", \"e97\", \"e112\", \"e154\", \"e65\", \"e64\", \"e141\", \"e144\", \"e146\", \"e238\", \"e240\", \"e243\", \"e245\", \"e254\"]\n2026-07-08 124 47 v8 1 (5751, 3766) About $409.8 billion: starting from Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and carrying the reported 21% sequential growth forward for the next three quarters ($91.1 billion, $110.2 billion, and $133.3 billion). This is a trajectory-based forecast, not a company FY2027 revenue target. [\"e109\", \"e110\", \"e173\", \"e179\", \"e180\", \"e181\", \"e182\", \"e199\", \"e201\", \"e202\", \"e203\", \"e215\", \"e216\", \"e223\", \"e224\", \"e228\", \"e230\", \"e242\", \"e243\", \"e245\", \"e254\", \"e255\"]\n2026-07-09 147 52 v4 1 (21140, 3657) About $430 billion: start from the roughly $393 billion reference and apply SemiAnalysis’s 20% uplift only to the estimated H2 FY2027 data-center compute portion, adding roughly $37 billion rather than applying the uplift to total revenue. The resulting estimate is below the $431.2 billion rung-1 threshold. [\"e234\", \"e111\", \"e127\", \"e269\", \"e154\", \"e65\", \"e272\", \"e141\", \"e144\", \"e257\", \"e258\", \"e259\", \"e261\", \"e238\", \"e240\"]\n2026-07-09 147 54 v8 1 (6629, 3673) Carrying Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion forward at its reported 21% sequential growth rate for the remaining three quarters gives approximately $409.8 billion for FY2027. The unquantified Q2 acceleration guidance points above that baseline, implying at least $400 billion (rung 1) as the most likely outcome. [\"e109\", \"e110\", \"e179\", \"e180\", \"e181\", \"e182\", \"e199\", \"e201\", \"e202\", \"e203\", \"e215\", \"e216\", \"e223\", \"e224\", \"e225\", \"e228\", \"e230\", \"e242\", \"e243\", \"e245\", \"e254\", \"e255\", \"e262\", \"e263\", \"e267\", \"e271\"]\n2026-07-10 167 56 v4 1 (23358, 3381) About $430 billion: start from the roughly $393 billion consensus and add about $37 billion implied by SemiAnalysis’s 20% premium on H2 FY2027 data-center compute only, not on total revenue. The reported Rubin changes and other new risks are not sized into an FY2027 revenue reduction, so the evidence does not support a precise further adjustment. [\"e111\", \"e112\", \"e127\", \"e154\", \"e74\", \"e234\", \"e299\", \"e141\", \"e142\", \"e144\", \"e146\", \"e165\", \"e169\", \"e238\", \"e257\", \"e258\", \"e261\", \"e245\", \"e291\", \"e65\", \"e272\"]\n2026-07-10 167 58 v8 1 (8756, 4325) About $409.8 billion on a run-rate projection: $75.25 billion in Q1 carried forward at 21% sequential growth for the remaining quarters. Q2 guidance for faster Data Center growth points above that baseline, but provides no amount to quantify the additional upside. [\"e109\", \"e110\", \"e179\", \"e180\", \"e181\", \"e182\", \"e192\", \"e215\", \"e216\", \"e242\", \"e245\", \"e254\", \"e263\", \"e271\", \"e309\", \"e324\", \"e325\"]\npair uncached cost per treatment entire window from date [('v4', 76), ('v8', 75)]\nold-2\nmatch at 148\nshown {'c1': ['v9', 'v8', 'v1', 'v2', 'v5', 'v6', 'v4', 'v3', 'v12', 'v7']}\n{'id': 'c1', 'outcome': 'new', 'target_view_id': '', 'dependencies': [], 'reason': 'jev: v1: different 0.84; v10: different 0.95; v11: different 0.98; v12: different 0.97; v13: different 0.97; v2: different 0.85; v3: different 0.94; v4: different 0.97; v5: different 0.86; v6: different 0.83; v7: different 0.97; v8: part_of 0.80; v9: part_of 0.99; groups joined: none'}\nusage [('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 8621, 1123)]\n2026-07-10 167 59 v14 1 (1920, 972) About $393 billion for FY2027, using Bloomberg’s direct sales projection; this is below $400 billion and therefore falls in rung 3. [\"e195\"]\n2026-07-10 167 61 v9 1 (10475, 3440) About $357 billion for FY2027: apply the Q1 Data Center share of 92% to the $91 billion Q2 total-revenue guide to estimate roughly $83.8 billion of Q2 Data Center revenue, then carry forward the 11.5% sequential growth implied by total-revenue guidance for the remaining quarters. [\"e74\", \"e170\", \"e171\", \"e202\", \"e204\", \"e109\", \"e153\", \"e163\"]\n2026-07-11 172 69 v14 0 (2079, 1400) About $393 billion for FY2027, using Bloomberg's specific projection. The AI-lab demand share and supportive capex and export-policy themes add upside pressure, but state no FY2027 NVIDIA revenue adjustment, so they do not imply a figure above $400 billion. [\"e195\", \"e213\"]\n2026-07-12 186 73 v14 1 (4997, 3039) About $387 billion: starting with Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of approximately $91 billion, I carry the roughly 11.5% sequential increase forward to Q3 and Q4. This remains within rung 3 and below $400 billion. [\"e195\", \"e213\", \"e216\", \"e217\", \"e218\", \"e219\", \"e220\", \"e221\", \"e222\", \"e223\", \"e224\", \"e229\", \"e230\", \"e231\", \"e232\", \"e233\", \"e234\", \"e235\", \"e236\", \"e238\", \"e240\", \"e241\", \"e248\", \"e252\", \"e253\", \"e254\", \"e255\", \"e257\"]\n2026-07-12 186 77 v9 1 (11687, 4442) About $400–410B of FY2027 Data Center revenue. I use the Q1 $75.25B result and Q2 growth outlook as the operating base, then give partial—not full—weight to the roughly $1T Blackwell/Vera Rubin visibility across calendar 2026–27 because it spans multiple periods and products; the discounted estimate is just above the $400B rung boundary. [\"e74\", \"e170\", \"e171\", \"e202\", \"e162\", \"e163\", \"e153\", \"e156\", \"e116\", \"e159\"]\n2026-07-13 208 79 v14 1 (7615, 2986) Approximately $387 billion: Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion followed by Q2 guidance of $91 billion implies about 11.5% sequential growth; carrying that growth through Q3 and Q4 gives roughly $101.5 billion and $113.2 billion, respectively. [\"e195\", \"e238\", \"e240\", \"e220\", \"e221\", \"e222\", \"e231\", \"e232\", \"e252\", \"e253\", \"e284\"]\n2026-07-13 208 82 v9 1 (12096, 3162) About $415B of FY2027 Data Center revenue: the guide-derived sequential-growth run-rate is about $356B, but Q1's 21% sequential segment growth, management's Q2 acceleration statement, and quantified 2027 hyperscaler spending and demand evidence imply a discounted uplift of roughly $59B. This is below the $450B rung-1 boundary. [\"e74\", \"e170\", \"e171\", \"e201\", \"e202\", \"e255\", \"e109\", \"e153\", \"e156\", \"e158\", \"e165\", \"e227\", \"e289\", \"e293\", \"e294\", \"e296\", \"e297\", \"e116\", \"e117\"]\n2026-07-14 243 93 v14 1 (11402, 2328) About $387 billion: starting with reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of $91 billion, carry the approximately 11.5% sequential increase into Q3 and Q4, yielding about $101.5 billion and $113.2 billion, respectively. [\"e195\", \"e238\", \"e240\", \"e234\", \"e220\", \"e222\", \"e221\", \"e252\", \"e321\", \"e231\", \"e376\", \"e379\"]\n2026-07-14 243 98 v9 1 (13805, 5757) About $420B of FY2027 Data Center revenue. The guided Q2 total and Q1 segment mix imply a roughly $356B run-rate baseline when guided sequential growth is carried forward; Q1’s 21% sequential Data Center growth, management’s stated Q2 acceleration, and demand evidence justify an uplift, but not to $450B. [\"e74\", \"e170\", \"e171\", \"e202\", \"e255\", \"e162\", \"e163\", \"e294\", \"e295\", \"e296\", \"e297\", \"e304\", \"e289\", \"e116\", \"e227\", \"e357\", \"e358\", \"e360\"]\n2026-07-15 274 108 v14 1 (15165, 2046) About $387 billion: Q1 revenue was $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance is $91 billion, an approximately 11.5% sequential increase. Carrying that growth forward gives roughly $101.5 billion in Q3 and $113.2 billion in Q4, for about $387.3 billion total. [\"e195\", \"e238\", \"e240\", \"e456\", \"e459\", \"e408\", \"e220\", \"e222\", \"e321\"]\npair uncached cost per treatment entire window from date [('v14', 71), ('v9', 70)]\nold-3\nmatch at 932\nshown {'c1': ['v3', 'v14', 'v30', 'v2', 'v4', 'v21', 'v6', 'v7', 'v31', 'v15']}\n{'id': 'c1', 'outcome': 'new', 'target_view_id': '', 'dependencies': [], 'reason': 'jev: v1: different 0.94; v10: different 0.96; v11: different 0.96; v12: different 0.97; v13: different 0.98; v14: different 0.80; v15: different 0.81; v16: different 0.96; v17: different 0.95; v18: different 0.95; v19: different 0.95; v2: different 0.92; v20: different 0.99; v21: different 0.89; v23: different 0.91; v24: different 0.96; v25: different 0.96; v26: different 0.95; v27: different 0.95; v28: different 0.90; v29: different 0.97; v3: part_of 1.00; v30: different 0.69; v31: same_matter_different_quantity 0.66; v32: different 0.86; v33: different 0.97; v34: different 0.95; v4: part_of 0.84; v5: different 0.97; v6: different 0.71; v7: different 0.55; v8: different 0.95; v9: different 0.97; groups joined: none'}\nusage [('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 19280, 2731), ('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 3492, 461), ('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 3701, 458), ('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 7096, 934), ('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 6722, 931), ('jev-1.14.0', 'match', 3470, 465)]\n2026-08-19 948 620 v3 1 (23572, 3677) Q1 actual revenue of $81.6 billion, Q2 guidance of $91 billion, the Q3 estimate of $103.1 billion, and about 12% sequential growth into Q4 imply a baseline around $391–$392 billion. Applying the carried estimate of 20% upside to second-half Data Center compute adds roughly $40 billion, implying total FY2027 revenue around $431–$433 billion. [\"e25\", \"e818\", \"e221\", \"e97\", \"e98\", \"e1812\", \"e60\", \"e1116\", \"e2334\", \"e2089\", \"e2296\", \"e733\", \"e2142\", \"e522\", \"e2143\", \"e1054\", \"e2341\"]\n2026-08-19 948 623 v35 1 (2538, 1296) $361 billion for FY2027: Morningstar explicitly estimates that figure, citing FY2026 data-center revenue of $194 billion and 86% annual growth. The estimate sits exactly at rung 2’s lower boundary and below rung 1’s $400 billion threshold. [\"e2295\"]\n2026-08-20 958 644 v3 1 (20195, 2427) Roughly $434–$437 billion: carry forward the prior $391–$392 billion quarterly baseline plus about $40 billion from the estimated 20% second-half Data Center compute upside, then add about $3–$4 billion for BofA’s $94–$95 billion Q2 forecast versus the $91 billion guide midpoint. The higher Q3 expectation is not added separately because it overlaps the second-half tracking uplift. [\"e97\", \"e98\", \"e60\", \"e1116\", \"e1812\", \"e1957\", \"e2142\", \"e2296\", \"e2329\", \"e2362\"]\n2026-08-20 958 645 v35 1 (2961, 2131) Around $361 billion with an unquantified modest upward tilt: the China shipment reports add potential revenue, but give no sales value from which to calculate a larger increment. That remains below the $400 billion rung-1 threshold. [\"e2295\", \"e2389\", \"e2390\", \"e2391\", \"e2392\"]\n2026-08-21 977 675 v3 1 (21628, 4170) Approximately $432–436 billion: applying the roughly $40 billion implied second-half Data Center compute upside from SemiAnalysis to the roughly $392 billion annual reference, with BofA's Q2 estimate adding about $3–4 billion versus guidance, while avoiding a separate overlapping Q3 addition. [\"e25\", \"e221\", \"e818\", \"e97\", \"e98\", \"e1957\", \"e60\", \"e1116\", \"e2362\", \"e1812\", \"e2296\", \"e2089\", \"e2334\", \"e733\", \"e1132\", \"e522\", \"e1054\"]\n2026-08-21 977 679 v35 1 (3566, 2595) Around the high-$300 billions, anchored on Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate with some upside from reported China shipments and demand evidence. The supplied evidence does not quantify an FY2027 increase of at least $39 billion, so the implied figure remains below $400 billion. [\"e2295\", \"e2389\", \"e2390\", \"e2391\", \"e2392\", \"e2404\", \"e2415\", \"e2416\", \"e2417\"]\n2026-08-22 980 685 v3 1 (20073, 3019) About $432–436 billion: apply SemiAnalysis's 20% upside to second-half FY2027 Data Center compute, implying roughly $40 billion above the $392 billion consensus, then include about $3–4 billion for BofA's $94–95 billion Q2 forecast versus the roughly $91 billion guide/consensus. This is a forecast, not an established result, and sits just above the $431.2 billion rung-1 boundary. [\"e25\", \"e97\", \"e98\", \"e60\", \"e1116\", \"e2362\", \"e2296\", \"e522\", \"e733\", \"e1132\", \"e59\", \"e1073\"]\n2026-08-22 980 688 v35 1 (3674, 2398) About $372 billion: apply the reported 92% Q1 FY2027 year-over-year growth rate to the cited $194 billion FY2026 revenue base ($194B × 1.92). [\"e2295\", \"e2389\", \"e2390\", \"e2391\", \"e2392\", \"e2404\", \"e2415\", \"e2416\", \"e2417\", \"e2445\"]\n2026-08-23 991 714 v3 1 (19566, 4178) About $438–440 billion: start from the $392 billion FY2027 estimate, add roughly $40 billion implied by SemiAnalysis’s 20% second-half Data Center compute upside, and allow about $6–8 billion for BofA’s Q2 and following-quarter estimates above the respective consensus figures. [\"e25\", \"e60\", \"e97\", \"e98\", \"e1116\", \"e2296\", \"e2089\", \"e2362\", \"e2480\", \"e2142\", \"e733\", \"e522\", \"e2051\", \"e2334\", \"e1812\", \"e2479\", \"e2379\", \"e2380\"]\n2026-08-23 991 737 v35 1 (3709, 3082) About $372 billion for FY2027: carry the reported 92% year-over-year Q1 FY2027 growth forward across the $194 billion FY2026 base ($194 billion × 1.92). [\"e2295\", \"e2389\", \"e2390\", \"e2391\", \"e2392\", \"e2404\", \"e2415\", \"e2416\", \"e2417\", \"e2445\"]\npair uncached cost per treatment entire window from date [('v3', 33), ('v35', 32)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
