{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md | sed -n '260,316p'\nrg -n 'judging|matching|version' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md | head -30\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/identity.py | sed -n '74,115p'\nrg -n 'test_.*(dependen|cycle|resume|theme|follows|closing)' tests --glob '*.py' | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md | sed -n '260,316p'\nrg -n 'judging|matching|version' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md | head -30\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/identity.py | sed -n '74,115p'\nrg -n 'test_.*(dependen|cycle|resume|theme|follows|closing)' tests --glob '*.py' | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"   260\t## 8. The first proof on stored data (`separation_proof.py`, `separated_edges.py`), $0\n   261\t\n   262\tThe seam replaces three functions of the store for the life of the proof (what judging reads, what a change queues, what\n   263\tfiling reads); no package file changes. 35 registered expectations hold; the script exits with an error otherwise.\n   264\t\n   265\t- **A. The unseeded fresh week with the `reads` edge \"data-center revenue reads total revenue\".** Every one of the 235 stored\n   266\t  readings filed again by the production entry point equals the stored filing: the company-wide outlook (`e22`) and the six\n   267\t  other statements keep their total-revenue home. From the stored state before the last day's round (rebuilt, equal to the\n   268\t  stored run): total revenue is judged before data-center revenue; the data-center request is the stored one plus the block\n   269\t  with total revenue's conclusion of that round and the closing sentence; every other judgement equals the stored one, the\n   270\t  unrelated pair included; the judge's check accepts the citation; the reverse edge is refused as a cycle.\n   271\t- **B. A stored seeded draw (17 `supports` edges).** Every one of its 243 stored readings filed again equals the stored filing\n   272\t  (the narrowest rule reads the edges as before). The last day's round, dry with labelled fakes, 14 calls when no conclusion\n   273\t  changes and 18 when all do: each supporter is judged before the question it supports and shown there; no question is shown\n   274\t  one it supports.\n   275\t- **C. Circles across the two kinds**, on the seeded state: a `reads` edge that would let data-center revenue and total revenue\n   276\t  read each other is refused; one that closes no circle (the Vera CPU question reading the Rubin shipping question) is written,\n   277\t  ordered before the questions that read it, gives filing no narrower home, and its opposite is then refused.\n   278\t\n   279\tPositive controls: with the edge read as the code reads it today, 13 expectations fail (the seven filings among them); with\n   280\tevery edge taken as `reads`, 12 fail (the seeded filing, the seeded order, the circle).\n   281\t\n   282\tThis first proof inserts its edges with a helper and derives the kind from the writers' marks; it shows the labelled examples\n   283\tA, B and C and nothing about a stored kind.\n   284\t\n   285\t## 9. The second proof (`separation_proof_2.py`), $0: the production writers, a whole week, the edge combinations, old rows\n   286\t\n   287\t20 registered expectations hold. The two production writers are wrapped so that each stores the kind of the edges it writes\n   288\t(in a side table on the scratch store); the readers read the stored kind.\n   289\t\n   290\t- **W1. The seeding module** on an empty store writes 17 edges, each stored as `supports`; filing reads them as the code does\n   291\t  today for every question; judging reads them the other way.\n   292\t- **W2. The unseeded fresh week, whole, with one change, and the data-center question's stored answers forced back**: at the\n   293\t  article that opened the data-center revenue question the matching answer names total revenue as a dependency. The production\n   294\t  check accepts it and the production writer writes the edge, stored as `reads`. The week then replays from its stored answers:\n   295\t  every reading and matching answer comes from the archive; questions, statements, the 449 links and all 235 filings equal the\n   296\t  stored run; every judgement of every other question equals the stored one. The only requests the archive does not hold are\n   297\t  the data-center question's seven judgements; each is the stored request of that day plus the block with total revenue's\n   298\t  conclusion of the same round (its first 600 characters) and the closing sentence, with total revenue judged first each day.\n   299\t  Those seven are answered by handing back the stored answer of the day. **These are not the seven requests a live judge would\n   300\t  produce**: a changed first answer changes the next day's previous conclusion, the statements carried forward and the change\n   301\t  flag. A real test would run each arm as a sequence from its own earlier answers; isolated sends of these seven requests would\n   302\t  answer another question (council round 31).\n   303\t- **X. The combinations of 2.2** on the seeded state: `reads` (total revenue, data-center revenue) on top of the `supports` edge\n   304\t  that already gives that reading is not written and is reported as a label that cannot be compared; `reads` (data-center\n   305\t  revenue, total revenue) is refused as a circle; a `reads` edge that closes no circle is written with its kind, its opposite\n   306\t  refused, its repeat with the same label not written, the same pair with another label refused as a conflict; filing's\n   307\t  reading is the same after all of it.\n   308\t- **M. Old rows**: the inventory of 2.3; a row of neither writer without a stored kind is refused.\n   309\t\n   310\tPositive controls: with the edge read as the code reads it today the week stops on 2026-09-23 at the first article whose\n   311\tstatement loses its total-revenue link (a matching request the archive does not hold); with duplicates written three\n   312\texpectations fail; with the writers storing no kind four fail.\n   313\t\n   314\tWhat the two proofs do not show: what a judge does with the line (no model was asked); a stored-kind implementation in the\n   315\tpackage (the kind lives in a side table of the harness); closing, successors and the later addition; the pages and the idea\n   316\troute under the rule; anything about how a dependency would be chosen, or any benefit to an answer.\n12:  - D538: one stored edge has two readers: judging (whose conclusion to read) and filing (`narrowest_links`: the reader becomes the\n18:  from an article, matching \"chooses a new thesis's dependencies, stating which conclusions it relies on\"; `reads` edges in\n26:    later one removed) rebuilds the stored request **byte-equal** (sha256) through `judging.build_prompt` and `model.build_request`\n    74\tdef batch_plan(candidates, outcomes):\n    75\t    \"\"\"Resolve same-answer duplicates and validate dependencies on the resulting identities before retry ends.\"\"\"\n    76\t    aliases, first_by_key, errors = {}, {}, []\n    77\t    for candidate in candidates:\n    78\t        cid = candidate['id']\n    79\t        outcome = outcomes.get(cid, ('skip', None, []))\n    80\t        if outcome[0] not in ('new', 'succession'):\n    81\t            continue\n    82\t        key = automatic_key(candidate)\n    83\t        first = first_by_key.setdefault(key, cid) if key is not None else cid\n    84\t        aliases[cid] = first\n    85\t        if outcome[:2] != outcomes[first][:2]:\n    86\t            errors.append(f'candidate {cid}: same-key succession conflicts with {first}')\n    87\t    graph, directions = {}, {}\n    88\t    for cid, first in aliases.items():\n    89\t        for dep in outcomes[cid][2]:\n    90\t            target = aliases.get(dep['view_id'], dep['view_id'])\n    91\t            chain = aliases.get(dep['wait_chain_view_id'], dep['wait_chain_view_id'])\n    92\t            edge = (first, target, chain, dep['wait_year'])\n    93\t            if edge in directions and directions[edge] != dep['direction']:\n    94\t                errors.append(f'candidate {cid}: same-key dependency direction conflicts')\n    95\t            directions[edge] = dep['direction']\n    96\t            if target:\n    97\t                graph.setdefault(first, set()).add(target)\n    98\t    for cid in graph:\n    99\t        stack, seen = list(graph[cid]), set()\n   100\t        while stack:\n   101\t            target = stack.pop()\n   102\t            if target == cid:\n   103\t                errors.append(f'candidate {cid}: coalesced dependencies lead back to itself')\n   104\t                break\n   105\t            if target not in seen:\n   106\t                seen.add(target)\n   107\t                stack.extend(graph.get(target, ()))\n   108\t    return aliases, errors\ntests/test_idea.py:682:def test_the_service_pick_follows_the_models_direct_label(ledger, items, index, tmp_path):\ntests/test_supported_versions.py:14:from test_theme_block import DAY, ledger  # noqa: E402\ntests/test_not_judged_bundle.py:96:def test_through_the_library_the_question_and_its_parts_appear_from_its_creation_day_and_stay_after_closing(tmp_path):\ntests/test_sequential_replay.py:95:def test_failure_stops_later_extraction_and_resume_keeps_sequence(tmp_path):\ntests/test_one_decider.py:16:from test_theme_block import ASSET_RUNGS, ledger  # noqa: E402\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:9:from test_theme_block import ASSET_RUNGS, DAY, ledger\ntests/test_english.py:195:def test_waiting_dependency_resolves_across_year_spellings(tmp_path):\ntests/test_evidence_in_view.py:7:from test_theme_block import ASSET_RUNGS, DAY, ledger\ntests/test_identity_repair.py:86:def test_coalesced_dependency_is_refused_before_matching_retry_ends(tmp_path):\ntests/test_identity_repair.py:122:def test_writer_failure_resumes_from_same_handover_without_partial_rows(tmp_path):\ntests/test_identity_repair.py:159:def test_failed_replay_day_is_not_completed_and_can_resume(tmp_path):\ntests/test_seeding.py:18:def test_seeding_writes_every_question_once_with_key_ladder_switch_and_dependency(tmp_path):\ntests/test_pull.py:37:def test_a_closing_on_a_day_without_items_is_dated_on_that_day_not_the_day_before(tmp_path):\ntests/test_theme_block.py:62:def test_an_asset_request_lists_open_judged_theme_theses_and_marks_what_changed_since_its_last_judgement(tmp_path):\ntests/test_theme_block.py:83:def test_theme_pushes_are_checked_against_the_block_stored_and_served(tmp_path):\ntests/test_theme_block.py:111:def test_a_round_judges_themes_first_and_a_changed_theme_queues_every_open_asset_thesis_once(tmp_path):\ntests/test_theme_block.py:134:def test_resumed_round_recovers_what_an_earlier_commit_queued(tmp_path):\ntests/test_theme_block.py:152:def test_theme_pushes_are_checked_against_the_block_the_request_carried(tmp_path):\ntests/test_theme_block.py:167:def test_a_ledger_written_before_the_theme_block_gains_the_column_when_opened_for_writing(tmp_path):\ntests/test_theme_block.py:204:def test_the_request_names_the_closed_set_for_cites_views_when_no_dependency_is_listed(tmp_path):\ntests/test_concurrency.py:73:def test_earlier_failure_accepts_no_later_handover_and_resume_preserves_order(tmp_path):\ntests/test_concurrency.py:88:def test_writer_failure_resumes_the_accepted_handover_without_reextracting(tmp_path):\ntests/test_jev_concurrency.py:30:def test_independent_jobs_overlap_but_decisions_and_hashes_keep_input_order(tmp_path):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '1256,1285p;2503,2524p;2538,2550p;3049,3068p;3084,3107p'\nrg -n 'def (view|close_view|is_open)|view_switches' src/hivemind/views/store.py\nrg -n 'live_lock.acquire|acquire\\\\(' scripts/replay.py scripts/run* src/hivemind --glob '*.py' | head -45\nrg -n 'revers|opposit|same' docs/prd/06-views.md | head -20\nnl -ba scripts/replay.py | sed -n '35,106p'\nnl -ba poc/ui/src/adapters/bundle.js | sed -n '152,177p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1256\t## D51 · 2026-10-21 · Claude's open items settled: one re-judging rule, dependencies chosen in the matching call, no consensus\n  1257\t\n  1258\t- By: Alex, item by item. Asked which items were his to decide, he had Claude re-check the twelve open items Claude\n  1259\t  had written in, against the latest design (\"for yourself to reiterate the issue in case you made stupid mistakes that\n  1260\t  are not issues anymore in the latest version\"). Then: \"好，一个一个来问我\" (the nine no longer issues dropped); on\n  1261\t  re-judging, \"A 可以但是设计逻辑要干净点；你思考下和我说\", then \"ok\"; on which views dependencies are chosen from,\n  1262\t  \"ok\"; on consensus, \"What … is a consensus that you're talking about … Every time the evidence updates or whatever,\n  1263\t  the ladder needs to be run by the model to determine whether it's going to shift from neutral to bearish or from\n  1264\t  neutral to bullish … That's the logic\"; then \"可以你再仔细的对齐一次逻辑\". On the page: \"那你 FE 为什么写定稿了，这不是瞎写吗？\"\n  1265\t- Decides:\n  1266\t  1. Re-judging has one rule: a view is re-judged when what it reads changed. It reads its own evidence and the\n  1267\t     conclusions (state and reasons) of the views it depends on. Its evidence changed when new evidence came or\n  1268\t     evidence was replaced (a repeat alone does not count); a dependency's conclusion changed when that view's\n  1269\t     judgement says so. Every judgement answers \"结论变不变\" in its fixed form: changed when the rung moved or a key fact\n  1270\t     or number behind the state changed (AMZN's capex guidance from +12% to +25% inside one rung), unchanged when the\n  1271\t     same thing is said again. Code checks only that a judgement that moved a rung, and the first judgement of a new\n  1272\t     view, say changed. This gives Alex's \"如果美联储有重大的改动……确实需要重判\" (log step 10) to the model and\n  1273\t     replaces the notice on a rung change only. A waiting view just built, and a dependency moving to its successor,\n  1274\t     are cases of the same rule, so B is re-judged when its arrow moves to the next period (one of the details dropped\n  1275\t     in D46 item 9, back as a case of this rule, as Claude told Alex before his \"ok\").\n  1276\t  2. A new view's dependencies are chosen in the matching call (step 4), from the views the model already has in front\n  1277\t     of it: the search results, the views listed in prompt part 5, and the views new in the same item; there is no\n  1278\t     other search. In step 5 code checks that each is one of the views shown (or a year it waits for) and that no loop\n  1279\t     forms. Writing into the views database has seven steps. Config holds two settings for the views database's model\n  1280\t     calls (matching, re-judging), no longer a separate one for dependencies. A dependency on a view in none of the three\n  1281\t     is missed, like a match the search misses; the records and the labels show it.\n  1282\t  3. Consensus is not part of the design: a view has one state, judged by the model from its evidence whenever that\n  1283\t     evidence changes (D46 item 1). The glossary row, the views notes and extraction's \"用来算共识\" go. Third-party views\n  1284\t     stay evidence of their tier.\n  1285\t  4. Open items are only what Alex deferred: how search ranks; the granularity of views, researched first (how many\n  2503\t## D191 · 2026-10-26 · Theme theses reach every company; no named dependant is required to open one\n  2504\t\n  2505\t- On the theme-dependency design (`docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md`), Alex decided the four points:\n  2506\t  1. A theme candidate does **not** have to name the company thesis it feeds. Alex: \"我觉得这个非常难，有时候一个政策影响非常的广，你这种做法基本不可行，不可能所有的公司都 map 到，你可以默认这些宏观的东西和所有公司都有影响，我觉得这个 1 to all mapping 比较 make sense，至于这个 thesis 的 state 对每个不同公司的影响需要别的方法来判断\". Decided: a theme thesis is context for every company thesis (one to all); how its state bears on each company is decided when that company's thesis is judged, not by an edge written at extraction. Explicit dependencies stay for the cases a document states (a company thesis on another thesis), and may be added to an existing thesis later (point 2).\n  2507\t  2. A dependency may be added to an existing thesis by a later item (\"可以\").\n  2508\t  3. From a macro-only item, a theme opens only when the theme is in the universe's list (\"是\"); an unlisted theme waits for a company item.\n  2509\t  4. `industry_aggregate` is renamed `shared_quantity`: a quantity or price outside any one company that several move on (\"好\").\n  2510\t- Consequences for the design, to be worked before any build: the judge of a company thesis reads the current state and reasons of the open theme theses of the themes its items were tagged with (block of the judging request), and states the sign it applies; a changed theme conclusion does not fan out to every company thesis in the same round (06-views: a repeated Fed statement must not trigger hundreds), it is read at each thesis's next judgement; proceedings that move no line are kept out by the admission test on themes (the model's judgement), not by a missing edge. The `feeds` field of the design is withdrawn for themes.\n  2511\t\n  2512\t## D192 · 2026-10-26 · Role v13 (tests instead of lists) fails its probe; wording is exhausted as a lever\n  2513\t\n  2514\t- Alex: \"接着做下一步，不要 scope creep, just solve the core problems on improving quality for the extraction\". Role v13 replaced the four category definitions and the ban list by the labeller's three tests (swing, independence, loss), added the first-contact rule (two to four questions for a company with no thesis shown) and named quarterly or run-rate statements as evidence; 7,580 characters against v12's 7,458.\n  2515\t- Probe ([role_probe.py](research/2026-10-26-thesis-admission-v12/role_probe.py), `poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/role-probe/`): the gold's 20 items re-sent with the stored v12 request's user message and v13's system prompt and schema, three samples each, sifted and scored at the candidate level against the gold's must-open and must-not-open keys; the stored v12 answers of two runs (r3, r4) are the controls. Must-open keys proposed: v12 9/15 and 8/15, v13 26/45 (8.7 per sample); must-not-open keys proposed: v12 0 and 1, v13 11/174 (3.7 per sample: a tax-rate thesis from the press release in two samples, a Taiwan proceeding in two, a run-rate thesis); candidates 30, 30, 33 per sample. $0.09.\n  2516\t- Read: the tests moved two cases the right way (the Helios milestone 3/3 against 1/3; the Ohio guarantee 2/3 against 0/2) and others the wrong way (the press release and the proceeding); coverage did not rise. The consistent misses (a numeric China-revenue thesis 0/5, Microsoft's capex 1/5, AMD's data-center FY2026 line) are judgements the model makes the same way under both wordings, not a reading of a list. Not adopted; `poc-v27` stays a configuration.\n  2517\t- A narrower v14 (role-v12 plus only the milestone clause the Helios gain came from, the D191 rename and the D185 exception, minus the peripherals sentence) is probed the same way; result appended here. Result: worse than v12 in the other direction: must-open keys proposed 14/45 (4.7 per sample against 9 and 8), candidates 17 per sample against 30; the February 25 call opened neither data-center revenue nor gross margin in any of three samples (two candidates each), while Helios rose to 2/3 and Ohio to 1/3. Twenty-five characters of wording moved coverage by half. Not adopted; `poc-v28` stays a configuration.\n  2518\t- Decided: role v12 stays. Two audited wordings moved the extractor in opposite directions on the same items; the extractor's behaviour is more sensitive to wording than to meaning, and a single sample at temperature 0.2 is the unit being measured. The levers that remain are structural, each Alex's call: (1) show the current view in block 5 so the swing test has an input; (2) sample the extraction three times and keep the candidates a majority proposes (identity by typed key), which turns the variance into a vote at three times the extraction cost (about +$1.7 over this window); (3) the first-contact pass as its own call on a company's first item. None is built here.\n  2519\t Beyond that, the remaining lever for extraction is not wording: the extractor never sees the current view (05-extraction block 5 shows question, focus and due date only), which is the input the swing test needs (trace review §5).\n  2520\t\n  2521\t## D193 · 2026-10-26 · Extraction coverage is at the model's steady state; the phase closes on v12 with the collision judge\n  2522\t\n  2523\t- Alex: \"太贵了抽 N 次 … 其他的点你自己深度思考啊 … 你深度的研究思考小范围尝试，给我结果让我清晰的做决策\". Sampling several times per item is ruled out on cost.\n  2524\t- Two structural arms probed on the gold's 20 items with the stored v12 user messages, three samples each ($0.22): extraction at `reasoning_effort: medium` (configuration only) and block 5 carrying each shown thesis's current rung and last reasons. Neither moves coverage: 8.3 of 15 must-open keys per sample against 9 and 8 for the two stored v12 runs; medium reasoning proposes fewer candidates (25 against 30) at 1.8× the time; the view block adds a little clutter (1.7 against 0–1). With D192's v13 and v14, five arms give the same picture: the gold's must-open coverage is the model's steady state on these texts, about 8–9 of 15, and the six misses are the same judgements under every arm.\n  2538\t## D195 · 2026-10-26 · The theme block: every asset thesis is judged with the open theme theses in view, and a changed theme conclusion reaches them in the same round\n  2539\t\n  2540\t- Alex: \"做，先零成本数完再改；然后你得确认这个架构和逻辑是对的\", then on the one open choice \"A 但是仔细思考怎么做才是正确的\". Census and design: `docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md` §8 (`theme_block_census.py`; Codex read-only review, 12 findings, each read against the code, §8.8).\n  2541\t- What the ledgers said ($0): every company judgement would carry a block (175 of 175 in r4, 2–6 theme lines); the narrow reading by item tags shows a block in 14 of 175, so Alex's one-to-all rule is the only one with data; in 9 judgements the theme was judged after the company thesis in the same round; without propagation 109 of 228 theme changes are never read inside the window; with it, 141 more judgement calls, about $0.24 on the window.\n  2542\t- Decided (A): under `judging-v4` (`poc-v29`) an asset thesis's request carries `[Themes in force]`: every open theme thesis with a current state, its rung, the reasons of its last judgement and whether it changed since this thesis was last judged; the answer carries `theme_pushes` (view id, push in the evidence-push vocabulary), checked by code against the block and stored as `judgements.theme_pushes_json`, served as `theme_pushes`. Theme theses are judged before asset theses in a round; a theme judgement that says changed queues every open asset thesis with evidence in force, once per round, the rule explicit dependants follow (`changed` is the PRD's filter: a repeat does not fire it, a facts-only change does). The round's queue is derived from the ledger (the day's changed views, the dependants of views judged at this sequence number with a changed conclusion, the asset theses a changed theme queued), which also closes a hole the review found: a round interrupted after some judgements committed lost what they had queued. Everything is gated on the prompt version; v3 ledgers replay unchanged.\n  2543\t- This replaces the consequence note under D191 (\"a changed theme conclusion does not fan out to every company thesis in the same round\"): that sentence was the assistant's, and the census priced both sides. Explicit dependencies, D191 point 2 and the UI are unchanged. A theme conclusion is never evidence (06-views) and is never cited in `cites`.\n  2544\t- Three r4 asset theses re-judged once under v4 ($0.009, `poc/reports/2026-10-26-theme-block/resend-three.txt`): the signs read as an analyst would give them (hyperscaler capex toward the bullish end for NVIDIA data-center revenue, AMD data-center growth and TSMC revenue; the H200 permission toward it for NVIDIA; the overseas-computing restriction away; a tungsten-scrap allocation ignored by all three). One replay of the window under `poc-v29` (r5) measures it beside r4; adoption as the replay default waits for that measurement.\n  2545\t\n  2546\t## D196 · 2026-10-27 · `poc-v29` (the theme block) is the replay default\n  2547\t\n  2548\t- Measured once over the r4 window (`poc/reports/2026-10-26-theme-block/results.md`): 245 asset judgements carried the block, 194 named a theme push with signs that follow each thesis's own ladder; propagation added 121 judgements (+$0.20) and changed a conclusion one time in ten; reasons read the same or better on the five theses with the same question in both ledgers; one judge call in 307 ran out of output on the largest thesis and answered on resume. The whole run cost $1.46 against $1.21 with cached input at its published rate ($1.59 against $1.33 with every input token at the input rate; the cost column priced cached input at the full rate until 2026-10-27, build-log row 57).\n  2549\t- Decided: `scripts/replay.py` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v29.json`; `poc-v26` stays as the control configuration. Not built: the block on the UI; a tighter aggregate-theme identity (the near-duplicate aggregates each take a line in every block).\n  2550\t\n  3049\t## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n  3050\t\n  3051\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\n  3052\t- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \"remains\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \"is not fact\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \"be precise about what is established\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \"established\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\n  3053\t- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\n  3054\t- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n  3055\t\n  3056\t## D261 · 2026-11-02 · A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again\n  3057\t\n  3058\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, while the judgement ruler (D3) was being built: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重，我需要你记录到我们的决策和原则里面，我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\".\n  3059\t- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the \"假的测量\" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.\n  3060\t- Decided (his words; written at the decision it governs, AGENTS §7.1): once a ruler and its gold have been reviewed (readers who did not write them read them against the decisions; Alex signed), neither the definition nor the gold changes again. A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold (`corrections-*.json`), printed with every score and never merged in. A new definition is a new version that only his decision opens, with its own gold derived from scratch; old scores stay as they were and are never compared with the new. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored against it before.\n  3061\t- What is locked by this record: the extraction standard page (`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, version 3 signed D243, with D250's four boundaries and counting unit) and `golden-v5/` (sha256 in `golden-v5.sha256`): no version 6; the loop's desk ruler (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/README.md`, D1–D3). What is still under construction and locks at his review: the judgement ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md`, its reader brief, question list and gold `gold-v1.json` (the sign-off is a separate record).\n  3062\t\n  3063\t## D262 · 2026-11-02 · The judgement ruler (D3) and its gold are fixed: the gold is reader B's answers; frozen at sha256 636c056d1e4252fa…\n  3064\t\n  3065\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, after reading the two readers' reasoning on every disagreement (readers A and B differed on 3 of 23 questions by range or yes/no and on 12 of 20 direction labels; the system disagreed with the draft on the total revenue and Vera CPU questions in every draw): \"那就不要理A了；我们就go with B 好吧，定下尺子金表\".\n  3066\t- Fixed by that decision: the ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md` (unit: a gold question at the window end 2026-07-14; material: golden-v5's 309 items by sha; a numeric question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match; the two null baselines printed with every score); the question list and the must_open mapping as built (`questions-v1.json`, 22 seeds + the Ohio guarantee); the gold `gold-v1.json` = reader B's 23 answers verbatim (B: a fresh-context Claude reader, model-authored, 3 questions marked no material: CoWoS capacity, semiconductor growth, SK Telecom), sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2` in `gold-v1.sha256` and in `score_judgement.py`, which refuses any other. Reader A (Codex) stays beside it as the control record (`reader-A.json`, `reconcile-v1.md`): its distance from B is the stick's own noise. Claude's two proposals of the afternoon (a three-level score when readers split; toss-up questions excluded) were not adopted: one range per question, every question counts. From here D261 applies: nothing in the ruler or the gold changes; a defect is a dated record in `corrections-v1.json`.\n  3067\t- First measurement on the frozen gold (`score-r4-identity.txt`, arm 4, three draws, judging-v5): judged questions agreeing 13/19, 15/18, 12/17; the lookup baseline (the rung containing the gold's reference figure) 9/15, 8/14, 8/14; always-neutral 5/11, 5/10, 5/10. Disagreeing in every draw: FY2027 total revenue (gold $400–435 billion, judge neutral by consensus lookup) and Vera CPU revenue (gold $8–18 billion, judge the top rung on management's $20 billion at face value); in two of three: the financing-commitments total (gold $25–60 billion, judge $10–20 billion). Never judged in any draw: NVIDIA's own capex (q12); the operating margin in two draws (q10): evidence never reached them, counted apart as \"no judgement\". The new judge (`judging-v6`, D260) has no run to score yet; a run on `poc-v90` is Alex's call.\n  3068\t\n  3084\t## D265 · 2026-11-02 · Extraction v72 / poc-v92 is the version: the default configuration, the base every later change builds on, the control of every later measurement; D207's narrowest rule is enforced in code\n  3085\t\n  3086\t- Alex, 2026-11-02 evening, on the measured v72: \"for the current version that you just fixed, I think it's highly probable that it's going to be the candidate. So, clean up the versioning. Like, whatever we just did, I think this is going to be the latest version. Use this, and don't drift again. With that, start to experiment the next steps that you talked about on what you need to do to fix the problems that you have discovered that still could be enhanced.\" The base-text question of D264 (v53 against v66) is thereby answered: the version is v72 as measured (role-v66's text under the architecture); its supporting-recall loss is fixed inside it, not by reverting its base.\n  3087\t- Versioning from here: `poc/config/poc-v92.json` is the default (`scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test `test_replay_script_defaults_run_the_default_jev_configuration_with_sixteen_and_eight_workers`, the README name it; `poc-v69` stays as the record of the placement architecture). A change to an extraction text is a new number (v73, v74 …: its own role, categories and review files, byte-identical where the text is unchanged) and a new `poc` configuration built from v92; a code rule applies under every configuration and changes no number. Every later measurement names poc-v92 as its control, three draws each, on the frozen ruler (§7.1); the 2026-11-02 draws `arms/r6-one-decider-v92/d1..3` are its baseline (`e2e-funnel-r6-v72.txt`). Nothing of the request shape (the day-start snapshot with takes lines, the links definition, no placement call) changes again without a decision in his words.\n  3088\t- The first fix, code, $0 (the sink of D264): `extraction.narrowest_links`, applied in `file_reading` to every filing from v20 on: a statement linked to a question and to a question that question depends on (the ledger's `dependencies`, the seeds' root-and-driver pairs, transitively) keeps the narrower one only, which is D207's \"narrowest question only\" made an identity rule where the ledger knows the hierarchy. Replayed over the three v92 ledgers: links 967/921/907 → removed 302/310/285 (31–34%), no statement left without a link (the rule keeps the narrower); the three revenue questions' share and the per-question piles after the rule are printed in `design-v72.md` §9. Test `test_a_statement_filed_under_a_driver_and_its_root_keeps_the_driver_only`.\n  3089\t- What the rule does not do: a statement whose only link is a revenue question it does not bear on (the reactor output, the optical plant) stays there; that is the extraction's noise class and the figure-line clause (D264's first mechanism), the next class.\n  3090\t- The second fix, text, proved for cents (D264's second mechanism, the supporting matters v66's check removes): the model's own account on six of the twenty lost matters (`probe-v72-missing-supporting.txt`) cited in three cases a check row whose own boundary should have sent the statement back (an arrangement in place against a new step; common knowledge without a figure against a competitor's share with a figure; a product detail against a delay of the product that carries the value), and those three boundaries were the ones written without an example. `review-v73.txt` (role and categories identical to v72's; `poc/config/poc-v93.json`) gives each its kept-side example in another domain and drops the row-1 clause the header already states: 3,548 → 3,822 characters, the reason being AGENTS §6's rule that a classification is a closed set with examples. Proof (`harness/resend_review_v73.py`, `proof-review-v73.txt`: the 17 articles of the 20 matters, three sends each under poc-v93 from v92 draw 1's snapshots, against the three stored v92 draws): the 20 matters appear 10 → 28 times of 60, present in at least two sends 0 → 11, the three probed cases 0/3, 1/3, 0/3 → 2/3, 3/3, 3/3; the guard, gold not-kept statements written on the same 17 articles, 0.47 → 0.61 per article per send (about 2.4 more per 17 articles against 6 more supporting matters per send). Not a patch by that ratio, but under v72 what the extraction writes reaches the judge, so the whole bench decides: three draws of poc-v93 with the narrowest rule against the v92 baseline (about $2.7) at his word. Not decided: whether poc-v93 replaces poc-v92 as the default.\n  3091\t\n  3092\t## D266 · 2026-11-02 · Three quick fixes on the v72 base, each proved on stored data in minutes, put together as poc-v94 and run once: the retold-arrangement noise, the quote refusals, and the judgement churn that was not one\n  3093\t\n  3094\t- Alex, on the five classes listed after the v72 measurement: \"2/4/5比较重要，快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\". (And on the first version of that list: \"你讲的tmd是人话吗？…再给我讲Ai黑话我就干死你\": every message to him is plain language, AGENTS \"Authority and scope\".)\n  3095\t- Item 2, the noise filed under the revenue questions. Census ($0, the three v92 draws, the gold's own row for each not-kept statement): 64 gold not-kept statements written a draw; the largest row is D250 item 1, an arrangement the item dates to an earlier month or year and retells with no new step (a partnership \"earlier this year\", a contract signed \"in May\"), 55 of 191, 29%; every other row 3% or less. Fix at the owner, the closing check's row 1 (`review-v74.txt`, 3,822 → 4,067 characters; role and categories identical to v73): the dated retelling named with two examples, the paired counter-example of v73's new-step boundary (D252). Proof for cents (`harness/resend_noise_row.py`, `proof-review-v74-noise.txt`: the nine articles that wrote that row at least twice over the stored draws, three sends each under `poc/config/poc-v94.json`): row statements written 57 → 32 (−44%), the articles' core and supporting matters present 25 → 24. Conclusion: works on the class, no loss of kept matters.\n  3096\t- Item 5, the quote check refusing core statements. Census ($0): 16, 11 and 14 refused quotes a draw; read against the closest source window, they are a word or two changed (the company's name for \"the company's\", \"As\" for \"While\", \"Although\" for \"While\", \"My\" for \"Our\"), a quote that copies one passage and runs on into the next, a run left out together with a changed word, and paraphrases (a comparison sentence restated as the company's own figure). Fix in code (`extraction.repair_quote`, D236 widened; `tests/test_quote_near.py`; D236's own tests hold): a quote whose words differ from one same-length source window by at most two edits (three above 30 words), every edited word a function word, a pronoun, a generic word for the company or the subject company's own name (`universe.companies[...]['name']`, given to the repair by `sift`), is that window; a quote that copies one passage exactly and runs on keeps the copied passage when it is at least eight words and ends at a sentence end. A changed month or number, another party's name, two names swapped, a dropped last word and a paraphrase are refused as before. Replayed over the 41 refused quotes of the three v92 draws: 27 repaired, each to the exact source passage, 14 refused (paraphrases, another company's name written for a pronoun, a typo in a proper noun, one stitched quote). The stored quote is still always verbatim source text.\n  3097\t- Item 4, \"the judgement changes its rung most days\", was my misreading of the funnel: the row counted the judge's own `changed` flag, which judging-v7 sets on most later judgements. The rungs themselves (the path of each question's rung over the 14 days, `e2e_funnel.py` now prints it as \"moved / moved back\"): v92 draw 1, 17 moves in 222 later judgements (8%) and one move back; v91 draw 1, 23 in 313 and two. The one reversal (FY2027 total revenue, 2 → 3 → 2 on 07-06/07/08) is the judge's arithmetic for the implied outcome varying between sends ($461, $392, $416 billion from the same figures), not new evidence. No fix built; the funnel's label corrected.\n  3098\t- Also in code since D265, under every configuration: `extraction.narrowest_links`. All of it together is `poc-v94` (= poc-v93 with T*-v74), launched at 20:21 as `arms/r7-combined-v94/d1..3` against the v92 baseline on the frozen ruler, at his \"全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; the numbers go to `log.md` row 14 and `design-v72.md` §10. Not decided: whether poc-v94 becomes the default (poc-v92 stays until the numbers are read).\n  3099\t- Measured (three draws, finished 21:27; `e2e-funnel-r7-v94.txt`; draw 3 stopped once on 07-05 when the judge named the H200 theme as a dependency of the China-share question twice and the check refused it, a judge-and-check mismatch not seen in the nine earlier draws, resumed from 07-04). Regressions first, v92 → v94: core not extracted 6.7 → 8.0, supporting dropped for no home 12.0 → 14.3, both inside the draw noise; core reaching 73.7 → 74.3 and supporting reaching 90.0 → 89.7, flat against predictions of +2 and +10 (the v73 boundary examples recover about two supporting matters a draw on the whole bench, against six a send on the 17 proof articles). Held: noise reaching 56.9 → 45.0 (−21%), the three revenue questions' share of links 61% → 45% with no statement under both total and Data Center revenue, quote refusals 16/11/14 → 6/10/8, judgement agreement 15/18, 16/17, 17/18 → 16/18, 16/19, 16/18, judge requests 5.1K → 4.2K tokens on average, cost $0.88 → $0.80 a draw, must_open 28/28 and may_open 40/42 unchanged, zero re-sent requests. Verdict: cleaner and cheaper, not worse on the desk's counts; whether poc-v94 becomes the default is Alex's call. Open defect recorded: the judge may name a shown theme as a dependency of an asset question (D263's consistency clause) and the check refuses it; twice in one round fails the day (resumable).\n  3100\t\n  3101\t## D267 · 2026-11-02 · poc-v94 is the default; no further three-draw runs for now; the extraction's remaining failures are read from the stored draws and reported\n  3102\t\n  3103\t- Alex, on the v94 numbers: \"我觉得可以设置为默认；你先做这个更新；但是我不想再跑3轮群补了，现在这一版本的抽取还有什么明显可以提升的地方，深度看失败的问题给我反馈，不要读错\". `poc/config/poc-v94.json` is named by `scripts/replay.py`, the README and the default-entry test (D265's versioning rule continues from v94: a text change is v75 and a new configuration; the control of any later measurement is `arms/r7-combined-v94/d1..3`). No three-draw run is sent until he asks for one; fixes are proved on stored data.\n  3104\t- The deep read of the v94 draws ($0; `design-v72.md` §11 holds the lists, each checked against the article or the raw answer): (1) 42 of the 148 supporting matters never reach the judge in any draw and 30 are never written at all: other companies' and partners' actions and figures with a path to the company (a memory maker's revenue and a customer's price rises, a rival's customer forecasts, a supplier's expansion, partners' adoption of the company's products) and analysts' scenario numbers; the closing check's rows \"another company's matter when you cannot say through which path\", \"product detail\" and \"arrangement in place\" remove what standard 5.1 kinds 2 and 3 keep (D240); v73's examples recovered about two a draw. (2) Of the five core matters never written, one is a scorer miss (the compute-framework retelling is written in other words and filed), four are real: an analyst's view that consensus is too low and a capex forecast in one note, \"Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy these processors\" (a policy fact inside a background sentence), and the four-die to two-chiplet design change (written under role-v53, dropped since v66 as a product detail). (3) About half of the statements filed under the Data Center revenue question are not evidence of it (one reader, 20 sampled: 6 right, 3 under the wrong question, 11 ecosystem or partner lines, a reactor demonstration, a market estimate), and the company's own blog posts supply most of them; 24% of the written noise is still the dated retelling. (4) The extraction links an open question's own estimates only when they name the question's period or population: 3.7 core and 14.3 supporting statements a draw are written and dropped for no home with the question open (the $20 billion CPU target against the Vera CPU question in 2 of 3 draws; 82% and 41% growth against total revenue; the $1 trillion Blackwell and Rubin figure). (5) The shown list suppresses proposals: the Ohio guarantee question, in the judgement gold, opened in one draw of three (two of three under the placement architecture); the operating-margin and capex seeds never receive a statement and are never judged. (6) Smaller: the remaining quote refusals (6–10 a draw) are paraphrases the model writes instead of copying a comparison sentence; two or three of fifteen sampled statements carry a doubtful tier (an author's commentary stored as fact). Nothing of this is built; the order and the fixes are proposals in §11.\n  3105\t\n  3106\t## D268 · 2026-11-02 · The first prompt audit's six fixes, each a contradiction or a missing example in the request, built as extraction v75 / poc-v95 and proved on stored data; the run is Alex's call\n  3107\t\n17:    'view_switches': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, open integer, reason text, by_whom text, after_seq integer',\n50:    'create index if not exists switches_view on view_switches(view_id, id)',\n86:    insert(conn, 'view_switches', view_id=view_id, open=1, reason='created', by_whom='matching', after_seq=seq)\n90:def view(conn, view_id):\n155:def view_key(conn, view_id):\n192:def is_open(conn, view_id):\n193:    row = conn.execute('select open from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n197:def close_view(conn, view_id, reason, by_whom, seq):\n198:    insert(conn, 'view_switches', view_id=view_id, open=0, reason=reason, by_whom=by_whom, after_seq=seq)\n206:def views_of_object(conn, object_id, only_open=True):\n286:def views_open_at_day_start(conn, object_ids, day):\n296:        switch = conn.execute('select open from view_switches where view_id=? and after_seq <= ? order by id desc limit 1', (v['view_id'], seq)).fetchone()\n302:def views_for_prompt(conn, object_ids, themes=False):\n437:def views_linked_to(conn, evidence_id):\nzsh:3: no matches found: scripts/run*\n17:- A thesis is a question with a state, not an assertion. Opposing views move the same state's direction rather than creating opposite duplicate theses.\n23:- Evidence needs the same search-then-compare discipline. Otherwise February's 12% capex guidance and April's 25% revision sit side by side unrelated, forcing every judgement to rediscover which is current; the comparison records the revision, and both stay in force (D202).\n27:- Rejudge when inputs change. A changed conclusion includes a new rung or materially changed supporting facts/numbers. A repeated Fed statement should not trigger hundreds of dependants; AMZN capex moving from 12% to 25% can trigger NVDA even within the same rung.\n36:│   └─ Thesis → A question + a ladder + a due date (Immutable once written. Five rungs, or two for yes/no. When matching opens a thesis, only one may be open for the same subject and focus at a time.)\n39:│       ├─ Dependency → Another thesis (Direction specifies which end of the other thesis is bullish for an asset thesis, or whether the two ladders have the same or opposite orientation for a theme thesis.)\n40:│       └─ Succession → The previous period's thesis (Successive periods of the same focus form a chain)\n54:The same event can affect assets differently: rate cuts can be bullish for Ethereum and bearish for JPM net interest income. Theme theses therefore do not label outcomes good or bad.\n78:3. One ladder concerns one thing. Separate numeric and event questions and connect them with dependencies. Likewise, separate components that can move in opposite directions, such as H20 and Blackwell chip classes.\n93:- Each judgement also declares whether the conclusion changed and explains why, comparing with the state and reasons before this round, including during retries. That earlier conclusion is for comparison, not incremental scoring. A rung change or a material change in the supporting facts/numbers counts: AMZN capex guidance moving from 12% to 25% growth changes the conclusion even within one rung. Repetition does not. A changed conclusion triggers dependent theses in the same round. Code requires changed=true for a first judgement or rung change; otherwise refuse under the same correction rules.\n118:B depends on A | What kind of thesis is A? (For an asset thesis B, state which end of A is bullish for B. For a theme thesis B, state whether their ladders have the same or opposite orientation.)\n132:- Count a statement once. A statement about A is A's evidence, including when two candidates arise from one item. B learns it through A's conclusion. Daily filing gives a statement one home: the narrowest open thesis it bears on, as that thesis's own figure, step or estimate or through the demand, supply, competition or pricing behind its answer, plus the same answer's candidates (D207, D259, D264, D265); the separate coverage-start reading was retired (D370). Dependencies are chosen only when B is created; a later item adding a dependency to an existing thesis is decided (D191 point 2) and to be built (D368).\n134:- The matching call chooses a new thesis's dependencies, stating which conclusions it relies on and each direction (D51). Choose only among searched theses, extraction block-5 theses and candidates opened from the same item; no extra search. Jev, the default matcher, is not asked for them, so new theses do not receive dependencies through the default matcher; building the choice on the Jev path is decided (D368). The historical seed questions are retired (D370). A historical seed's dependency arrow means \"supports\" (D368, by D208): for filing, the supporting (driver) thesis is the narrower one; for judging, the supported (root) thesis reads the supporting theses' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged before their roots. The judging code reads the stored edge the other way today; the fix is to be built and measured (D368). Completed events are evidence, not dependencies: today's oil price influencing OPEC output is evidence for the OPEC-output thesis.\n138:## Succession: the same focus over successive periods\n141:- Successive periods of the same focus form a chain, such as Fed year-end 2026 rate → 2027 rate → 2028 rate. The chain records period order. Dependency traversal follows the rules above.\n143:- Keep ladder orientation across succession: a strongly bullish first rung remains strongly bullish, although thresholds can change. Dependencies retain their direction; reversing the ends would break it.\n170:  ↓ 6 Write to the library (Code): Resolve extraction's group associations to final theses and save them in this step. Each subject has its own writing queue; write theme theses before asset theses. Save new theses with their dependency edges. Store every incoming piece once, as its own record with all its links (D204): a repeat also records the pair as the same claim; a replacement is linked wherever the piece it revises is linked and the pair is recorded as a revision, ordered by when each statement was made, both in force (D202); an older statement arriving later is stored and linked as one more piece, with no revision recorded. The writer retires nothing. If compared data changes before writing, repeat matching only for the affected part.\n180:| Merge into existing | The candidate concerns the same focus or a part of it, such as H20 China revenue within China revenue. Merge only into open theses; closed theses can only be succeeded. | Compare its evidence within the target thesis and preserve grouping under this section's rules. Use the existing ladder and due date. |\n181:| Succession | The next period of the same focus: the next year for numbers, or continued tracking after an event thesis closed | Create a thesis and record succession |\n183:| Skip | Too broad or mixed, bundling questions that can move oppositely, such as all US chip controls on China; numbers beyond this/next year; the same focus and period as a closed thesis; or an out-of-universe subject. Proposed themes go to human review; out-of-universe companies receive only a processing-log entry. | Do not create it. Evidence also linked to a specific valid thesis still counts; evidence linked only to the skipped candidate is not stored. |\n185:- The D155 POC uses code for fully determined duplicate identity and model comparison when scope or legacy identity needs judgement. A shared quantity (an aggregate opened under its admission reason) is one thesis per theme, measure and period: its population or wording is not identity, so code merges another wording into the open one and succeeds it for the next period (D197). Reference lists guide research without vetoing candidates. Same group does not mean same thesis. See docs/poc/grouping-improvement-plan.md for the contract and measured scope.\n    35\t        with sqlite3.connect(ledger.resolve().as_uri() + '?mode=ro', uri=True) as conn:\n    36\t            tables = {r[0] for r in conn.execute(\"select name from sqlite_master where type='table'\")}\n    37\t            if not tables:\n    38\t                return\n    39\t            if 'views' not in tables:\n    40\t                raise SystemExit('cannot verify question origins in the existing ledger')\n    41\t            columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(views)')}\n    42\t            if 'created_from_input' not in columns:\n    43\t                raise SystemExit('cannot verify question origins in the existing ledger')\n    44\t            seeded = conn.execute(\"select count(*) from views where lower(substr(created_from_input, 1, 5))='seed:'\").fetchone()[0]\n    45\t            if seeded:\n    46\t                raise SystemExit(f'existing ledger has {seeded} seeded questions; use a clean ledger')\n    47\t    except sqlite3.Error as error:\n    48\t        raise SystemExit(f'cannot inspect existing ledger: {error}') from error\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef main():\n    52\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    53\t    parser.add_argument('--from', dest='from_day', required=True)\n    54\t    parser.add_argument('--until', dest='until_day', required=True)\n    55\t    parser.add_argument('--day0', default=None)\n    56\t    parser.add_argument('--testdb', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n    57\t    parser.add_argument('--views', required=True, help='the ledger this run writes (a new run: a new dated folder)')\n    58\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', required=True, help='the model-call archive of this run')\n    59\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118.json'))\n    60\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n    61\t    parser.add_argument('--only', default=None, help='comma-separated object ids to restrict the stream to')\n    62\t    parser.add_argument('--cap', type=float, default=None, help='USD spend cap for this run')\n    63\t    parser.add_argument('--max-items-per-day', type=int, default=None)\n    64\t    parser.add_argument('--workers', type=int, default=16, help='extraction requests prepared at a time (D183); 1 is the serial path')\n    65\t    parser.add_argument('--jev-workers', type=int, default=None,\n    66\t                        help='Jev matching questions sent at a time when --workers > 1; default 8 for Jev, 1 for another engine')\n    67\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n    68\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.views), exist_ok=True)\n    69\t    log_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(args.views), 'replay.log')\n    70\t\n    71\t    def log(*parts):\n    72\t        line = ' '.join(str(p) for p in parts)\n    73\t        print(line, flush=True)\n    74\t        with open(log_path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    75\t            handle.write(line + '\\n')\n    76\t\n    77\t    cfg = config.load(args.config)\n    78\t    if cfg.baseline is not None:\n    79\t        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses retired seeded-question baseline; select a configuration without it')\n    80\t    refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)\n    81\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n    82\t    archive = model.Archive(args.archive)\n    83\t    day_runner = None\n    84\t    if args.workers > 1:\n    85\t        jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\n    86\t        day_runner = parallel_day.ParallelDay(os.path.abspath(args.testdb), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.views)), 'manifests'),\n    87\t                                              extraction_workers=args.workers, jev_workers=jev_workers)\n    88\t    log(f'--- replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version}'\n    89\t        f' workers {args.workers}')\n    90\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\n    91\t                        from_day=args.from_day, until_day=args.until_day, day0=args.day0, spend_cap_usd=args.cap, log=log,\n    92\t                        only_objects=set(args.only.split(',')) if args.only else None, max_items_per_day=args.max_items_per_day,\n    93\t                        day_runner=day_runner)\n    94\t    log('totals:', totals)\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    98\t    main()\n   152\t          input_id: s.input_id,\n   153\t          day: s.day,\n   154\t          arrival_day: s.arrival_day,\n   155\t          source: source(s.source, s.day),\n   156\t        })),\n   157\t        replaced_by: e.replaced_by ? { ...e.replaced_by, day: e.replaced_by.day ?? null } : null,\n   158\t        replaces: e.replaces,\n   159\t      })),\n   160\t      dependencies: v.dependencies.map((d, i) => ({\n   161\t        depends_on: d.depends_on,\n   162\t        direction: d.direction,\n   163\t        wait_year: d.wait_year,\n   164\t        wait_chain_view_id: d.wait_chain_view_id ?? null,\n   165\t        resolutions: d.resolutions ?? [],\n   166\t        day: dated(d.day, d.seq, `${path}/dependencies/${i}/day`),\n   167\t      })),\n   168\t      switches: v.switches\n   169\t        .map((s, i) => {\n   170\t          if (![true, false, 0, 1].includes(s.open))\n   171\t            throw new ContractError(\n   172\t              `${path}/switches/${i}/open`,\n   173\t              'expected a boolean or SQLite 0/1',\n   174\t            );\n   175\t          return {\n   176\t            day: dated(s.day, s.after_seq, `${path}/switches/${i}/day`),\n   177\t            seq: s.after_seq,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'separate (dependency|one for dependencies|call.*dependenc)|dependency call|dependency selection' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -38\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3084,3103p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md | sed -n '1,70p'\nrg -n 'lock|writer' scripts/run_replay* src/hivemind/stream.py src/hivemind/replay.py src/hivemind/views/store.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'separate (dependency|one for dependencies|call.*dependenc)|dependency call|dependency selection' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -38\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3084,3103p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md | sed -n '1,70p'\nrg -n 'lock|writer' scripts/run_replay* src/hivemind/stream.py src/hivemind/replay.py src/hivemind/views/store.py\"","aggregated_output":"1280:     calls (matching, re-judging), no longer a separate one for dependencies. A dependency on a view in none of the three\n6409:  directs both the corrected reading and the separate dependency selection; neither is accepted by the other's result.\n6432:## D536 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: no measurement of the reversed reading direction is sent now; next, at $0, size where dependency selection could act in the stored unseeded fresh week (council consensus, reflection round 27)\n  3084\t## D265 · 2026-11-02 · Extraction v72 / poc-v92 is the version: the default configuration, the base every later change builds on, the control of every later measurement; D207's narrowest rule is enforced in code\n  3085\t\n  3086\t- Alex, 2026-11-02 evening, on the measured v72: \"for the current version that you just fixed, I think it's highly probable that it's going to be the candidate. So, clean up the versioning. Like, whatever we just did, I think this is going to be the latest version. Use this, and don't drift again. With that, start to experiment the next steps that you talked about on what you need to do to fix the problems that you have discovered that still could be enhanced.\" The base-text question of D264 (v53 against v66) is thereby answered: the version is v72 as measured (role-v66's text under the architecture); its supporting-recall loss is fixed inside it, not by reverting its base.\n  3087\t- Versioning from here: `poc/config/poc-v92.json` is the default (`scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test `test_replay_script_defaults_run_the_default_jev_configuration_with_sixteen_and_eight_workers`, the README name it; `poc-v69` stays as the record of the placement architecture). A change to an extraction text is a new number (v73, v74 …: its own role, categories and review files, byte-identical where the text is unchanged) and a new `poc` configuration built from v92; a code rule applies under every configuration and changes no number. Every later measurement names poc-v92 as its control, three draws each, on the frozen ruler (§7.1); the 2026-11-02 draws `arms/r6-one-decider-v92/d1..3` are its baseline (`e2e-funnel-r6-v72.txt`). Nothing of the request shape (the day-start snapshot with takes lines, the links definition, no placement call) changes again without a decision in his words.\n  3088\t- The first fix, code, $0 (the sink of D264): `extraction.narrowest_links`, applied in `file_reading` to every filing from v20 on: a statement linked to a question and to a question that question depends on (the ledger's `dependencies`, the seeds' root-and-driver pairs, transitively) keeps the narrower one only, which is D207's \"narrowest question only\" made an identity rule where the ledger knows the hierarchy. Replayed over the three v92 ledgers: links 967/921/907 → removed 302/310/285 (31–34%), no statement left without a link (the rule keeps the narrower); the three revenue questions' share and the per-question piles after the rule are printed in `design-v72.md` §9. Test `test_a_statement_filed_under_a_driver_and_its_root_keeps_the_driver_only`.\n  3089\t- What the rule does not do: a statement whose only link is a revenue question it does not bear on (the reactor output, the optical plant) stays there; that is the extraction's noise class and the figure-line clause (D264's first mechanism), the next class.\n  3090\t- The second fix, text, proved for cents (D264's second mechanism, the supporting matters v66's check removes): the model's own account on six of the twenty lost matters (`probe-v72-missing-supporting.txt`) cited in three cases a check row whose own boundary should have sent the statement back (an arrangement in place against a new step; common knowledge without a figure against a competitor's share with a figure; a product detail against a delay of the product that carries the value), and those three boundaries were the ones written without an example. `review-v73.txt` (role and categories identical to v72's; `poc/config/poc-v93.json`) gives each its kept-side example in another domain and drops the row-1 clause the header already states: 3,548 → 3,822 characters, the reason being AGENTS §6's rule that a classification is a closed set with examples. Proof (`harness/resend_review_v73.py`, `proof-review-v73.txt`: the 17 articles of the 20 matters, three sends each under poc-v93 from v92 draw 1's snapshots, against the three stored v92 draws): the 20 matters appear 10 → 28 times of 60, present in at least two sends 0 → 11, the three probed cases 0/3, 1/3, 0/3 → 2/3, 3/3, 3/3; the guard, gold not-kept statements written on the same 17 articles, 0.47 → 0.61 per article per send (about 2.4 more per 17 articles against 6 more supporting matters per send). Not a patch by that ratio, but under v72 what the extraction writes reaches the judge, so the whole bench decides: three draws of poc-v93 with the narrowest rule against the v92 baseline (about $2.7) at his word. Not decided: whether poc-v93 replaces poc-v92 as the default.\n  3091\t\n  3092\t## D266 · 2026-11-02 · Three quick fixes on the v72 base, each proved on stored data in minutes, put together as poc-v94 and run once: the retold-arrangement noise, the quote refusals, and the judgement churn that was not one\n  3093\t\n  3094\t- Alex, on the five classes listed after the v72 measurement: \"2/4/5比较重要，快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\". (And on the first version of that list: \"你讲的tmd是人话吗？…再给我讲Ai黑话我就干死你\": every message to him is plain language, AGENTS \"Authority and scope\".)\n  3095\t- Item 2, the noise filed under the revenue questions. Census ($0, the three v92 draws, the gold's own row for each not-kept statement): 64 gold not-kept statements written a draw; the largest row is D250 item 1, an arrangement the item dates to an earlier month or year and retells with no new step (a partnership \"earlier this year\", a contract signed \"in May\"), 55 of 191, 29%; every other row 3% or less. Fix at the owner, the closing check's row 1 (`review-v74.txt`, 3,822 → 4,067 characters; role and categories identical to v73): the dated retelling named with two examples, the paired counter-example of v73's new-step boundary (D252). Proof for cents (`harness/resend_noise_row.py`, `proof-review-v74-noise.txt`: the nine articles that wrote that row at least twice over the stored draws, three sends each under `poc/config/poc-v94.json`): row statements written 57 → 32 (−44%), the articles' core and supporting matters present 25 → 24. Conclusion: works on the class, no loss of kept matters.\n  3096\t- Item 5, the quote check refusing core statements. Census ($0): 16, 11 and 14 refused quotes a draw; read against the closest source window, they are a word or two changed (the company's name for \"the company's\", \"As\" for \"While\", \"Although\" for \"While\", \"My\" for \"Our\"), a quote that copies one passage and runs on into the next, a run left out together with a changed word, and paraphrases (a comparison sentence restated as the company's own figure). Fix in code (`extraction.repair_quote`, D236 widened; `tests/test_quote_near.py`; D236's own tests hold): a quote whose words differ from one same-length source window by at most two edits (three above 30 words), every edited word a function word, a pronoun, a generic word for the company or the subject company's own name (`universe.companies[...]['name']`, given to the repair by `sift`), is that window; a quote that copies one passage exactly and runs on keeps the copied passage when it is at least eight words and ends at a sentence end. A changed month or number, another party's name, two names swapped, a dropped last word and a paraphrase are refused as before. Replayed over the 41 refused quotes of the three v92 draws: 27 repaired, each to the exact source passage, 14 refused (paraphrases, another company's name written for a pronoun, a typo in a proper noun, one stitched quote). The stored quote is still always verbatim source text.\n  3097\t- Item 4, \"the judgement changes its rung most days\", was my misreading of the funnel: the row counted the judge's own `changed` flag, which judging-v7 sets on most later judgements. The rungs themselves (the path of each question's rung over the 14 days, `e2e_funnel.py` now prints it as \"moved / moved back\"): v92 draw 1, 17 moves in 222 later judgements (8%) and one move back; v91 draw 1, 23 in 313 and two. The one reversal (FY2027 total revenue, 2 → 3 → 2 on 07-06/07/08) is the judge's arithmetic for the implied outcome varying between sends ($461, $392, $416 billion from the same figures), not new evidence. No fix built; the funnel's label corrected.\n  3098\t- Also in code since D265, under every configuration: `extraction.narrowest_links`. All of it together is `poc-v94` (= poc-v93 with T*-v74), launched at 20:21 as `arms/r7-combined-v94/d1..3` against the v92 baseline on the frozen ruler, at his \"全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; the numbers go to `log.md` row 14 and `design-v72.md` §10. Not decided: whether poc-v94 becomes the default (poc-v92 stays until the numbers are read).\n  3099\t- Measured (three draws, finished 21:27; `e2e-funnel-r7-v94.txt`; draw 3 stopped once on 07-05 when the judge named the H200 theme as a dependency of the China-share question twice and the check refused it, a judge-and-check mismatch not seen in the nine earlier draws, resumed from 07-04). Regressions first, v92 → v94: core not extracted 6.7 → 8.0, supporting dropped for no home 12.0 → 14.3, both inside the draw noise; core reaching 73.7 → 74.3 and supporting reaching 90.0 → 89.7, flat against predictions of +2 and +10 (the v73 boundary examples recover about two supporting matters a draw on the whole bench, against six a send on the 17 proof articles). Held: noise reaching 56.9 → 45.0 (−21%), the three revenue questions' share of links 61% → 45% with no statement under both total and Data Center revenue, quote refusals 16/11/14 → 6/10/8, judgement agreement 15/18, 16/17, 17/18 → 16/18, 16/19, 16/18, judge requests 5.1K → 4.2K tokens on average, cost $0.88 → $0.80 a draw, must_open 28/28 and may_open 40/42 unchanged, zero re-sent requests. Verdict: cleaner and cheaper, not worse on the desk's counts; whether poc-v94 becomes the default is Alex's call. Open defect recorded: the judge may name a shown theme as a dependency of an asset question (D263's consistency clause) and the check refuses it; twice in one round fails the day (resumable).\n  3100\t\n  3101\t## D267 · 2026-11-02 · poc-v94 is the default; no further three-draw runs for now; the extraction's remaining failures are read from the stored draws and reported\n  3102\t\n  3103\t- Alex, on the v94 numbers: \"我觉得可以设置为默认；你先做这个更新；但是我不想再跑3轮群补了，现在这一版本的抽取还有什么明显可以提升的地方，深度看失败的问题给我反馈，不要读错\". `poc/config/poc-v94.json` is named by `scripts/replay.py`, the README and the default-entry test (D265's versioning rule continues from v94: a text change is v75 and a new configuration; the control of any later measurement is `arms/r7-combined-v94/d1..3`). No three-draw run is sent until he asks for one; fixes are proved on stored data.\n     1\t# Council Q, round 3: the dependency probe's design, before any send (read-only; no edits, no model calls)\n     2\t\n     3\t## Alex's word\n     4\tAsked to choose after council Q (A: no daily wrapper yet, link the related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents; B: build\n     5\tthe daily wrapper and warn testers; C: stop), Alex answered \"A\" (2026-11-20).\n     6\t\n     7\t## What I found since round 2 (read these)\n     8\t- **The dependency stretch already ran (D533–D542).** `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/`:\n     9\t  - `DEPENDENCY-SELECTION-CENSUS.md` (D537): in the unseeded fresh week the one clear useful pair was \"data-center revenue FY2027\n    10\t    ← total revenue FY2027\" (the part reading the whole), useful and source-backed; \"total revenue growth FY2028 ← data-center\n    11\t    revenue FY2027\" was a risk (\"a dependency would pass an assumed number on\"). Readers marked DC/total both ways (a circle risk).\n    12\t  - D538: one stored edge has two readers: judging (whose conclusion to read) and filing (`narrowest_links`: the reader becomes the\n    13\t    narrower home; seven statements would lose their total-revenue link).\n    14\t  - `SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` (D539–D542): `reads` vs `supports` edges; closed as a provisional candidate, **not sound for build**; a\n    15\t    reopened slice must first settle a cycle through an awaited question, closing, a theme shown twice, historical readers, the label.\n    16\t  - So round 2's \"decided and not built\" was incomplete: decided (D368 item 2), worked on, not ready to build. I will tell Alex.\n    17\t- **Direction.** Your round-2 point read D368 item 4 (seed edges: the root reads its drivers). PRD 06 line 134: for a question opened\n    18\t  from an article, matching \"chooses a new thesis's dependencies, stating which conclusions it relies on\"; `reads` edges in\n    19\t  SEPARATION-DESIGN §2. The census's useful case is the part reading the whole. The probe therefore tests Data Center reading total\n    20\t  revenue; it does not test the root reading its drivers.\n    21\t- **$0 check done** (`render_check.py`, `render-check.json`; `check.txt`):\n    22\t  - The block production renders shows the total's rung and its reasons cut at 600 characters. old-2: $411B reference, $419B,\n    23\t    Q3 $113.5B, Q4 $127B all shown. old-1: $411B and $404B shown; its reasons never state Q4. old-3: $419B, Q3, Q4 $127B shown, but\n    24\t    the final \"$446 billion\" is cut (the rung \"Strongly bullish\", at least $431.2B, is shown).\n    25\t  - `probe.py check`: each draw's scratch copy rolled back to before the Data Center question's 09-20 judgement (that row and any\n    26\t    later one removed) rebuilds the stored request **byte-equal** (sha256) through `judging.build_prompt` and `model.build_request`\n    27\t    in all three draws; the changed request adds 682–764 characters (the block, and the closing sentence's `cites_views` clause).\n    28\t\n    29\t## The probe (`probe.py send`)\n    30\t- Per draw (old-1 v8←v4, old-2 v9←v14, old-3 v35←v3): control = the stored 09-20 request re-sent unchanged; changed = the same\n    31\t  state plus one dependency row (`first_is_bullish`), rendered by production code with its 600-character cut. Three samples each,\n    32\t  each in its own empty archive (fresh samples), a refused answer retried once with production's note. 18 sends, about $0.006 each\n    33\t  (18k input, 7.6k output at luna's $0.10/$0.50), cap $0.40.\n    34\t- The total's conclusion shown is its same-round 09-20 judgement (production judges dependencies first).\n    35\t\n    36\t## Reading, written before any answer\n    37\tFor every answer, I and a blind reader (you, given answers under shuffled labels with the total's shown conclusion and the evidence\n    38\tthe request lists) record: the FY2027 Data Center estimate; any Q4 Data Center figure; whether each figure of its arithmetic traces to\n    39\tevidence or to the dependency; whether it relates its figure to the total.\n    40\t- **Reconciles:** FY Data Center below the total's shown FY figure; a stated Q4 Data Center below the total's shown Q4 (when shown);\n    41\t  no unsupported step (a figure with no source in the request).\n    42\t- **Pass:** changed reconciles in at least 2 of 3 samples in each draw; control reconciles in at most 1 of 3 in at least two draws\n    43\t  (else the stored contradiction is a coin flip the probe cannot separate: inconclusive); no added refusal; no new unsupported step.\n    44\t- **What it decides:** pass → the next step is the build design (D542's five open items and the `reads`/`supports` separation),\n    45\t  back to the council and Alex; fail → linking alone does not reconcile; the cause is the judge's own arithmetic, back to the\n    46\t  council; inconclusive → report as such.\n    47\t\n    48\t## Questions\n    49\t- (a) Is this probe sound? What would make it misleading (the 600-character cut, old-1's missing Q4, the same-round total, the\n    50\t  reading rule)?\n    51\t- (b) Is \"Data Center reads total\" the right first direction given D368 item 4, PRD 06 and D537?\n    52\t- (c) Anything to change before the send?\n    53\t\n    54\tEnd with CONSENSUS or DISAGREE. Under 400 words.\nzsh:4: no matches found: scripts/run_replay*\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
