 24): this stretch of the lean investigation is closed and consolidated on the decision page (section 7); the default and both systems stay; D375 and D368 are Alex's decisions awaiting implementation and acceptance; next a separate $0 assessment of D368's dependency channel on a stored, correctly directed case, with a stop rule | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md` (section 7) |\n878:| D534 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 25): the dependency-channel assessment corrected (its lines were built from conclusions judged after the receiver; eight edges into two questions); before any measurement design, a $0 chronology for the two receiving questions and an ordering-and-propagation proof with labelled fake judgement outputs, with a stop rule | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md` |\n879:| D535 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 26): the one-chain ordering proof of D368's direction accepted as a bounded wiring result; before any measurement design, a source-backed decision-relevant case among the supporting lines and a verified rebuild of the state of 2026-07-14 before its judging round, both at $0 | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md` |\n880:| D536 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 27): no measurement of the reversed reading direction is sent now (D368 item 4 stays recorded, awaiting build and measurement; the harness is kept); next, at $0, a design census of where dependency selection could act in the stored unseeded fresh week, with a stop rule | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md` |\n881:| D537 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 28): the dependency-selection census of the unseeded fresh week has one clear case (data-center revenue reading total revenue) and negative controls; before any send, a stored-data proof of the edge's effect on filing and judging, with a stop rule | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/DEPENDENCY-SELECTION-CENSUS.md` |\n882:| D538 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 29): one dependency edge shows the intended conclusion to the judge (conditional proof) and removes seven filing links through the narrowest rule; the dependency slice's design is opened at $0, beginning with the separation of the edge's two uses; no send, no frozen piece changed | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/EDGE-PROOF-RESULT.md` |\n883:| D539 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 30): the separation of a dependency edge's two uses (kind set by the writer; judging and filing each read one derived relation) is kept as a candidate; its design continues at $0 (duplicate and old-row contracts, the D265 and D207 reading with its cost, completed tables, a proof through real writers) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` |\n884:| D540 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 31): the separation stays a provisional research candidate (not applying the narrowest rule to a chosen dependency is a provisional interpretation, not a product rule); no judge call; the filing and duplicate-label contracts are finished at $0 first, with a stop if homes cannot be expressed or a label's meaning would have to be invented | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` |\n885:| D541 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 32): the seed edge's label (`last_end`, defined nowhere) stops everything that touches a seed edge and is given no meaning; the filing finding is a bounded hand reading; the unseeded failure-and-reader contract is finished at $0 before the separation is called sound | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` |\n886:| D542 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council round 33): the dependency stretch (D533 to D542) is closed with the separation of an edge's two uses recorded as a provisional candidate, not sound for build; the status is consolidated to one next task; nothing sent; no general stopping rule adopted | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` |\n1034:| D690 | 2026-11-20 | Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product and the research line rests until his new direction; B (other companies' own figures, the judge's carried conclusion) and C (new paid test questions) not taken; D689's reopening conditions stand; D681–D690 records committed locally, not pushed | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n1035:| D691 | 2026-11-20 | Alex chooses A after council Q (library useful for sources, not its number answers: linked questions contradict): no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few-cents probe; the dependency stretch D533–D542 stays a provisional candidate | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n1036:| D692 | 2026-11-20 | Under Alex's A: the dependency probe passes (linked 2 of 3 reconcile, unchanged 0 of 3; $0.0176); the stored extreme did not recur; the dependency design review reopens at $0, then Alex; the self-made reference traced apart | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
